const e={B0001:["Driver Frontal Stage 1 Deployment Control","The restraint control module tests the firing loop of the first inflator stage in the driver airbag, which sits in the steering wheel hub and is fed through the clock spring. B0001 is stored when that loop is open, shorted or outside its resistance window; the fault byte added to the code names the exact type.",["Corroded or poorly seated connector between steering wheel harness and airbag module","Broken or worn conductor in the clock spring","Internal fault in the driver airbag module (stage 1 squib)","Chafed lead in the steering wheel or column harness"],["Airbag warning lamp or service airbag message stays on","Driver frontal airbag may not deploy in a crash","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0002","B0003","B0010"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי נהג‏ 1"],B0002:["Driver Frontal Stage 2 Deployment Control","Dual-stage driver airbags hold a second charge that the restraint module fires only in severe crashes or after a short delay, so the cushion fills harder or for longer; a Nissan patent bases that choice on the change in vehicle speed and belt use. B0002 flags a fault in the firing loop of this second stage.",["Open stage 2 squib lead at the airbag module connector","Stage 2 track in the clock spring broken","Replacement restraint module loaded with unsuitable software (Land Rover SSM 74577)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Driver airbag loses its second, high-severity stage","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0001","B0003","B0011"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי נהג‏ 2"],B0003:["Driver Frontal Stage 3 Deployment Control","Some driver airbag modules carry a third pyrotechnic element in addition to the two inflator stages, and B0003 covers its firing loop. FCA lists the code as driver frontal squib 3; its STAR case S2108000180 found B0003-2B (wires shorted together) next to B0001 and B0002 when connector locks behind the steering wheel were not engaged.",["Connector position assurance lock at the airbag module not engaged","Third squib or vent valve squib in the airbag module faulty","Damaged clock spring conductor for the third circuit"],["Airbag warning lamp on, often together with B0001 or B0002","Adaptive venting or third deployment stage unavailable","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0001","B0002","B0012"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי נהג‏ 3"],B0004:["Driver Knee Bolster Deployment Control","A knee airbag, also called an active knee bolster, sits in the lower dash below the steering column. It fills the space in front of the driver's knees and holds the lower body back in a frontal crash, mainly for unbelted occupants. B0004 reports a fault in its firing loop. Mercedes-Benz stores B000413 for an open squib of the driver kneebag.",["Faulty or loose knee airbag connector under the dash (Ford TSB 24-2444)","Harness pinched or damaged during work below the steering column","Internal fault in the knee airbag module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Driver knee airbag may not deploy in a frontal crash","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0013","B0001","B0014"],""],B0005:["Collapsible Steering Column Deployment Control","Some steering columns can change how much energy they soak up while collapsing in a frontal crash. In a Delphi/Nexteer patent a controller fires pyrotechnic actuators that force an absorber strap into a tighter path or couple in extra absorbers, matching the column to driver size and crash severity. B0005 is the restraint module code for the firing loop of such an actuator.",["Restraint module configuration or software does not match the vehicle (Land Rover SSM 74577)","Open or shorted lead to the pyrotechnic column actuator","Faulty actuator in the steering column"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Adaptive energy absorption of the column unavailable, no effect on normal steering","Safety note: the column actuator is pyrotechnic; leave tests and connector work to a workshop with the battery disconnected"],4,0,["B0001","B0004"],""],B0006:["Driver Frontal Deployment Loop Short to Ground","B0006 is missing from the public J2012 code lists, which go straight from B0005 to B0010. The only documented use found has nothing to do with airbags: on the 2025 Ram 1500 the body control module stores B0006-11 for a short to ground in the latch control of the left RamBox stowage lid, fixed by a module update (flash 08-204-24). The title describes a driver airbag firing loop shorted to ground.",["On Ram 1500 2025 the code belongs to the left stowage lid latch circuit of the body module, not the airbag","Driver airbag squib lead chafed against metal (ground short)","Insulation damage inside the clock spring"],["Airbag warning lamp on when stored by the restraint module","On Ram 1500 2025 stowage lid will not open electrically, alarm may sound","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0007","B0001","B0016"],""],B0007:["Driver Frontal Deployment Loop Short to Battery","Like B0006, this number is absent from the public J2012 lists. FCA uses B0007-11 on the 2025 Ram 1500 for the latch control of the right RamBox stowage lid, again a short to ground in the body control module and cured by the same flash 08-204-24; an airbag meaning is not documented anywhere. The title names a driver airbag loop shorted to battery voltage.",["On Ram 1500 2025 the code belongs to the right stowage lid latch circuit of the body module","Squib lead touching a powered wire in the column or steering wheel harness","Moisture bridging pins in a connector of the airbag circuit"],["Airbag warning lamp on, affected stage disabled by the module","On Ram 1500 2025 right stowage lid inoperative","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0006","B0002","B0017"],""],B0010:["Passenger Frontal Stage 1 Deployment Control","The front passenger airbag in the dashboard is normally dual-stage like the driver bag, but it also depends on occupant detection: FMVSS 208 allows it to be suppressed for small occupants and requires a readiness indicator that monitors the system. B0010 reports a fault in the firing loop of its first stage. Mercedes-Benz stores B001013 when the stage 1 squib of the passenger bag is open;",["Loose, corroded or unlocked connector at the passenger airbag module","Harness damaged during dashboard or glovebox work","Internal fault in the passenger airbag module (stage 1 squib)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Front passenger airbag may not deploy in a crash","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0011","B0012","B0001"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי נוסע‏ 1"],B0011:["Passenger Frontal Stage 2 Deployment Control","B0011 is the passenger counterpart of B0002: it concerns the second inflator stage of the dashboard airbag, which the module adds in severe crashes or fires with a delay. Mercedes-Benz logs B001113 for an open stage 2 squib of the front passenger airbag, and Mitsubishi lists B0011 as passenger airbag module 2. Stage 1 of the same bag has its own code B0010, a third element B0012.",["Poor contact on the stage 2 pins or open stage 2 lead","Stage 2 squib in the passenger airbag module faulty","Output stage in the restraint control module faulty"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag loses its second stage for severe crashes","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0010","B0012","B0002"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי נוסע‏ 2"],B0012:["Passenger Frontal Stage 3 Deployment Control","In the J2012 order B0012 is the third element of the front passenger airbag. Mercedes-Benz uses B001213 for the squib of the vent valve in that airbag, and Mitsubishi lists B0012 as passenger airbag module 3. GM gives the number a different meaning. Its later sensing and diagnostic modules assign B0012 to stage 1 of the steering wheel airbag;",["On GM vehicles weak terminal tension or chafed wires at the steering wheel airbag coil","Open or shorted third squib (vent valve) in the passenger airbag (J2012 meaning)","Restraint control module fault"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Depending on maker, passenger airbag venting or GM driver airbag stage 1 affected","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0010","B0011","B0003"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי נוסע‏ 3"],B0013:["Passenger Knee Bolster Deployment Control","B0013 belongs to the knee airbag on the passenger side, which deploys from the lower glovebox area and keeps the passenger's knees and thighs from sliding under the dash. Mercedes-Benz logs B001313 for an open squib of the front passenger kneebag. Ford pairs B0013:1A with the driver knee code B0004 on the 2024 Ranger;",["Faulty connector at the passenger knee airbag (Ford TSB 24-2444)","On GM vehicles fault in the driver airbag stage 2 loop or clock spring","Internal fault in the passenger knee airbag"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger knee airbag (or on GM driver airbag stage 2) may not deploy","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0004","B0010","B0015"],""],B0014:["Driver Knee Airbag Deployment Control","B0014 is not in the public J2012 code lists; there the driver knee airbag has B0004 and the passenger knee airbag B0013. The number is documented only at General Motors, and with another meaning. GM modules from about 2010 use B0014 for the side airbag in the driver seat;",["On GM vehicles loose or high-resistance side airbag connector under or in the driver seat","Seat harness chafed by seat frame, motor or foam","Internal fault in the airbag module served by this loop"],["Airbag warning lamp or service airbag message, often intermittent","Affected airbag may not deploy","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0004","B0015","B0020"],"בקרת הפעלת כרית אוויר ברכיים נהג"],B0015:["Passenger Knee Airbag Deployment Control","B0015 does not appear in the public J2012 code lists, which assign the passenger knee airbag to B0013. Only General Motors documents the number, as the firing loop of the belt pretensioner built into the driver's retractor.",["On GM vehicles loose or corroded connector at the driver belt pretensioner","Harness under the power seat rubbing on frame or seat motor (GM PIT4898C)","Internal fault in the pretensioner or airbag served by this loop"],["Airbag warning lamp on, sometimes intermittent","On GM, belt pretensioner may not fire; power seat may fail if the harness is shorted","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0013","B0014","B001A"],"בקרת הפעלת כרית אוויר ברכיים נוסע"],B0016:["Right Front/Passenger Frontal Deployment Loop Short to Ground","The public J2012 code lists skip B0016. General Motors used it in two generations with different meanings. In older modules, documented for the Saab 9-5 2006 and the Saab 9-3 up to 2011, B0016 means low resistance in the passenger frontal stage 1 loop: the reading drops under about 1.5 ohms, tolerance 0.2, for two seconds.",["Squib leads shorted together or to ground in the passenger frontal loop (older GM)","Connector position assurance lock not seated (GM 08-09-41-002H)","On later GM vehicles fault in the left roof rail airbag loop"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger frontal airbag stage 1 (older GM) or left head airbag (later GM) may not deploy","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0017","B0010","B0006"],""],B0017:["Right Front/Passenger Frontal Deployment Loop Short to Battery","None of the public J2012 lists contains B0017 either. In older GM modules (Saab 9-5 2006, Saab 9-3 up to 2011) it marks an open passenger frontal stage 1 loop, set once the loop reads more than roughly 4.5 ohms for two seconds, so the component matches the title but the fault type does not. Later GM vehicles use B0017 with GM's usual fault bytes, where 01 stands for short to battery.",["On GM 2020-22 models faulty SDM software, cured by reprogramming (21-NA-176)","Open passenger frontal stage 1 loop (older GM meaning)","Squib lead in contact with a powered wire"],["Airbag warning lamp on or an OnStar SIR notification without lamp","Affected airbag stage may be disabled","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0016","B0011","B0007"],""],B0018:["Center Frontal Stage 1 Deployment Control","In the J2012 order of seating positions (driver, passenger, center, then second and third row) B0018 covers stage 1 of a frontal airbag for the middle seat of the first row. FMVSS 208 demands frontal airbags only for the outboard front seats, so such a bag is rare, and no carmaker publicly documents B0018 with this meaning.",["Open or shorted stage 1 loop of a first-row center frontal airbag (J2012 meaning)","On older GM/Saab passenger frontal stage 1 loop shorted to battery or ground","Restraint control module fault"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Affected frontal airbag stage may not deploy","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0019","B001A","B0010"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי מרכזי‏ 1"],B0019:["Center Frontal Stage 2 Deployment Control","B0019 is the stage 2 member of the first-row center frontal series B0018 to B001A, meant for the second inflator charge of a middle-seat frontal airbag. No carmaker publicly documents the code with this meaning.",["On GM vehicles fretting corrosion in the passenger airbag in-line connector (HHR PI0117B)","Fault in the stage 2 loop of a first-row center frontal airbag (J2012 meaning)","Internal fault in the airbag module on this loop"],["Airbag warning lamp on","On GM the passenger frontal airbag stage 1 may not deploy","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0018","B001A","B0010"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי מרכזי‏ 2"],B001A:["Center Frontal Stage 3 Deployment Control","B001A closes the first-row center frontal series and stands for a third stage of a middle-seat frontal airbag, matching B0003 for the driver and B0012 for the passenger. No carmaker documents it publicly in this sense. At General Motors the number belongs to the anchor-mounted belt pretensioner on the driver side, a second pretensioner at the belt end fitting that works next to the retractor unit coded B0015.",["On GM vehicles pinched, misrouted or corroded anchor pretensioner harness","Fault in the third stage loop of a first-row center frontal airbag (J2012 meaning)","Internal fault in the pretensioner"],["Airbag warning lamp on","On GM the driver anchor pretensioner may not fire","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0018","B0019","B0015"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי מרכזי‏ 3"],B0020:["Left Side Airbag Deployment Control","B0020 covers the firing loop of the left front side airbag, the thorax bag usually built into the outer flank of the driver seat backrest. Toyota names B002011 and B002012 as short to ground and short to battery on the 2022 Tundra, where the wireless phone charger caused false entries that new SRS software cures (TSB005722).",["Poor contact or corrosion at the side airbag connector or jumper harness under or in the seat","Internal fault in the left seat side airbag module","Pinched or chafed side airbag lead in the seat frame","Restraint module software reacting to interference, e.g. Toyota Tundra 2022 with wireless charger"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left front side airbag may not deploy in a side impact","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0028","B0021","B0030"],"בקרת הפעלת כרית אוויר צד שמאלי"],B0021:["Left Curtain Deployment Control 1","In the J2012 order B0021 is the first firing loop of the left curtain airbag, the bag that drops from the roof rail over the side windows. Mitsubishi files it under the left curtain module and stores byte 11, 12, 13 or a short to another circuit once the condition has lasted 2 seconds.",["Raised contact resistance at the curtain airbag or restraint module connector","Damaged lead along the A-, B- or C-pillar or the roof rail","Internal fault in the left curtain airbag module","Fault or unsuitable software in the restraint control module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left curtain airbag may not deploy in a side impact or rollover","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0022","B0029","B0020","B0046"],"בקרת הפעלת וילון שמאלי‏ 1"],B0022:["Left Curtain Deployment Control 2","B0022 belongs to a second firing loop for the left curtain airbag. Mercedes-Benz shows what that means in practice: on the A-Class, CLA and GLB, B002213 is an open squib in the left rear window bag, the curtain section for the rear seats, while B0021 serves the front one (LI54.21-P-070658, version 1 of 2019 and version 4 of 2020). Cars with a single curtain inflator never set it.",["Raised contact resistance at the restraint module connector (Mercedes LI54.21-P-070658)","Damaged lead to the rear curtain section at the C-pillar or roof rail","Internal fault in the rear left curtain airbag module","Fault or unsuitable software in the restraint control module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Head protection for the left rear seat may be missing","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0021","B002A","B0046"],"בקרת הפעלת וילון שמאלי‏ 2"],B0023:["Left Side Deployment Stage 1 Loop Short to Ground","B0023 does not appear in the J2012 code lists, which jump from B0022 to B0028, and no carmaker documents it as a ground short of a left side airbag stage. It is documented at General Motors with another meaning: in the Saab 9-4X 2011 manual B0023 is the right roof rail (curtain) airbag loop, with bytes for short to battery (01), short to ground (02), open (04) and resistance above 4.2 or below 1.4 ohms (0D, 0E),…",["Connector position assurance not engaged, so shorting bars bridge the loop (GM 08-09-41-002H)","Chafed lead touching body ground","Internal fault in the affected airbag module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","The airbag on the affected loop may not deploy","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0020","B0021","B0016"],""],B0024:["Right Side Deployment Control","B0024 is missing from the public J2012 lists; there the right front side airbag is B0028. General Motors used the number twice. Older modules, such as those of the 2006 Saab 9-5 and the Saab 9-3, assign it to driver frontal stage 1: on the 9-5 the voltage at the module pin leaves the 1.0 to 4.1 volt window for 2 seconds, on the 9-3 the loop is shorted to ground or battery.",["Restraint module software fault on 2021 GM models (PIT5827, 21-NA-176)","Short to ground or battery in the driver frontal stage 1 loop (older GM/Saab)","Worn clock spring in the driver airbag loop (older GM/Saab)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Depending on the vehicle, the driver airbag or a seat side airbag may be affected","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0028","B0020","B0001"],"בקרת הפעלת צד ימני"],B0025:["Left Side Deployment Stage 2 Control","No public J2012 code list contains B0025, and no manufacturer publicly describes a second stage of a left side airbag under this number. The only trace is at General Motors: the Saab 9-4X 2011 manual groups B0025 with the roof rail airbag codes B0016 and B0023 but gives no descriptor for it. Two-stage side airbags are rare in any case.",["Open, shorted or high-resistance squib loop of the airbag the module assigns to this code","Connector or its position lock not fully engaged","Fault or unsuitable software in the restraint control module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side or curtain protection may be reduced on the affected side","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0020","B0023","B0026"],"בקרת שלב הפעלת צד שמאלי‏ 2"],B0026:["Left Side Deployment Stage 2 Loop Open","B0026 is missing from the public J2012 lists. General Motors documents it in older restraint modules with a meaning other than the title: on the 2006 Saab 9-5, B0026 is an open circuit in driver frontal stage 1, set when the measured resistance stays above 4.5 ohms, tolerance 0.2, for 2 seconds; the Saab 9-3 manuals add bytes for an open loop and too high resistance in the same driver circuit.",["Airbag connector or its position lock not fully seated (GM 08-09-41-002H)","Broken track in the clock spring (driver loop on older GM/Saab)","Open squib inside the airbag module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Depending on the vehicle, the driver airbag may not deploy","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0022","B0024","B0001"],"חוג שלב הפעלת צד שמאלי‏ 2 — נתק"],B0028:["Right Side Airbag Deployment Control","B0028 is the right-hand twin of B0020: the firing loop of the right front side airbag, normally in the outer flank of the passenger seat. Honda asked for parts from 2018-20 Accord and CR-V and from the 2015 TLX that stored B0028-13, an open or raised resistance in the passenger side airbag inflator.",["Poor contact or corrosion at the side airbag connector or jumper harness under or in the seat","Internal fault in the right seat side airbag inflator","Lead pinched or stretched by seat adjustment","Restraint module software reacting to interference (Toyota Tundra 2022)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right front side airbag may not deploy in a side impact","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0020","B0029","B0038"],"בקרת הפעלת כרית אוויר צד ימני"],B0029:["Right Curtain Deployment Control 1","B0029 stands for the first firing loop of the right curtain airbag. FCA's STAR case S2010000001 for the 2019 Ram heavy-duty pickup reads B0029-11 as a ground short in right curtain squib 1 and sends the technician to the wiring at the C-pillar trim fixings. Mitsubishi lists the right curtain module under B0029 and sets the ground short after 2 seconds.",["Lead pinched or chafed at pillar trim fixings (FCA S2010000001)","Raised contact resistance at the curtain or restraint module connector","Internal fault in the right curtain airbag module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right curtain airbag may not deploy in a side impact or rollover","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B002A","B0021","B0028"],"בקרת הפעלת וילון ימני‏ 1"],B002A:["Right Curtain Deployment Control 2","B002A is the second firing loop of the right curtain airbag, needed only where the right side has two curtain inflators or a separate curtain section for the rear seats. Mercedes-Benz uses it that way on the A-Class, CLA and GLB: B002A13 marks an open squib in the right rear window bag, while the front part reports B0029; a known trigger was poor contact at the control unit plug (LI54.21-P-070658).",["Raised contact resistance at the restraint module connector (Mercedes LI54.21-P-070658)","Damaged lead to the rear curtain section at the C-pillar or roof rail","Internal fault in the rear right curtain airbag module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Head protection for the right rear seat may be missing","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0029","B0022","B0038"],"בקרת הפעלת וילון ימני‏ 2"],B0030:["Second Row Left Side Airbag Deployment Control","In J2012 the B003x block covers the second seat row, and B0030 is the left rear side airbag, mounted in the rear door or the outer backrest. Mitsubishi files B0030 under the rear side airbag module LH and sets a short to another circuit after 2 seconds.",["Raised contact resistance at the restraint module or rear side airbag connector","Damaged lead in the rear door transition or rear seat backrest","Internal fault in the rear left side airbag module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Rear left side airbag may not deploy in a side impact","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0038","B0020","B0040"],"בקרת הפעלת כרית אוויר צד שמאלי שורה שנייה"],B0031:["Second Row Left Frontal Stage 1 Deployment Control","B0031 points to the first firing stage of a frontal airbag that protects the left rear passenger, so it can only be stored where such a bag exists. The known production case is Mercedes-Benz's S-Class of 2020: an optional rear airbag (standard on the Maybach) unfolds from the back of the front seat for the two outer rear seats, built as a gas-filled tube frame that draws ambient air into its cushion.",["Loose or corroded connector of the airbag lead routed through the front seat backrest","Internal fault in the rear-seat airbag module in the front seatback","Lead stretched or pinched by the seat track or folding mechanism","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left rear passenger may lose frontal airbag protection in a crash","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0032","B0033","B0039","B0030"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי שמאלי שורה שנייה‏ 1"],B0032:["Second Row Left Frontal Stage 2 Deployment Control","B0032 concerns a second igniter for the rear-seat frontal airbag on the left. A second stage lets the module add gas later or skip it, depending on crash severity and on who sits behind the seat; a Mercedes-Benz filing for a backrest-mounted rear airbag allows separate deployment devices for its chambers so they can fire in sequence.",["Loose or corroded connector of the airbag lead routed through the front seat backrest","Open or short only in the stage 2 pair of wires to the rear airbag","Faulty second igniter inside the rear-seat airbag module","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Rear-seat airbag may inflate with less force or not at all","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0031","B0033","B003A"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי שמאלי שורה שנייה‏ 2"],B0033:["Second Row Left Frontal Stage 3 Deployment Control","B0033 is the third deployment element of a frontal airbag for the left second-row seat. A third igniter can be a further gas chamber; a Breed patent describes an inflator with one igniter per chamber whose firing order and 0 to 25 ms delays the controller chooses. Mercedes-Benz fills the stage 3 slot of its front bags with the vent valve squib (B000313, B001213), a model for what stage 3 may mean behind a seat.",["Connector position assurance lock missing or not seated, so the plug works loose","Damaged stage 3 lead or igniter in the rear airbag","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Adaptive inflation of the left rear airbag is lost","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0031","B0032","B003B"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי שמאלי שורה שנייה‏ 3"],B0034:["Right Side Deployment Stage 2 Control","B0034 is absent from the J2012 lists, which skip from B0033 to B0038 in the second-row block, and no carmaker or bulletin documents it publicly; the code cannot be traced to a real vehicle. The title describes a second firing stage for the right side airbag.",["Poor contact or corrosion at the side airbag connector or jumper harness under or in the seat","Fault in the squib loop the module assigns to this code","Fault or unsuitable software in the restraint control module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right side airbag protection may be reduced","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0028","B0036","B0025"],"בקרת שלב הפעלת צד ימני‏ 2"],B0036:["Right Side Deployment Stage 2 Loop Short to Ground","B0036 appears neither in the public J2012 lists nor in any accessible manufacturer document, so the code is not publicly verifiable. Its title describes a short to ground in a second stage of the right side airbag.",["Chafed side airbag lead touching the seat frame or body","Connector lock not engaged, shorting bars bridge the loop","Internal short in the side airbag module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right side airbag may not deploy in a side impact","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0034","B0028","B0023"],""],B0038:["Second Row Right Side Airbag Deployment Control","B0038 watches the firing loop of the side airbag for the right-hand second-row seat, fitted in the rear door trim or in the outer bolster of the rear backrest. Mitsubishi lists it as rear side airbag module RH with exactly this J2012 wording and logs B0038-12 when the circuit has been shorted to supply for 2 seconds.",["Poor contact at the rear side airbag connector in the door or rear seat","Internal fault in the right rear side airbag module","Lead chafed against a powered wire, e.g. at the rear seat fold or B-pillar"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right rear passenger may lack side airbag protection","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0030","B0028","B0048"],"בקרת הפעלת כרית אוויר צד ימני שורה שנייה"],B0039:["Second Row Right Frontal Stage 1 Deployment Control","B0039 belongs to the right-hand rear-seat frontal airbag, stage 1, which is the primary charge that the module fires in any frontal crash severe enough to need the bag. The bag sits in the back of the passenger seat ahead; Mercedes-Benz offers this layout as an S-Class option and fits it as standard to the Maybach, where it is meant to ease head and neck loads on belted outer rear passengers.",["Loose or corroded connector of the airbag lead routed through the front seat backrest","Internal fault in the right rear-seat airbag module","Lead stretched or pinched by the seat track or folding mechanism","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right rear passenger may lose frontal airbag protection","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B003A","B003B","B0031","B0038"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי ימני שורה שנייה‏ 1"],B003A:["Second Row Right Frontal Stage 2 Deployment Control","B003A covers stage 2 of the right rear-seat frontal airbag. The second charge allows the module to soften or strengthen inflation; for a rear bag this matters because the person behind the front seat may be an adult, a child or a child seat facing either way, a point Mercedes-Benz stressed when it introduced the S-Class rear airbag in 2020.",["Loose or corroded connector of the airbag lead routed through the front seat backrest","Open or short only in the stage 2 pair of wires","Faulty second igniter in the right rear-seat airbag","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Rear airbag may not adapt its inflation to the occupant","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0039","B003B","B0032"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי ימני שורה שנייה‏ 2"],B003B:["Second Row Right Frontal Stage 3 Deployment Control","B003B is the third firing element of the right rear-seat frontal airbag. In front airbags Mercedes-Benz uses this third position for the squib that opens a vent valve and lets gas escape (B000313 driver, B001213 passenger); a patent from Breed shows the other option, a third gas chamber with its own igniter that the controller can fire later, for example in a second impact.",["Loose or corroded connector of the airbag lead routed through the front seat backrest","Damaged stage 3 lead or vent squib in the right rear airbag","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right rear airbag may deploy without its adaptive third stage","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0039","B003A","B0033"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי ימני שורה שנייה‏ 3"],B0040:["Third Row Left Side Airbag Deployment Control","B0040 is reserved for a side airbag at the left seat of a third row, as found in some seven-seat SUVs and vans; most of them protect that row only with an extended curtain. A Joyson (TK Holdings) patent states its seatback side module may serve any row, third included, and a GM application gives rear-row side bags their own gas generators and allows the rear row to be the third.",["Poor contact at the side airbag connector of the third-row seat or rear quarter trim","Lead strained by folding or removing the third-row seat","Internal fault in the third-row side airbag"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left third-row occupant may lack side airbag protection","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0048","B0030","B0041"],"בקרת הפעלת כרית אוויר צד שמאלי שורה שלישית"],B0041:["Third Row Left Frontal Stage 1 Deployment Control","B0041 would report the first stage of a frontal airbag for the left third-row seat, which would have to deploy from the back of the second-row seat in front of it. Such bags are described in patents, for instance a Daimler application for an airbag at the rear of a front seat and a Mercedes-Benz filing that compensates for a sliding seat with stacked chambers, but no production vehicle with third-row frontal airbags…",["Loose connector of the airbag lead in the second-row seatback","Lead strained when the second-row seat is folded or slid","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Frontal airbag for the left third-row seat may not deploy","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0042","B0043","B0049","B0040"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי שמאלי שורה שלישית‏ 1"],B0042:["Third Row Left Frontal Stage 2 Deployment Control","B0042 stands for the second stage of a frontal airbag aimed at the left third-row passenger. A second stage only makes sense with an inflator that has two independently fired charges, as in Breed's multi-chamber design where the controller picks which chamber fires first and the gap between them. No carmaker documents B0042 for the third row, and no series car with such a bag is known.",["Open or short only in the stage 2 wiring","Connector lock not engaged at the airbag plug","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Adaptive two-stage inflation for this seat is unavailable","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0041","B0043","B004A"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי שמאלי שורה שלישית‏ 2"],B0043:["Third Row Left Frontal Stage 3 Deployment Control","B0043 completes the left third-row frontal group as its stage 3 element. By analogy with front airbags this can be a vent valve squib, as Mercedes-Benz uses for B000313 and B001213, or a further gas chamber like the third chamber in Breed's patent that is kept for a second collision. No public source ties B0043 to a third-row bag.",["Damaged stage 3 lead or squib","Short between two firing loops in a shared harness","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Third deployment element of this airbag is disabled","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0041","B0042","B004B"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי שמאלי שורה שלישית‏ 3"],B0046:["Left Curtain Deployment Loop Open","B0046 appears in none of the accessible J2012 code lists, which jump from B0043 to B0048, and no carmaker or bulletin uses it publicly, so the code cannot be traced to a vehicle. Its title describes an open firing loop of the left curtain airbag that drops from the roof rail.",["Unplugged or loose curtain airbag connector at the pillar or roof rail","Broken lead in the roof rail harness, e.g. after headliner work","Open igniter inside the left curtain airbag"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left curtain airbag may not deploy in a side impact or rollover","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0047","B0021","B0022"],"חוג הפעלת וילון שמאלי — נתק"],B0047:["Left Curtain Deployment Loop Short to Ground","B0047 is missing from the accessible J2012 lists as well, and no vehicle maker or NHTSA bulletin documents it, so it is not publicly traceable. The title names a grounded left curtain airbag loop; this inflatable curtain covers the side windows in side impacts and rollovers.",["Insulation of the curtain lead chafed through against the body","Lead pinched by a pillar trim or headliner clip","Internal short to housing in the left curtain airbag"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left curtain airbag deployment may be blocked","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0046","B0021","B0029"],""],B0048:["Third Row Right Side Airbag Deployment Control","B0048 is the right-hand counterpart of B0040: the deployment loop of a side airbag for the right seat in a third row. Few vehicles have one, because the third row usually relies on a curtain that reaches back to the D-pillar.",["Poor contact at the third-row right side airbag connector","Lead damaged by folding, sliding or removing the third-row seat","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right third-row occupant may lack side airbag protection","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0040","B0038","B0049"],"בקרת הפעלת כרית אוויר צד ימני שורה שלישית"],B0049:["Third Row Right Frontal Stage 1 Deployment Control","B0049 marks the stage 1 charge of a right third-row frontal bag, the main charge of a bag that would have to come out of the second-row seatback ahead of it. Daimler's application for a bag mounted behind a front seat and Mercedes-Benz's later design with chambers that bridge a changing seat gap show how such a bag can be built;",["Loose connector of the airbag lead in the second-row seatback","Lead strained when the second-row seat is folded or slid","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Frontal airbag for the right third-row seat may not deploy","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B004A","B004B","B0041","B0048"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי ימני שורה שלישית‏ 1"],B004A:["Third Row Right Frontal Stage 2 Deployment Control","B004A is the second-stage loop of the right third-row frontal airbag. Stage 2 is a separately ignited charge: Breed's patent shows an inflator whose chambers each carry their own igniter, fired alone, together or with a delay chosen by the controller, and Mercedes-Benz's rear airbag filing allows one deployment device per chamber for sequential filling.",["Open or short only in the stage 2 wiring","Loose connector in the second-row seatback","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Two-stage inflation for the right third-row seat is lost","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0049","B004B","B0042"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי ימני שורה שלישית‏ 2"],B004B:["Third Row Right Frontal Stage 3 Deployment Control","B004B is the last code of the third-row frontal block: stage 3 of the right-hand bag. What a third element does is up to the maker. Mercedes-Benz shows one answer in its front airbags, where the third slot is a vent valve squib (B000313, B001213); Breed's patent shows another, a third chamber held back for a later second impact.",["Damaged stage 3 lead or squib","Restraint module configured for equipment the vehicle does not have (wrong part or coding)","Loose connector in the second-row seatback"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right third-row airbag may deploy without its third element","Safety note: do not probe the airbag circuit yourself; unplug airbag connectors only with the battery disconnected and the stated wait time observed"],4,0,["B0049","B004A","B0043"],"בקרת הפעלת שלב חזיתי ימני שורה שלישית‏ 3"],B0050:["Driver Seat Belt Sensor","B0050 monitors the switch in the driver's belt buckle that tells the restraint module whether the belt is latched; the module uses it for the belt reminder and for choosing the airbag and pretensioner response. Usually a two-wire Hall sensor whose current changes when the steel tongue enters the buckle.",["Corroded terminals at the inline connector between buckle and seat harness","Faulty Hall sensor or switch inside the driver buckle","Buckle lead pinched or stretched by the seat track","Foreign object or debris in the buckle confusing the sensor"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Belt reminder for the driver may warn wrongly or stay silent","Restraint module may treat the driver as unbelted and adapt airbag and pretensioner firing","Safety note: the buckle connector sits under the seat next to the side airbag and pretensioner plugs; disconnect the battery and observe the wait time before unplugging anything"],4,0,["B0051","B0052","B0070"],"חיישן חגורת בטיחות נהג"],B0051:["First Row Center Seat Belt Sensor","B0051 belongs to the buckle sensor of a middle seat in the front row, found in pickups and vans with a front bench for three. FMVSS 208 requires a belt warning only for the outboard front seats, so a centre buckle sensor is extra equipment that feeds the restraint module and, where fitted, a reminder for that place. Typical hardware is a non-contacting Hall buckle switch as offered by CTS and described by Allegro.",["Loose or corroded connector of the centre buckle under the bench seat","Faulty Hall switch in the centre buckle","Lead strained by a fold-down centre seat or console"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Centre seat belt reminder may be wrong or missing","Safety note: the buckle connector sits under the seat next to the side airbag and pretensioner plugs; disconnect the battery and observe the wait time before unplugging anything"],4,0,["B0050","B0052","B0071"],""],B0052:["Passenger Seat Belt Sensor","B0052 concerns the front passenger's buckle sensor, reporting to the airbag module whether the tongue is latched. That signal feeds the passenger belt reminder that FMVSS 208 requires at the front outboard seats and helps the module decide how the passenger airbag and pretensioner fire.",["Loose or corroded buckle connector under the passenger seat","Faulty Hall sensor inside the passenger buckle","Buckle lead pinched or torn by the seat rails or a mat fixing","Input fault inside the airbag control module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger belt reminder warns although the belt is fastened, or stays silent","Passenger airbag and pretensioner strategy may assume an unbelted occupant","Safety note: the buckle plug sits under the seat next to airbag and pretensioner plugs; only unplug it with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0050","B0051","B0053","B0072"],"חיישן חגורת בטיחות נוסע"],B0053:["Second Row Left Seat Belt Sensor","B0053 is the J2012 slot for the buckle sensor at the second row's left seat. Rear buckle sensors drive the rear belt reminder: for vehicles built from September 2028, FMVSS 208 S7.5(c) demands a start-up display of which rear belts are fastened or open and a warning when one is unlatched while driving. No carmaker documents B0053 with this meaning publicly;",["Loose or corroded buckle connector under the left rear seat","Faulty switch or Hall sensor in the left rear buckle","Lead damaged by folding or sliding the second-row seat","Older GM/Saab module: deployment record with a loop fault, module replacement needed"],["Airbag or rear belt warning lamp on","Rear belt display shows the left seat wrongly as fastened or unfastened","Safety note: the buckle plug sits under the seat near pretensioner and side airbag plugs; only unplug it with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0054","B0055","B0073","B0052"],"חיישן חגורת בטיחות שמאלית שורה שנייה"],B0054:["Second Row Center Seat Belt Sensor","B0054 is reserved for the buckle sensor of the middle seat in the second row. That position often has its buckle in a split bench or under a fold-down armrest, so the lead runs through moving seat parts. The rear warning required by FMVSS 208 S7.5(c) for vehicles made from September 2028 covers every rear designated seat, the middle one included.",["Lead of the centre buckle strained at the split bench or armrest hinge","Loose or corroded connector of the centre buckle","Faulty Hall switch in the centre buckle"],["Airbag or rear belt warning lamp on","Middle rear seat shown wrongly in the belt status display","Safety note: buckle plugs under the rear bench lie close to pretensioner wiring; only unplug them with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0053","B0055","B0074"],"חיישן חגורת בטיחות מרכזית שורה שנייה"],B0055:["Second Row Right Seat Belt Sensor","B0055 stands for the buckle sensor of the right seat in the second row, behind the front passenger and in vans often beside the sliding door. Where that seat is a removable captain's chair, a disconnect in the buckle lead is unavoidable; IEE points out in a patent that a wireless buckle sensor alone cannot tell the module whether the seat is fitted, so a missing signal may mean a fault or simply an empty floor.",["Seat connector not engaged after the removable seat was refitted","Corroded buckle connector, e.g. from wet floor near the sliding door","Faulty sensor in the right rear buckle"],["Airbag or rear belt warning lamp on","Right rear seat shown wrongly or missing in the belt status display","Safety note: seat and buckle plugs under the seat lie near pretensioner and side airbag lines; only unplug them with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0053","B0054","B0075"],"חיישן חגורת בטיחות ימנית שורה שנייה"],B0056:["Third Row Left Seat Belt Sensor","B0056 belongs to the left third-row seat's buckle sensor, found in larger SUVs, minivans and seven-seat estates. Third-row seats usually fold flat into the floor, so the buckle lead has to pass through the folding mechanism and is flexed every time the cargo area is extended.",["Buckle lead broken or chafed in the fold-flat mechanism of the third row","Loose or corroded connector at the third-row seat","Faulty sensor in the left third-row buckle"],["Airbag or rear belt warning lamp on","Fault may appear only with the third-row seat folded or raised","Safety note: third-row buckle plugs can sit near pretensioner wiring; only unplug them with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0057","B0058","B0076"],"חיישן חגורת בטיחות שמאלית שורה שלישית"],B0057:["Third Row Center Seat Belt Sensor","In J2012, B0057 is the buckle sensor for the third row's centre seat, a position found only in eight-seat vans and SUVs. FMVSS 208 S7.5(c) will require a belt warning there from September 2028. No carmaker documents B0057 publicly with this meaning.",["Faulty buckle sensor or lead at the middle third-row seat","Older GM trucks: broken wire in the rear door harness to the pretensioner (bulletin 14609)","Older GM/Saab module: shorted passenger pretensioner squib or connector"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Depending on the module: wrong belt status for the middle third-row seat, or passenger pretensioner possibly inactive","Safety note: buckle and pretensioner plugs carry firing circuits nearby; only unplug them with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0056","B0058","B0077","B0064"],"חיישן חגורת בטיחות מרכזית שורה שלישית"],B0058:["Third Row Right Seat Belt Sensor","B0058 is the J2012 code for the buckle sensor at the right seat of the third row. The sensor reports a latched or free belt to the module that runs the rear belt display, which FMVSS 208 S7.5(c) makes mandatory for every rear seat from September 2028. Fold-flat third rows and access from the right-hand sliding door put the lead under strain. No carmaker documents B0058 publicly with this meaning.",["Buckle lead of the right third-row seat damaged by folding or loading","Older GM/Saab module: open passenger pretensioner loop, e.g. broken rear door wire","Faulty sensor in the right third-row buckle"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Depending on the module: right third-row seat shown wrongly, or passenger pretensioner may not fire","Safety note: buckle and pretensioner plugs carry firing circuits nearby; only unplug them with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0056","B0057","B0078"],"חיישן חגורת בטיחות ימנית שורה שלישית"],B0060:["Driver Seat Belt Tension Sensor","B0060 refers to a belt tension sensor in the driver's belt, a force gauge usually bolted to the lower anchor with the webbing running through it. In Delphi's design a spring-loaded slider moves against the belt pull and a Hall element between two magnets turns the travel into a voltage; the springs give way at roughly 5 to 15 lb.",["Loose or corroded connector at the anchor-mounted tension sensor","Tension sensor output stuck or out of range, e.g. jammed slider","Sensor lead pinched under the seat or at the sill trim"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Restraint module may fall back to a default firing strategy for the driver","Safety note: the sensor plug sits beside the seat near pretensioner and side airbag plugs; only unplug it with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0061","B0050","B00B5"],"חיישן מתיחת חגורת בטיחות נהג"],B0061:["Passenger Seat Belt Tension Sensor","B0061 covers the belt tension sensor of the front passenger seat, a key input for passenger occupant classification. FMVSS 208 lets carmakers meet the child-seat rules for advanced airbags by fitting a system that automatically switches the passenger airbag off for small occupants. A child seat strapped in tightly presses into the cushion and can look as heavy as an adult on the weight sensor;",["Loose or corroded plug at the passenger belt tension sensor","Tension sensor reading out of range or stuck","Input fault in the occupant classification or airbag module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag status indicator may show an unexpected on or off state","A tightly fastened child seat may not be recognised reliably","Safety note: the sensor plug sits beside the passenger seat near airbag and pretensioner plugs; only unplug it with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0060","B0052","B00A0"],"חיישן מתיחת חגורת בטיחות נוסע"],B0062:["Knee Airbag Deployment Loop Short to Ground","None of the publicly available J2012 code lists contain B0062; they jump from B0061 to B0070, and no carmaker describes it with the knee airbag meaning shown in the title. J2012 files knee airbag loops under B0004 for the driver and B0013 for the passenger, with the fault type in the added byte;",["Knee airbag lead chafed against a dash bracket or steering column part","Damaged knee airbag connector after work under the dashboard","Saab 9-3: fault in the driver-side curtain or rollover bar loop instead"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Knee airbag may stay inactive in a frontal crash","Safety note: knee airbag plugs sit under the dashboard; do not probe the circuit and only unplug them with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0004","B0013"],""],B0064:["Driver Seat Belt Pretensioner Deployment Loop Resistance Low","No publicly available J2012 code list includes B0064; there, B0060 names the driver belt tension sensor. Older airbag modules from General Motors do use it: on the 2006 Saab 9-5, B0064 is set when the resistance of the driver pretensioner loop stays below 1.5 ohms, with a 0.2-ohm tolerance, for 2 seconds; B0065 marks an interrupted loop and B0066 a voltage at pin 34 outside 1.0 to 4.1 V.",["Pretensioner leads shorted together, e.g. squashed harness at the B-pillar","Colorado/Canyon extended cab: fatigued wires in the rear door harness (bulletin 14609)","Damaged or contaminated pretensioner connector","Internal fault of the driver pretensioner squib"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Driver belt pretensioner may not work properly in a crash","Safety note: pretensioner plugs sit at the B-pillar or under the seat; do not probe the loop and only unplug them with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0060","B0070","B0057"],"התנגדות חוג הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות נהג — ערך נמוך"],B0070:["Driver Seat Belt Pretensioner A Deployment Control","B0070 covers the firing loop of the driver's first (A) belt pretensioner, the squib the airbag module ignites to take slack out of the belt in a crash. A short or open in that loop lets the module no longer count on the device, so it lights the airbag lamp.",["Loose or corroded plug at the driver pretensioner (B-pillar base or seat side)","Firing lead chafed by seat rails or trim clips","Interference from added electronics, e.g. a wireless charger (Toyota Tundra 2022, ECU update)","Internal fault in the pretensioner squib"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Driver belt is not tightened in a crash; airbags themselves are usually unaffected","Safety note: the pretensioner is a pyrotechnic part; work on it only with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed, ideally at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0079","B007E","B0072","B0050"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות נהג‏ A"],B0071:["First Row Center Seat Belt Pretensioner Deployment Control","B0071 is reserved for a pretensioner at the middle seat of the first row, which exists only where a three-person front bench is fitted. The airbag module would watch this squib like any other firing loop and flag an open, a short or a resistance outside its window. No carmaker publishes B0071 with this meaning.",["Plug under the front bench centre seat loose or corroded","Harness damaged when the centre seat or console is folded or removed","Airbag module configured for a centre pretensioner the vehicle does not have","Internal fault of the centre pretensioner"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Middle front occupant gets no belt pretensioning in a crash","Safety note: pyrotechnic component; disconnect the battery, wait the specified time and leave the work to a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0070","B0072","B0074"],""],B0072:["Passenger Seat Belt Pretensioner A Deployment Control","B0072 reports a fault in the deployment loop of the front passenger's A-stage belt pretensioner. While that loop is faulty the device cannot be relied on to fire, so the airbag module lights its lamp and keeps the code.",["Passenger pretensioner plug not latched or corroded","Lead pinched at the passenger seat base or B-pillar trim","Interference from added electronics such as a wireless charger","Pretensioner squib with internal fault"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Front passenger belt may stay slack in a crash","Safety note: the pretensioner is pyrotechnic; only handle it de-energised (battery off, wait time) and have it serviced at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B007A","B007F","B0070","B0052"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות נוסע‏ A"],B0073:["Second Row Left Seat Belt Pretensioner Deployment Control","B0073 concerns the pretensioner at the left outer seat of the second row, normally built into the rear retractor. Mitsubishi documents it under exactly this name: with the ignition on, its airbag sensor unit stores B0073 with byte 11, 12, 13, 1A or 1B for a short to ground, a short to power, an open, lines shorted to each other or excessive resistance, and with byte 55 when the stored configuration does not match…",["Plug at the left rear retractor loose or damaged after trim or seat removal","Harness to the left rear pretensioner shorted to ground or power","Airbag module configuration does not match the fitted rear pretensioners (Mitsubishi byte 55)","Internal fault of the left rear pretensioner or of the airbag module"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left rear occupant gets no belt pretensioning in a crash","Safety note: pyrotechnic part in the rear retractor; work only with the system de-energised and preferably at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0075","B007B","B00E3","B0053"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות שמאלית שורה שנייה"],B0074:["Second Row Center Seat Belt Pretensioner Deployment Control","B0074 would flag the firing loop of a pretensioner at the second row's middle seat. Rear centre belts with their own pretensioner are rare; IIHS rear-seat tests concentrate on the outboard positions, and no carmaker publishes B0074 with the J2012 meaning.",["On GM vehicles, fault in the passenger presence sensor mat or its pinched wire (older GM meaning)","Plug of the rear centre pretensioner disturbed when the bench is folded or removed","Open or short in the harness to the rear centre seat"],["Airbag warning lamp on","On GM vehicles also passenger airbag status shows OFF with an adult seated","Safety note: restraint parts may be pyrotechnic or part of the airbag control; disconnect the battery, observe the wait time and use a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0073","B0075","B007D","B00E5"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות מרכזית שורה שנייה"],B0075:["Second Row Right Seat Belt Pretensioner Deployment Control","B0075 is the right-hand counterpart of B0073: the pretensioner at the second row's right outer seat. Mitsubishi lists it as PRE-TEN REAR RH with the J2012 title and tests the circuit whenever the ignition is on; byte 11 stands for a short to ground and 13 for an open circuit, while further bytes cover shorts to power, crossed wires, high resistance or a configuration mismatch, each after 2 seconds.",["Plug at the right rear retractor not fully latched after interior work","Chafed lead to the right rear pretensioner (short to ground or power)","Interference from added electronics, fixed by an ECU update (Toyota Tundra 2022)","Internal fault of the right rear pretensioner"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right rear occupant without belt pretensioning in a crash","Safety note: the rear retractor contains a pyrotechnic charge; work on it only de-energised and leave it to a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0073","B007C","B00E4","B0055"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות ימנית שורה שנייה"],B0076:["Third Row Left Seat Belt Pretensioner Deployment Control","B0076 belongs to the pretensioner at the left seat of the third row, a position found only in vehicles with a third seat row. No carmaker publishes B0076 with this meaning. Mercedes shows how third-row units are logged in practice: its LI54.21-P-070658 names open-circuit faults of the emergency tensioning retractors at the left and right of the third seat row as B00E7 and B00E6, the C-stage slots, so a B0076 is not…",["Plug at the third-row left belt disturbed by folding or removing the seat","Harness damaged by luggage or trim work in the cargo area","Airbag module coded for a third-row pretensioner that is not fitted"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Third-row left occupant without pretensioning in a crash","Safety note: pyrotechnic belt component; disconnect the battery and wait before touching it, repair at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0077","B0078","B00E7"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות שמאלית שורה שלישית"],B0077:["Third Row Center Seat Belt Pretensioner Deployment Control","B0077 stands for the pretensioner at the middle seat of the third row. Hardly any vehicle fits one, and no manufacturer documents B0077 with this J2012 meaning; Mercedes, which equips some models with third-row tensioning retractors, lists only a left and a right unit (B00E7/B00E6). The number is met more often in older GM-built Saabs.",["On older Saab 9-3/9-5, fault at the driver-side side-impact or B-pillar sensor (older GM meaning)","Plug of the third-row centre pretensioner disturbed during seat folding or removal","Airbag module coded for a centre pretensioner that is not installed"],["Airbag warning lamp on","On Saab, side airbag deployment on the driver side may be impaired","Safety note: airbag sensors and pretensioners belong to the pyrotechnic restraint system; work only de-energised and at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0076","B0078","B00E8"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות מרכזית שורה שלישית"],B0078:["Third Row Right Seat Belt Pretensioner Deployment Control","B0078 refers to the right seat of the third row and its belt pretensioner. No carmaker publishes B0078 in this J2012 sense, and Mercedes models with third-row tensioning retractors log the right-hand unit as B00E6 instead.",["On older Saab 9-3/9-5, fault at the passenger-side side-impact or B-pillar sensor (older GM meaning)","Plug at the third-row right belt loosened when the seat was folded or removed","Internal fault of the third-row right pretensioner"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Third-row right occupant without pretensioning, or on Saab impaired side-impact detection on the passenger side","Safety note: pyrotechnic restraint parts; only work on them with the battery disconnected, after the wait time, at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0076","B0077","B00E6"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות ימנית שורה שלישית"],B0079:["Driver Seat Belt Pretensioner B Deployment Control","B0079 marks the driver's second (B) pretensioner. Mercedes-Benz uses the code in exactly this way: in LI54.21-P-070658, valid for A-Class, CLA and GLB, B007913 is an open circuit in the squib of the belt end fitting tensioner on the driver's side, while the retractor of the same seat appears as B007E.",["Plug at the driver's belt end fitting tensioner beside the seat loose or corroded","Lead to the end fitting tensioner pinched by the seat rail","On a 2006 Saab 9-5, wrong side-impact sensor fitted (older GM meaning)","Internal fault of the end fitting tensioner squib"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Driver's lap belt section not tightened in a crash","Safety note: the end fitting tensioner is pyrotechnic; never probe it live – battery off, wait time, specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0070","B007E","B007A","B0080"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות נהג‏ B"],B007A:["Passenger Seat Belt Pretensioner B Deployment Control","B007A is the passenger-side twin of B0079 and covers the second pretensioner on the front passenger seat. Mercedes lists B007A13 for an open in the squib of the passenger's belt end fitting tensioner on the A-, CLA- and GLB-Class and keeps the passenger retractor apart as B007F.",["Plug at the passenger end fitting tensioner disturbed, e.g. after seat removal","Lead to the lap tensioner pinched under the passenger seat","Internal fault of the passenger lap tensioner"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger's lap belt not tightened in a crash, higher risk of sliding under it","Safety note: pyrotechnic tensioner next to the seat; disconnect the battery, observe the wait time, have a specialist workshop do the repair"],4,0,["B0072","B007F","B0079","B0082"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות נוסע‏ B"],B007B:["Second Row Left Seat Belt Pretensioner B Deployment Control","B007B would cover a second pretensioner on the outboard left seat in row two, for example a lap tensioner in addition to the retractor unit. No manufacturer publishes B007B. The documented rear cases use other slots: Mitsubishi files its left rear retractor pretensioner under B0073, and Mercedes logs the left rear emergency tensioning retractor as B00E3, the C-stage code.",["Plug of the left rear lap or anchor tensioner disturbed when the bench was removed","Airbag module coded for a rear B-stage tensioner that is not fitted","Floor harness to the left rear seat damaged"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left rear lap belt not tightened in a crash","Safety note: pyrotechnic part at the rear seat; work only de-energised (battery off, wait) and at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0073","B007C","B00E3"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות שמאלית שורה שנייה‏ B"],B007C:["Second Row Right Seat Belt Pretensioner B Deployment Control","B007C is the second-row right counterpart of B007B: an additional pretensioner stage at the right outer rear seat. No manufacturer publishes this code. On that seat Mitsubishi uses B0075 for its retractor pretensioner and Mercedes uses B00E4 for the right rear emergency tensioning retractor, so neither leaves a role for B007C. A B stage would typically be a buckle or anchor unit acting on the lap belt;",["Plug of the right rear buckle or anchor tensioner loosened during seat work","Airbag module configuration lists a stage that is not installed","Internal fault of the right rear B-stage tensioner"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right rear lap belt not pretensioned in a crash","Safety note: the tensioner contains a pyrotechnic charge; only work on it with the battery disconnected and at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0075","B007B","B00E4"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות ימנית שורה שנייה‏ B"],B007D:["Second Row Center Seat Belt Pretensioner B Deployment Control","B007D names a second pretensioner at the middle seat of the second row. No carmaker documents it, and since even one pretensioner at the rear centre seat is uncommon, a second stage there is rarer still.",["Plug at the rear centre buckle or anchor tensioner loosened by folding the bench","Airbag module coded for a rear centre B stage that is not present","Harness under the rear bench chafed or pinched"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Rear centre occupant without the second pretensioning stage","Safety note: pyrotechnic belt hardware; de-energise the system (battery off, wait time) and have a specialist workshop do the work"],4,0,["B0074","B007B","B007C","B00E5"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות מרכזית שורה שנייה‏ B"],B007E:["Driver Seat Belt Pretensioner C Deployment Control","B007E is the driver's third (C) pretensioner circuit. Mercedes-Benz fills this slot with the retractor: in LI54.21-P-070658 for the A-, CLA- and GLB-Class, B007E13 is an open circuit at the squib of the driver's emergency tensioning retractor, with B0079 for the belt end fitting tensioner and B0080 for the driver's belt force limiter.",["Retractor plug at the lower driver-side B-pillar loose or terminals spread","Harness pinched by B-pillar or sill trim","Internal fault of the driver retractor pretensioner"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Driver's shoulder belt is not tightened in a crash","Safety note: the retractor holds a pyrotechnic charge; disconnect the battery, wait, and leave the work to a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0070","B0079","B007F","B0080"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות נהג‏ C"],B007F:["Passenger Seat Belt Pretensioner C Deployment Control","B007F covers the passenger's third (C) pretensioner and is the best-documented code of this series. Mercedes lists B007F13 as an open in the squib of the front passenger's emergency tensioning retractor (A-, CLA- and GLB-Class).",["Retractor plug at the lower passenger-side B-pillar loose or with spread terminals (FCA S2008000193)","Body harness pinched between B-pillar trim retainer and body (FCA S2008000137)","Internal fault of the passenger retractor pretensioner"],["Airbag warning lamp on, often after recent interior or body repair","Passenger shoulder belt not tightened in a crash","Safety note: pyrotechnic retractor in the B-pillar; work on it only de-energised (battery off, wait time) and at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0072","B007A","B007E","B0082"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות נוסע‏ C"],B0080:["Driver Seat Belt Load Limiter Deployment Control","B0080 reports a fault in the firing loop that switches the driver's belt force limiter. In adaptive retractors a small squib, fired by the airbag module, changes the level at which the webbing is paid out, so the chest load suits crash severity and occupant.",["Raised contact resistance at the airbag module connector (Mercedes LI54.21-P-070658)","Chafed or disconnected lead to the driver's retractor at the B-pillar","Restraint module software needing an update (Ford Fusion/MKZ)","Internal fault of the load limiter squib in the retractor"],["Airbag warning lamp on, sometimes with an SRS message in the cluster","Driver's belt keeps only its basic force limiting level in a crash","Safety note: pyrotechnic part in the driver's retractor; work only de-energised (battery off, wait time) at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0079","B007E","B0081","B0082"],"בקרת הפעלת מגביל עומס חגורת בטיחות נהג"],B0081:["First Row Center Seat Belt Load Limiter Deployment Control","B0081 is assigned to a squib-switched limiter for the centre place of a three-across front bench. No carmaker publishes the code with this meaning. Mercedes-Benz files a first-row centre tensioning retractor under its own code B1B36, and NHTSA's 2013 study notes that load limiters became universal only at the two outer front seats.",["On GM vehicles, fault or mismatch of the passenger presence module in the seat (different meaning)","Wiring to a centre front seat retractor damaged in the seat base","Internal fault of the centre seat load limiter squib"],["Airbag warning lamp on","On GM vehicles the passenger airbag status shows OFF although an adult is seated","Safety note: airbag system with pyrotechnic parts; diagnose and repair only de-energised at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0071","B0080","B0082","B0084"],""],B0082:["Passenger Seat Belt Load Limiter Deployment Control","B0082 covers the firing loop of the front passenger's switchable belt force limiter. Two manufacturers document this meaning. In the Mercedes A-Class, CLA and GLB, B008213 marks an interrupted igniter of the passenger-side belt force limiter. Ford special service message 51998 covers 2023 Escape, Corsair, Bronco Sport and Maverick that store B0082:1A because of the passenger belt retractor at connector C303B;",["Poor connection at the passenger retractor plug (Ford C303B, SSM 51998)","Raised resistance at the airbag module connector (Mercedes LI54.21-P-070658)","Internal fault of the passenger retractor and limiter assembly"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger belt cannot switch its force limiting level in a crash","Safety note: pyrotechnic retractor at the passenger B-pillar; work only de-energised (battery off, wait time) at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0072","B007A","B007F","B0080"],"בקרת הפעלת מגביל עומס חגורת בטיחות נוסע"],B0083:["Second Row Left Seat Belt Load Limiter Deployment Control","B0083 is intended for a switchable force limiter on the left rear seat. No manufacturer publishes it with this J2012 meaning. Rear load limiters do exist: in an IIHS rear-seat test series presented in 2020, ten vehicles had both pretensioner and limiter at the back and one had a limiter alone. Much more often B0083 is a GM code for another part.",["On GM vehicles, corroded left front impact sensor or unlatched connector lock (PI1480, different meaning)","Wiring to the left rear retractor damaged under trim or seat","Internal fault of the rear load limiter squib"],["Airbag warning lamp on, possibly only intermittently","Left rear belt keeps a fixed limiting level in a crash","Safety note: restraint system with pyrotechnic parts; work only de-energised at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0073","B007B","B0084","B0085"],"בקרת הפעלת מגביל עומס חגורת בטיחות שמאלית שורה שנייה"],B0084:["Second Row Center Seat Belt Load Limiter Deployment Control","B0084 names a squib-switched force limiter for the middle rear seat. Neither a carmaker nor a bulletin shows it with that meaning, and the hardware is rare: NHTSA's 2013 evaluation reports load limiters as standard only at the outer front seats, and the rear centre belt is often a plain retractor.",["On GM vehicles, fault at the right front impact sensor or its plug (different meaning)","On Saab 9-3/9-5, open or short in the driver seat position sensor circuit (different meaning)","Damaged lead to a centre rear limiter where one is fitted"],["Airbag warning lamp on","On Saab 9-3/9-5 the second stage of the driver airbag is disabled","Safety note: airbag system with pyrotechnic parts; diagnose only de-energised at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0074","B007D","B0083","B0085"],"בקרת הפעלת מגביל עומס חגורת בטיחות מרכזית שורה שנייה"],B0085:["Second Row Right Seat Belt Load Limiter Deployment Control","B0085 points to the igniter circuit that would change the force level of the right rear belt. No maker documents it with that meaning. Joyson offers dual-stage limiters with degressive or adaptive behaviour, and an Autoliv patent switches from the stiff to the soft torsion section when the controller fires a squib once cabin deceleration crosses a threshold;",["On GM vehicles, left front side impact sensor or its door wiring faulty (different meaning)","Lead to the right rear retractor pinched by seat or trim","Internal fault of the right rear limiter squib"],["Airbag warning lamp on","On GM vehicles the code clears from history only after 100 fault-free ignition cycles","Safety note: pyrotechnic restraint parts; work only de-energised at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0075","B007C","B0083","B0084"],"בקרת הפעלת מגביל עומס חגורת בטיחות ימנית שורה שנייה"],B0086:["Third Row Left Seat Belt Load Limiter Deployment Control","B0086 is reserved for a switchable force limiter at the left third-row seat. No manufacturer documents it, and an electrically fired limiter that far back is unusual. Delphi's rear-seat patent explains why: without airbags or weight sensing in rear rows, it picks the level from the length of webbing drawn out, about 4–6 kN for a large occupant or a child seat and 2–3 kN for a small occupant.",["On GM vehicles, right front side impact sensor or wiring faulty (different meaning)","Third-row harness stressed by folding or removing the seat","Internal fault of the third-row limiter squib"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left third-row belt limits force only at a fixed level","Safety note: restraint system with pyrotechnic parts; work only de-energised at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0076","B0087","B0088"],"בקרת הפעלת מגביל עומס חגורת בטיחות שמאלית שורה שלישית"],B0087:["Third Row Center Seat Belt Load Limiter Deployment Control","B0087 would flag the igniter circuit of an adaptive belt force limiter on the centre position of row three. That combination is close to theoretical: no carmaker documents the code, and NHTSA's 2013 study dates universal fitment of load limiters (by model year 2007) only for the front outboard seats.",["On GM vehicles, left rear side impact sensor or its connector faulty (different meaning)","Damaged lead to a third-row centre limiter where fitted"],["Airbag warning lamp on","On GM vehicles the AIR BAG indicator is lit by the cluster at the module's request","Safety note: airbag system with pyrotechnic parts; diagnose only de-energised at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0077","B0086","B0088"],"בקרת הפעלת מגביל עומס חגורת בטיחות מרכזית שורה שלישית"],B0088:["Third Row Right Seat Belt Load Limiter Deployment Control","B0088 closes the load limiter series with the right third-row seat. No manufacturer documents it with this meaning. If such a squib-switched limiter is fitted, the module tests its loop for opens, shorts and out-of-window resistance like any igniter; an Autoliv patent shows the principle, where gas from a squib releases a blocking ring so the softer torsion section takes over.",["On GM vehicles, right rear side impact sensor or wiring faulty (different meaning)","Harness to the right third-row seat strained by seat folding","Internal fault of the right third-row limiter squib"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right third-row belt cannot change its limiting level","Safety note: pyrotechnic restraint parts; work only de-energised at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0078","B0086","B0087"],"בקרת הפעלת מגביל עומס חגורת בטיחות ימנית שורה שלישית"],B0090:["Left Frontal Restraints Sensor","B0090 concerns the left frontal crash sensor, a satellite accelerometer in the front crumple zone that tells the airbag module early how hard the front end is being hit. Bosch notes such upfront units sharpen frontal crash detection beside the central sensors. Several makers use the code exactly so.",["Water in the left front sensor connector damaging the harness (Acura 18-016)","Replacement sensor part number not matching the restraint controller (FCA S2408000050)","Restraint controller software needing a reflash (FCA TSB 08-150-26)","Sensor damaged by a front-end impact or poor refitting after body repair"],["Airbag warning lamp on, often after front-end repair or water exposure","Frontal crash detection relies on the module's internal sensor only","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and observe the wait time before touching sensors or wiring, work at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0094","B0095","B0091"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון חזיתית שמאלית"],B0091:["Left Side Restraints Sensor 1","B0091 covers the first left-side crash sensor, which Mitsubishi places in the front door and lists as DOOR SATEL SENS LH with the J2012 title in brackets. The airbag unit checks it with the ignition on and stores a subtype after a two-second delay: -11 for a short to ground, -55 when the configuration held in the unit does not fit the vehicle, -81 for a communication fault, plus further bytes.",["Short or poor contact in the door harness or connector to the sensor","Internal fault of the front door satellite sensor","Airbag unit configuration not matching the vehicle (Mitsubishi subtype -55)","Internal fault of the airbag diagnosis unit"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side and curtain airbags on the left may deploy late or not in a side impact","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and keep the wait time before door work, then have it checked at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0092","B0093","B0096","B0090"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד שמאלי‏ 1"],B0092:["Left Side Restraints Sensor 2","B0092 belongs to the second crash sensor on the left side. Mitsubishi fits it at the left B-pillar and lists it as B-PILLAR SAT SEN LH, adding the J2012 title Left Side Restraints Sensor 2; its index shows only subtype -55, set two seconds after the unit finds that its stored configuration does not fit the vehicle.",["Airbag unit configuration not matching the fitted sensors (Mitsubishi subtype -55)","Loose or corroded plug at the B-pillar sensor after trim or body work","On GM-built Saabs, passenger presence system fault (different meaning)","Internal fault of the B-pillar satellite sensor"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left side impact detection rests on the remaining sensors only","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and keep the wait time before removing pillar trim, work at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0091","B0093","B009A","B0097"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד שמאלי‏ 2"],B0093:["Left Side Restraints Sensor 3","B0093 is the third left-side crash sensor. Mitsubishi mounts it at the left C-pillar, names it C-PILLAR SAT SEN LH and gives the J2012 wording Left Side Restraints Sensor 3. Unlike the B-pillar unit, it carries the full set of subtypes: -11 when the sensor line is shorted to ground, -55 for a configuration mismatch, -81 when communication with the sensor fails, and others, each confirmed after two seconds with the…",["Sensor line shorted to ground or poor contact at the C-pillar plug (subtypes -11/-81)","Internal fault of the C-pillar satellite sensor","Airbag unit configuration not matching the vehicle (subtype -55)","Internal fault of the airbag diagnosis unit"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left side impact sensing behind the front door is degraded","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and keep the wait time before work at the rear pillar, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B0091","B0092","B0098","B009A"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד שמאלי‏ 3"],B0094:["Center Frontal Restraints Sensor","B0094 refers to a single crash sensor placed in the middle of the vehicle front, used where a car has one central frontal satellite rather than a left and right pair. Mitsubishi's airbag unit shows it as CRASH ZONE SENS and adds the J2012 name Center Frontal Restraints Sensor.",["Open, short or corroded contact in the harness to the centre front sensor (subtypes -11/-12/-88)","Internal fault of the crash zone sensor, e.g. offset or self-diagnosis error (subtypes -25/-28)","Sensor or airbag unit not the specified part, or unit configuration wrong (subtypes -86/-55)","Sensor or bracket bent by a front-end impact or refitted poorly after body work"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Frontal crash detection falls back on the sensors inside the airbag unit","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and keep the wait time before work at the front sensor, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B0090","B0095","B0091","B0096"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון חזיתית מרכזית"],B0095:["Right Frontal Restraints Sensor","B0095 is the right-hand partner of B0090: an acceleration satellite in the right front crumple zone that lets the airbag module judge early how severe a frontal hit is. Honda's Fit and HR-V of model years 2016–2017 use the code this way, B0095-87 meaning the right front impact sensor sends nothing; in request AER17060A Honda asked dealers to report such cars before any repair.",["Replacement sensor part number not matching the restraint controller (FCA S2408000050)","Water or road salt in the sensor housing or plug at the right front","Restraint controller software needing a reflash (FCA TSB 08-150-26)","Internal failure of the right front acceleration sensor"],["Airbag warning lamp on, often after front-end repair","Frontal impacts on the right are judged later or less precisely","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and keep the wait time before touching the sensor, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B0090","B0094","B0096"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון חזיתית ימנית"],B0096:["Right Side Restraints Sensor 1","B0096 concerns the first crash sensor on the right side, mirror image of B0091. Mitsubishi puts it in the right front door, calls it DOOR SATEL SENS RH and prints the J2012 title beside it; its airbag unit checks the sensor with the ignition on and, after two seconds, stores -11 for a ground short, -81 when data from the sensor stop and -55 for a configuration that does not fit the car, among nine subtypes in total.",["Chafed wire or poor contact in the door harness between body and right front door","Internal fault of the right front door satellite sensor","Airbag unit configuration not matching the vehicle (Mitsubishi subtype -55)","On Saab 9-3/9-5, passenger belt buckle switch circuit fault (different meaning)"],["Airbag warning lamp on, sometimes only after the right front door has been opened or worked on","Side and curtain airbags on the right may fire late in a side impact","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and keep the wait time before removing the door trim, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B0091","B0097","B0098","B0095"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד ימני‏ 1"],B0097:["Right Side Restraints Sensor 2","B0097 is the second right-side crash sensor. Mitsubishi fixes it at the right B-pillar, lists it as B-PILLAR SAT SEN RH and gives Right Side Restraints Sensor 2 as the J2012 name. Only subtype -55 appears there: the unit flags, after two seconds with the ignition on, that the stored configuration does not match the fitted sensors.",["Airbag unit configuration not matching the fitted sensors, e.g. after unit replacement (Mitsubishi subtype -55)","Plug at the right B-pillar sensor loose or damaged after trim or seat belt work","Right B-pillar sensor sending no signal (Honda subtype -87)","On Saab 9-3/9-5, driver belt buckle switch circuit fault (different meaning)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right side impacts near the B-pillar are detected only by the remaining sensors","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and keep the wait time before removing pillar trim, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B0092","B0096","B0098","B009D"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד ימני‏ 2"],B0098:["Right Side Restraints Sensor 3","B0098 belongs to the third right-side crash sensor. In Mitsubishi's airbag index it is the C-PILLAR SAT SEN RH, given with the J2012 wording Right Side Restraints Sensor 3. The full set of nine subtypes applies, each set two seconds after detection with the ignition on;",["Open or shorted line or poor contact at the right C-pillar plug (subtypes -11/-12/-88/-81)","Internal fault of the right C-pillar sensor, e.g. offset or reset error (subtypes -28/-93)","Airbag unit configuration not matching the vehicle (subtype -55)","On the Saab 9-3, passenger presence system fault (different meaning)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right side impact sensing at the rear door is degraded","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and keep the wait time before work at the rear pillar, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B0093","B0096","B0097","B009D"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד ימני‏ 3"],B0099:["Roll Over Sensor","B0099 reports a fault in the rollover sensing that decides whether curtain airbags and pretensioners fire when a vehicle tips. Bosch integrates rollover sensors in its base airbag control unit, so the sensor is often part of the module.",["Internal fault of the rollover sensor built into the airbag control unit (module replacement)","Airbag unit loose, mounted at an angle or after a crash no longer within its fitting tolerance","Wiring or plug fault where a separate rollover sensor is fitted","Restraint controller software or configuration not matching the vehicle"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Curtain airbags and pretensioners may not fire in a rollover","Safety note: airbag control unit with rollover sensing; work only de-energised (battery off, wait time) at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B0090","B0091","B0095","B0096"],""],B009A:["Left Side Restraints Sensor 4","B009A extends the left-side sensor row past the three positions most cars use. No carmaker documents this code publicly. Mitsubishi's airbag index ends the left row at B0093 (C-pillar), and FCA numbers its pillar satellites in its own B276x range, so neither fills the fourth slot.",["Damaged line or plug to the fourth left sensor, often after seat or trim removal","Internal fault of the fourth left crash satellite","Airbag module coded for a sensor layout the vehicle does not have"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left side impact detection in the area of the missing sensor is weaker","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and keep the wait time before any work on sensors or wiring, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B009B","B009C","B0093","B009D"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד שמאלי‏ 4"],B009B:["Left Side Restraints Sensor 5","B009B names a fifth crash sensor on the left side. No carmaker documents this code publicly, and the reviewed bulletins and airbag indexes stop well before it. Why vehicles carry several side satellites at all follows from FMVSS 214: cars must protect occupants in a moving barrier crash and in a vehicle-to-pole test, and a narrow pole can strike anywhere along the side.",["Line or connector fault on the way to the fifth left sensor","Internal fault of the fifth left satellite (pressure or acceleration type)","Replacement sensor of the wrong part number after a body repair"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side and curtain airbags on the left may deploy later in a side impact","Safety note: airbag system; switch off, disconnect the battery and keep the wait time before work, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B009A","B009C","B009E"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד שמאלי‏ 5"],B009C:["Left Side Restraints Sensor 6","B009C is the sixth and last left-side slot in the J2012 sensor block. No carmaker documents this code publicly. Real vehicles show how many side satellites are usual: FCA's 2019 Jeep Cherokee recall 19V-449 lists two engine bay sensors and four for B- or C-pillar positions, three per side at most, and FCA files those pillar units as B2761 to B2765 rather than in the B009x block.",["Airbag module configured for more side sensors than are fitted","Damaged rear body harness or plug to the sixth left sensor","Internal fault of the sixth left satellite"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side impact sensing at the rear left is reduced","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and keep the wait time, then have it diagnosed at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B009A","B009B","B009F"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד שמאלי‏ 6"],B009D:["Right Side Restraints Sensor 4","B009D opens the second half of the right-side sensor row, after B0096 to B0098. No carmaker documents this code publicly; Mitsubishi stops its right row at the C-pillar sensor B0098, and Honda's Fit and HR-V use only two side sensors per side.",["Communication with the fourth right sensor lost through wiring, plug or sensor fault","Internal fault of the fourth right crash satellite","Airbag module coded for a sensor layout the vehicle does not have"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right side impact detection in the area of that sensor is weaker","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect the battery and keep the wait time before work on sensors, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B009E","B009F","B0098","B009A"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד ימני‏ 4"],B009E:["Right Side Restraints Sensor 5","B009E stands for a fifth crash sensor on the vehicle's right flank. No carmaker documents this code publicly: Mitsubishi's airbag index ends its right row with the C-pillar unit B0098, and the NHTSA bulletin index shows no entry for B009E at all. A fifth right-hand sensor would mostly make sense on long bodies, vans with sliding doors or vehicles with extra seat rows.",["Open, shorted or corroded line or plug to the fifth right sensor, often after door or trim work","Internal fault of the fifth right crash sensor (pressure or acceleration type)","Airbag control unit coded for a sensor that the vehicle does not have"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side and curtain airbags on the right may react later in the area of that sensor","Safety note: airbag system; unplug sensors only with the ignition off, battery disconnected and wait time observed; after replacement have the configuration checked, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B009D","B009F","B009B","B0098"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד ימני‏ 5"],B009F:["Right Side Restraints Sensor 6","B009F would be the sixth and last right-hand restraints sensor in the J2012 block. No carmaker documents it publicly with this meaning. The number does appear at GM, but for another part: on 2008–2013 two-mode hybrid Tahoe, Yukon, Escalade, Silverado and Sierra trucks, bulletin PIT4614C ties a no-crank condition with B009F stored in the SDGM gateway to water passing the seal of the HVCID crash sensor for the…",["Damaged rear body harness or plug to the sixth right sensor","Internal fault of the sixth right acceleration satellite","On GM two-mode hybrids, water or corrosion at the high-voltage impact detection sensor (different meaning, PIT4614C)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","On GM two-mode hybrids, no crank or a Service Hybrid message instead","Safety note: airbag and, on hybrids, high-voltage system; disconnect plugs only de-energised; after a sensor change have it checked or initialised, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B009E","B009D","B009C"],"חיישן מערכת הריסון צד ימני‏ 6"],B00A0:["Occupant Classification System","B00A0 is the catch-all code for occupant classification, the function that judges at the front passenger place whether the passenger airbag may fire and with what force, as FMVSS 208 demands for advanced airbags.",["Poor contact or open circuit in the passenger seat harness or plug, often after seat removal","Low battery voltage or voltage dip while cranking (Mitsubishi -22, Mazda B00A0:09)","Zero-point reset not done or not possible after seat work (Nissan reprograms the unit)","Internal fault of the classification sensor or control unit, often replaced with the seat cushion"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag status lamp shows the wrong state or the passenger airbag stays switched off","Fault may appear only after cold starts with a weak battery","Safety note: airbag system; unplug seat and sensor connectors only de-energised; after replacing seat sensors or the unit, the zero-point reset/calibration must be done, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00A1","B00B0","B00C0"],""],B00A1:["Occupant Position System","B00A1 covers the occupant position system, which watches where a person sits rather than how heavy they are, so that an airbag can be held back when someone is too close to it. FMVSS 208 accepts this as dynamic automatic suppression (DASS): the bag must be switched off before the occupant's head, neck or upper body reach a zone beside the cover that the maker defines. No carmaker publishes B00A1 itself.",["System not initialised after seat cover, seat-back sensor or control unit replacement","Damaged seat harness or loose plug under the seat","Faulty position sensor or position control unit","Damp seat, accessory seat covers or objects disturbing the sensors"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Airbag off indicator stays on although the occupant sits upright","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect seat and sensor plugs only de-energised; after a sensor or unit change initialise/calibrate the system, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00A0","B00B7","B00C7"],"מערכת מצב נוסע"],B00B0:["Driver Seat Occupant Classification Sensor A","B00B0 is the first of five classification inputs on the driver seat. No carmaker publishes this code, and J2012 leaves it to the maker which sensor the letter A means. Classification normally sits in the passenger seat; a Bosch patent notes that it can be omitted on the driver side, on the assumption that drivers are adults, or fitted there as well.",["Open or poor contact in the driver seat harness or plug to input A","Cushion sensor mat creased or damaged, e.g. after seat cover work","Sensor or seat replaced without the required zero-point calibration"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Driver airbag may deploy with a fixed instead of an adapted stage","Safety note: airbag system; unplug seat and sensor connectors only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time); calibrate the sensor after replacement, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B1","B00B2","B00B3","B00B4","B00A0"],""],B00B1:["Driver Seat Occupant Classification Sensor B","B00B1 marks the second of the five driver seat classification sensors. No carmaker documents it publicly, and the letter is not tied to a fixed spot. Seat weight systems often measure at the corners: a CTS patent puts one thick-film strain gauge sensor at each corner between seat pan and slide rail, so the occupant's whole weight passes through four bridges whose leads meet in one junction box before the airbag…",["Seat refitted with wrong bolt torque or distorted mounting, loading the sensor unevenly","Strained or chafed lead to load input B under the seat","Internal fault of the strain gauge sensor"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Weight-based adjustment of the driver airbag unavailable","Safety note: airbag system; work on seat and sensor plugs only de-energised; calibrate the seat sensors after replacement or seat refitting, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B0","B00B2","B00B3","B00B4","B00A0"],""],B00B2:["Driver Seat Occupant Classification Sensor C","B00B2 is the third driver seat classification sensor in the J2012 list. No carmaker documents the code publicly. A widely used sensor type is Bosch's iBolt: the four bolts that anchor the seat frame are swapped for sensor bolts, a magnet and Hall element register how far a bending beam deflects, and the unit derives weight and how it is spread, separating an empty seat, a one-year-old, children of three and six, a…",["Internal fault of the Hall-type sensor bolt at seat anchor C","Sensor bolt overloaded or seat frame bent, e.g. after a crash or wrong torque","Open or poor contact in the lead to input C"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Driver airbag cannot be matched to occupant size","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect seat and sensor plugs only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time); calibrate weight sensors after replacement, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B1","B00B3","B00B0","B00B4","B00A0"],""],B00B3:["Driver Seat Occupant Classification Sensor D","B00B3 refers to the fourth of five driver seat classification inputs. No carmaker publishes it, and the mapping of letters to sensors is undocumented. A fourth input can rest on a different principle: Delphi patented a silicone-filled bladder between cushion foam and seat frame, carrying a pressure sensor and capacitive films whose spacing shrinks under load, so that weight and its spread over the cushion are…",["Seat harness worn by seat movement, open or intermittent contact to input D","Sensor binding or preloaded in the seat structure","Recalibration not done after sensor or unit replacement","Internal fault of the sensor, e.g. leaking bladder or failed pressure cell"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Classification of the driver unavailable for airbag staging","Safety note: airbag system; unplug seat and sensor connectors only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time); recalibrate after any sensor change, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B2","B00B4","B00B1","B00B0","B00A0"],""],B00B4:["Driver Seat Occupant Classification Sensor E","B00B4 is the fifth and last driver seat classification sensor. No carmaker documents the code publicly. A fifth input need not weigh anything: IEE's BodySense uses capacitive sensing in the seat surface, placed over the heater mat, under the cover and on top of the foam, and tells a child restraint from a seated person whatever the belt tension, posture, weight or height;",["Open or poor contact in the seat harness or plug to input E","Damaged seat heater or trim where the capacitive electrode shares its layer","Internal fault of the fifth classification sensor or its electronics"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Possible related faults of the seat heater on the same seat","Safety note: airbag system; work on seat and sensor plugs only de-energised; after replacing a sensor or trim follow the maker's calibration, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B3","B00B2","B00B1","B00B0","B00A0"],""],B00B5:["Driver Seat Track Position Restraints Sensor","B00B5 reports a fault of the driver seat track position sensor, which tells the airbag module whether the seat is pushed far forward toward the steering wheel. FCA uses it with exactly this meaning: GPOP tech tips for the Dodge Dart (PF), Jeep Cherokee (KL) and Chrysler 200 (UF) name B00B5-13, an open circuit, among codes to clear with engineering before replacing the restraint controller, and a 2024 tip for the…",["Open circuit or bent/corroded pins in the seat harness to the track sensor (FCA subtype -13)","Sensor loose or wrongly positioned on the seat track, so the Hall switch no longer sees the track edge","Low system voltage (FCA asks to check this before replacing the controller)","Internal fault of the Hall-effect seat track sensor"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Driver airbag may fire without seat position adjustment (e.g. second stage locked out)","Safety note: airbag system; unplug the seat and sensor connectors only de-energised; after replacing the sensor check its position output/calibration, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B6","B00C5","B0084","B00A0"],""],B00B6:["Driver Seat Recline Position Restraints Sensor","B00B6 concerns a sensor that tells the restraint system how far the backrest of the driver seat is reclined. No carmaker documents this code publicly, and the NHTSA bulletin index has no entry for it.",["Lead pinched or broken at the seat back hinge, where it flexes with every adjustment","Internal fault or loose mounting of the recline sensor","Sensor or seat back replaced without the required zero setting"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Airbag adaptation to a reclined seating position unavailable","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect seat and sensor plugs only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time); calibrate the sensor after replacement, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B5","B00C6","B00A1"],""],B00B7:["Driver Seat Occupant Position Sensor A","B00B7 is the first of five occupant position sensors for the driver seat. No carmaker publishes the code, and J2012 does not say which sensor the letter A means. Position sensing serves the DASS route of FMVSS 208, which also exists for the driver: the driver bag must already be suppressed when a test dummy's head, neck or chest moves into a zone next to the cover that the maker defines.",["Open or poor contact in the lead to position sensor A (e.g. headliner or trim harness)","Sensor face covered, dirty or misaligned after trim work","Internal fault of position sensor A"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Out-of-position suppression of the driver airbag unavailable","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect sensor and seat plugs only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time); calibrate/initialise position sensors after replacement, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B8","B00B9","B00BA","B00BB","B00A1"],"חיישן מצב נוסע מושב נהג‏ A"],B00B8:["Driver Seat Occupant Position Sensor B","B00B8 names the second occupant position sensor at the driver seat. The code is not published by any carmaker, and the letter assignment is the maker's choice. Instead of looking down from the roof, a position sensor can sit at the airbag cover itself: a patent first filed in 1998 by Automotive Systems Laboratory, now held by Joyson, puts an active infrared, ultrasonic or electric field sensor in or near the…",["Fault in the lead to a sensor at the steering wheel or cover, e.g. via the clockspring","Sensor window covered by stickers, covers or dirt","Internal fault of position sensor B"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Airbag cannot be suppressed if the driver is very close to the cover","Safety note: airbag system; work at steering wheel, cover or sensor plugs only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time); calibrate the sensor after replacement, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B7","B00B9","B00BA","B00BB","B00A1"],"חיישן מצב נוסע מושב נהג‏ B"],B00B9:["Driver Seat Occupant Position Sensor C","B00B9 is the third occupant position sensor of the driver seat. No carmaker publishes it. A third input could judge posture from the seat back: a patent now held by Joyson places two electric field electrodes under the seat-back cover, one across the upper middle and inboard side and one along the outboard edge, and combines them with seat weight to block the side airbag when a small occupant leans into its path.",["Seat-back cover or sensor replaced without initialisation","Damaged seat-back harness or plug under the seat","Damp seat or accessory seat cover disturbing the electric field"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side airbag suppression for leaning occupants unavailable","Safety note: airbag system with seat side airbag; disconnect seat plugs only de-energised; initialise/calibrate after sensor or cover replacement, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B8","B00BA","B00B7","B00BB","B00A1"],"חיישן מצב נוסע מושב נהג‏ C"],B00BA:["Driver Seat Occupant Position Sensor D","B00BA covers position input D, the fourth of the driver seat sensors. Its use by a carmaker is not documented publicly. Early out-of-position concepts mixed several sensor kinds: a 1989 Automotive Systems Laboratory patent uses a pyroelectric detector for presence, ultrasound for the distance to wheel and dashboard and a pressure transducer under the occupant for weight, recommends redundant sensors of each kind…",["Open or shorted lead to position sensor D","Signal disagreeing with the other position inputs, e.g. sensor dirty or misaligned","Internal fault of position sensor D"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Staged driver airbag deployment based on position restricted","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect sensor and seat plugs only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time); calibrate position sensors after replacement, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B9","B00BB","B00B8","B00B7","B00A1"],"חיישן מצב נוסע מושב נהג‏ D"],B00BB:["Driver Seat Occupant Position Sensor E","B00BB is the fifth and last driver seat occupant position sensor in the J2012 block. No carmaker publishes this code. Position need not be measured on the body itself: an ATI patent family dating back to 1992 infers it from the seat, using a potentiometer or other track sensor, a recline angle sensor and belt spool-out from a shaft encoder in the retractor, and may suppress or depower the bag when the seat is fully…",["Open, shorted or loose lead to position sensor E","Restraint module configured for a fifth position sensor that is not fitted","Internal fault of position sensor E"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Position-based adjustment of the driver airbag partly unavailable","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect sensor and seat plugs only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time); calibrate the sensor after replacement, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00BA","B00B9","B00B8","B00B7","B00B5"],"חיישן מצב נוסע מושב נהג‏ E"],B00C0:["Passenger Seat Occupant Classification Sensor A","B00C0 flags the first of up to five classification inputs in the front passenger seat. Their job comes from FMVSS 208: the passenger bag must stay off when a 12-month dummy sits in a listed child restraint or a newborn dummy lies in a car bed, yet it must be live for a 5th percentile woman, and a yellow PASSENGER AIR BAG OFF lamp reports the suppressed state.",["Loose plug or chafed wire to input A under the passenger seat, often after the seat was removed","Classification sensor A itself delivers no or an implausible signal","Objects under the seat, items hanging on the seat back or pressure from the rear disturbing the measurement"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag off lamp shows a state that does not match the occupant","Safety note: passenger airbag may be wrongly enabled or disabled; seat and sensor plugs only de-energised, recalibrate the classification after repairs, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00C1","B00C2","B00A0","B00D5","B00B0"],""],B00C1:["Passenger Seat Occupant Classification Sensor B","B00C1 belongs to input B of the passenger seat classification. It is unpublished as such, but Toyota shows why a seat can carry several such sensors: on 2012–2013 Camry, Prius c and Yaris and 2013 Avalon, a left and a right weight detector sit between seat frame and rails. Their readings decide whether the passenger bag is armed, and they also serve as collision sensing.",["Load cell B damaged or drifting, for example after the seat was forced or dropped","Seat pan or sensor bolts fitted under tension or with the wrong torque, preloading the cell","Zero-point calibration not done after sensor or seat work","Poor contact at the plug of sensor B"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag off lamp lit although an adult is seated","Safety note: passenger airbag status may be wrong; disconnect seat sensors only de-energised, keep tightening torques and run the zero-point calibration with the scan tool, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00C0","B00C2","B00A0","B00B1"],""],B00C2:["Passenger Seat Occupant Classification Sensor C","B00C2 names the third classification input of the passenger seat. No carmaker documents it, and nobody has tied the letter to a known part. Another common sensor type besides load cells is a mat in the cushion. Hyundai extended the cover of the OCS mat in 2006–2011 Accent cars to 15 years with unlimited mileage: the mat should spot child seats and small occupants, and a faulty one could let the bag fire for a child;",["Liquid, rain or condensation soaked into the seat cushion and sensor","Sensor mat cracked or worn from years of getting in and out","Damaged lead or plug between mat and classification unit"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Fault may come and go with weather or after cleaning the seat","Safety note: a child on the passenger seat may not be detected; replace mats only as the maker's kit with the seat de-energised, then recalibrate, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00C1","B00C3","B00A0","B00B2"],""],B00C3:["Passenger Seat Occupant Classification Sensor D","B00C3 is the fourth passenger seat classification input. No carmaker documents it under this number. Some classification signals are not a weight at all but a frequency, which makes them prone to electrical noise. Tesla reported for 2017–2019 Model 3 cars that the OCS frequency could leave its valid range because of interference on the passenger seat harness, so the airbag symbol appeared on the touchscreen.",["Electrical interference coupled into the seat harness (seat heating, motors, routing near other leads)","Harness under tension or plug loose at the classification module when the seat moves","Internal fault of sensor D or the classification module"],["Airbag warning lamp or airbag symbol on the display","Fault may depend on seat position or on other electrical loads being switched on","Safety note: occupant classification unreliable; work on seat wiring only de-energised (12 V off, wait time), use the maker's filter or rework kit where one exists, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00C2","B00C4","B00A0","B00B3"],""],B00C4:["Passenger Seat Occupant Classification Sensor E","B00C4 stands for the fifth and last passenger seat classification input; no public carmaker source uses it. Two field cases show what goes wrong besides wiring. Mazda found on 2016–2019 models that a phone, tablet or laptop lying on an empty passenger seat could make the system see a person: the passenger belt warning came on while PASS AIRBAG OFF stayed dark, and the advice was simply to keep devices off the seat.",["Classification module calibrated wrongly or not at all after replacement","Open or high-resistance contact on the lead to input E","Electronic devices or other objects on the seat confusing the sensing"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger belt warning or airbag status lamp does not match who or what is on the seat","Safety note: passenger airbag may stay enabled for a child seat; disconnect only de-energised, calibrate with the maker's procedure after any module change, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00C3","B00C0","B00A0","B00D1","B00B4"],""],B00C5:["Passenger Seat Track Position Restraints Sensor","B00C5 reports a fault of the sensor that tells the restraint controller where the passenger seat sits on its rails. FCA uses the code with exactly this name. A 2022 STAR case for the 2021 Dodge Durango treats B00C5-13, circuit open, with the airbag lamp on: check the yellow 30-way plug I6634A under the passenger seat and make sure the seat track position return wire R730 is seated in cavity B11, using a…",["Terminal pushed back or loose in the under-seat connector (FCA Durango, R730 return wire)","Lead to the track sensor pinched or torn by the moving seat","Track position sensor faulty or its gap to the rail wrong after seat work","Restraint controller internal fault, only after wiring and sensor are ruled out"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag deployment can no longer be adapted to the seat position","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect under-seat plugs only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), do not replace the restraint controller before checking pins, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B5","B00C6","B00A0"],""],B00C6:["Passenger Seat Recline Position Restraints Sensor","B00C6 concerns the sensor that reports how far the passenger seat back is reclined. It appears neither in any public carmaker list nor in NHTSA bulletins. On the passenger side the angle matters mainly for classification, because a reclined back carries part of the occupant's weight.",["Lead to the recline sensor stretched or broken at the seat back hinge","Recline potentiometer or inclination sensor worn or faulty","Angle reference not learned after replacing the seat back or the sensor"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag off lamp may light for an adult sitting with the seat back reclined","Safety note: airbag system; work on seat back and sensor only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), relearn or calibrate afterwards, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00B6","B00C5","B00A0"],""],B00C7:["Passenger Seat Occupant Position Sensor A","B00C7 opens the row of five passenger seat position sensors, a code absent from all public carmaker documents. The passenger seat is where position sensing reached series cars: Honda's OPDS puts sensors in the passenger seat back that judge sitting height and whether a child leans toward the door, and then blocks the seat-mounted side airbag and lights a side airbag off indicator.",["Position system not initialised after seat cover, seat back sensor or control unit replacement","Electrode or lead in the seat back damaged, for instance by a non-original seat cover or repairs","Damp seat back or objects pressed against it"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side airbag off indicator lit although the passenger sits upright","Safety note: side airbag may be wrongly enabled or blocked; work on the seat back only de-energised and initialise the system afterwards, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00C8","B00A1","B00B7"],"חיישן מצב נוסע מושב נוסע‏ A"],B00C8:["Passenger Seat Occupant Position Sensor B","B00C8 marks the second occupant position sensor of the passenger seat. No carmaker publishes it. A position input does not have to look at the person; it can come from how the load spreads over the seat. In a Honda application filed in 2002, a weight unit under each side of the seat carries four strain gauges in a bridge;",["Plug or lead to sensor B damaged when the seat was moved or removed","Strain gauge bridge or position sensor B faulty, drifting with temperature","Seat frame mounted under tension, so the load split looks implausible"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag may be suppressed or released without regard to sitting position","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect seat sensors only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), recalibrate after work on the seat, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00C7","B00C9","B00A1","B00B8"],"חיישן מצב נוסע מושב נוסע‏ B"],B00C9:["Passenger Seat Occupant Position Sensor C","B00C9 names position sensor C of the passenger seat, and no carmaker lists it publicly. One concept for a third input watches the gap between torso and seat back: a patent first filed by Automotive Systems Laboratory in 1998, now with Joyson, pairs an electric field sensor in the cushion with a capacitive or radar proximity sensor in the back, aimed at the band about 10 to 18 inches above the cushion.",["Lead to the seat back sensor broken at the hinge or after trim work","Proximity sensor C faulty or its signal disagrees with the cushion sensor","Thick accessory covers or a wet seat back weakening the field signal"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Airbag status lamp may change while the passenger leans forward","Safety note: airbag system; seat back and sensor only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), no third-party seat covers over sensors, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00C8","B00CA","B00A1","B00B9"],"חיישן מצב נוסע מושב נוסע‏ C"],B00CA:["Passenger Seat Occupant Position Sensor D","B00CA is position input D, the fourth for the passenger seat. Its use is not documented by any carmaker. Optical sensing is one way to fill such a slot: a patent family of Automotive Technologies International, going back to 1995, places imagers with infrared lighting at the A-pillar, in the headliner or on top of the dashboard, two arrays spaced apart for depth, and calls an occupant out of position once head or…",["Lead to sensor D damaged at the pillar, headliner or dashboard after trim or glass work","Sensor view blocked or lens dirty, for example by stickers or accessories","Internal fault of position sensor D"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Out-of-position suppression for the passenger no longer available","Safety note: airbag system; work at pillar, headliner or dashboard only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), recheck sensor alignment afterwards, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00C9","B00CB","B00A1","B00BA"],"חיישן מצב נוסע מושב נוסע‏ D"],B00CB:["Passenger Seat Occupant Position Sensor E","B00CB is the fifth and last passenger seat occupant position sensor. No carmaker publishes it. Position alone is not always enough; an early patent of Automotive Technologies International, first filed in 1992, also wants the speed at which the occupant approaches the bag.",["Open or shorted lead to sensor E in the headliner, mirror base or dashboard","Transducer of sensor E faulty or covered","Restraint module coded for a sensor the vehicle does not carry"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag deploys without position-based suppression or staging","Safety note: airbag system; disconnect sensors only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), check configuration after replacement, specialist workshop only"],4,0,["B00CA","B00C7","B00A1","B00BB"],"חיישן מצב נוסע מושב נוסע‏ E"],B00D0:["Driver Seat Belt Indicator","B00D0 reports a fault in the driver's seat belt warning, meaning the lamp, its circuit or the output or message that drives it, not the buckle switch. No carmaker documents it publicly. The warning itself is mandatory: FMVSS 208 S7.3 asks at ignition-on for a 4 to 8 s chime plus a lamp for at least 60 s while the driver is unbelted, or a 4 to 8 s lamp with the chime tied to the unfastened belt;",["Open or shorted lamp circuit or connector between restraint module and cluster","Warning lamp or LED in the instrument cluster failed","Belt warning message not received by the cluster, for example after a cluster change without configuration"],["Driver belt warning lamp stays dark or stays on regardless of the belt","Airbag or restraint warning lamp may be on","Safety note: legally required warning missing; buckle up regardless, cluster and restraint wiring only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), specialist workshop"],2,0,["B00D1","B0050","B00D2"],"חיווי חגורת בטיחות נהג"],B00D1:["Passenger Seat Belt Indicator","B00D1 covers the passenger seat belt warning. Unlike the driver warning, it only makes sense if the car knows the seat is occupied, so it leans on occupant sensing. No carmaker documents the code. Ford's 2014 F-150 uses the passenger sensing system to decide who gets Belt-Minder reminders: above 6 mph and after 1 to 2 minutes, lamp and chime come on for six seconds every 25 seconds for about five minutes.",["Open or shorted circuit to the passenger belt lamp or its display segment","Lamp, LED or display unit for the passenger warning failed","Occupancy information missing or wrong, so the warning logic cannot run"],["No passenger belt reminder, or a reminder for an empty seat","Airbag or restraint warning lamp may be on","Safety note: passenger may ride unbelted without warning; wiring work only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), specialist workshop"],2,0,["B00D0","B0052","B00A0","B00C0"],"חיווי חגורת בטיחות נוסע"],B00D2:["Restraint System Malfunction Indicator 1","B00D2 means the restraint module has found a fault in the circuit of its primary warning lamp, the airbag or SRS light. FMVSS 208 S4.5.2 requires such a readiness indicator, watching its own readiness and within the driver's view, and FMVSS 101 lets it push other messages out of a shared display. No carmaker publishes B00D2.",["Bulb or LED of the airbag warning lamp failed","Lamp lead open, shorted to ground or to battery voltage, or loose cluster connector","Internal fault in the instrument cluster circuit board"],["Airbag lamp does not come on for the bulb check at ignition-on, or stays on","A substitute warning such as a central warning lamp or a tone may appear","Safety note: airbag faults may go unnoticed; work on cluster and restraint wiring only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), specialist workshop only"],2,0,["B00D3","B00D4","B00D5"],""],B00D3:["Restraint System Malfunction Indicator 2","B00D3 refers to a second restraint malfunction indicator. No carmaker documents which lamp that is, so its meaning has to be inferred. One reading is a backup for the main lamp: the 1995 Saab 900 calls its SRS light warning lamp 1 and switches the central warning lamp on for good if that circuit fails.",["Open or shorted circuit to the second restraint indicator","Second indicator lamp or LED failed","Restraint module or cluster configured for an indicator the vehicle does not have"],["Airbag lamp on, second indicator dark or not doing its bulb check","Backup warning missing if the main airbag lamp also fails","Safety note: restraint warnings incomplete; work on cluster and wiring only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), specialist workshop only"],2,0,["B00D2","B00D4"],""],B00D4:["Restraint System Malfunction Audible Indicator","B00D4 concerns the audible restraint warning, the tone that stands in when a fault cannot be shown by the lamp. Ford's 2014 F-150 manual describes it: system readiness is signalled by the warning light, or by a backup tone if the light is out, and a problem announces itself as five beeps in a row, repeated until the fault and the lamp are put right.",["Open or shorted lead to the chime or speaker used for restraint warnings","Chime module or cluster speaker failed","Tone request from the restraint module not received by the sounding unit"],["No warning tone where one would be expected, other warning chimes may also be silent","Airbag warning lamp on","Safety note: fallback warning missing; work on cluster and restraint wiring only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), specialist workshop"],2,0,["B00D2","B00D3"],""],B00D5:["Restraint System Passenger Disable Indicator","B00D5 concerns the lamp that tells the front occupants the passenger airbag is off. FMVSS 208 wants it yellow, worded PASSENGER AIR BAG OFF (short form PASS AIR BAG OFF) and separate from the readiness lamp; Ford's 2014 F-150 places it by the radio and lights it briefly at start as a self-test.",["Indicator lead shorted to ground, shorted to power or open (Mitsubishi -11/-12/-13)","Passenger airbag off indicator itself failed","Network or gateway software fault, as on 2021 Ford Edge/Nautilus (SSM 50127)","Internal fault of the airbag control unit output"],["Passenger airbag off lamp stays dark during the start check or shows the wrong state","Airbag warning lamp on","Safety note: occupants cannot see whether the passenger airbag is off; do not fit a rear-facing child seat until repaired, wiring only de-energised, specialist workshop"],2,0,["B00DF","B00A0","B00D2","B00C0"],""],B00DF:["Passenger Restraints Disable Switch","B00DF is set for the key switch that lets the passenger airbag be turned off by hand. FMVSS 208 S4.5.4 allowed it on vehicles built before September 2012 with no forward rear seats or a short rear row; it must take the key, stay apart from the ignition and keep the bag off until switched back, and 49 CFR 595.5 governs retrofits under an NHTSA letter. Two makers use the code.",["Switch circuits present in the harness of a vehicle without the switch, damaged or picking up faults (FCA B00DF-95)","Key switch worn or its lead open or shorted","Restraint module software counter or configuration error (Ford B00DF:4A)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag does not follow the switch position, or the off lamp disagrees with it","Safety note: passenger airbag state uncertain; no rear-facing child seat on that seat until checked, wiring and switch only de-energised (ignition off, battery off, wait time), specialist workshop"],2,0,["B00D5","B00A0"],""],B00E0:["Third Row Left Seat Belt Pretensioner B Deployment Control","B00E0 points to a second pretensioner stage (B) on the left seat of the third row. Such a stage would be an extra device next to the retractor, typically a lap or anchor tensioner that pulls on the lower belt end. No carmaker publishes B00E0.",["Plug of the lap or anchor tensioner at the left third-row seat loose, unlatched or corroded","Lead strained or chafed by folding and stowing the third-row seat","Airbag module coded for a B stage the vehicle does not have (after module or seat replacement)","Internal open or short in the tensioner squib"],["Airbag warning lamp lit","Lap belt at the left third-row seat may not be pulled tight in a crash","Safety note: pyrotechnic part – work only with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed, preferably at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00E1","B00E2","B00E7","B0076"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות שמאלית שורה שלישית‏ B"],B00E1:["Third Row Right Seat Belt Pretensioner B Deployment Control","On the right seat of the third row, B00E1 stands for a B-stage tensioner whose firing loop shows an open, a short or an out-of-window resistance. In no public service document does a manufacturer use B00E1. Where Mercedes-Benz fits a right third-row tensioner, it is the retractor, and the airbag unit reports it as B00E6 (LI54.21-P-070658, versions of March and June 2020).",["Connector of the right third-row buckle or anchor tensioner not fully seated","Wiring under the cargo floor or side trim pinched or damaged by loads","Raised contact resistance at the airbag module plug","Defective squib inside the tensioner"],["Airbag lamp on in the instrument cluster","Occupant at the right of the third row gets no B-stage tensioning","Safety note: the tensioner contains a pyrotechnic charge; only work on it de-energised (battery off, wait time) and leave it to a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00E0","B00E2","B00E6","B0078"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות ימנית שורה שלישית‏ B"],B00E2:["Third Row Center Seat Belt Pretensioner B Deployment Control","B00E2 would report the firing circuit of a B-stage tensioner at the centre seat of the third row. This is about the rarest slot in the pretensioner table: a centre seat in row three is uncommon, and a second tensioner stage on it even more so. No manufacturer documents the code.",["Module variant coding expects a centre B stage that is not installed","Plug under the third-row centre seat disconnected after seat removal","Squib of the centre lap tensioner open or shorted internally"],["Airbag indicator stays on after the self-test","Centre occupant of the third row may lack lap-belt tensioning in a crash","Safety note: pyrotechnic restraint component – disconnect the battery, wait the specified time and have the work done by a specialist"],4,0,["B00E0","B00E1","B00E8","B0077"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות מרכזית שורה שלישית‏ B"],B00E3:["Second Row Left Seat Belt Pretensioner C Deployment Control","B00E3 is the C-stage tensioner of the left outer rear seat, and two makers document it codegenau. Stellantis case S2408000089 (Jeep Wrangler 2023) has the occupant restraint controller store B00E3-13, named there for the retractor tensioner at the left of row two, after a service visit; the fix was to secure connector D3244A with a push-pull-push check, no parts.",["Retractor pretensioner plug not latched after trim or seat work (Jeep Wrangler 2023, connector D3244A)","High contact resistance at the airbag control unit connector (Mercedes LI54.21-P-070658)","Lead to the left rear retractor chafed at the C-pillar or seat frame","Faulty squib in the retractor pretensioner"],["Airbag warning lamp or SRS message in the cluster","Left rear shoulder belt is not retracted in a crash","Safety note: the retractor pretensioner is pyrotechnic; work only with the system de-energised (battery off, wait time) and preferably at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00E4","B00E5","B0073","B007B","B0053"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות שמאלית שורה שנייה‏ C"],B00E4:["Second Row Right Seat Belt Pretensioner C Deployment Control","B00E4 belongs to the outboard seat on the right in the back and its C-stage tensioner. Mercedes-Benz uses it in that sense: every version of LI54.21-P-070658 seen here (December 2019 to June 2020) lists B00E413 as an open in the squib of the tensioning retractor at the rear right.",["Poor contact at the SRS control unit plug (Mercedes A-Class/CLA/GLB)","Plug at the right rear retractor loose after trim removal","Airbag control unit itself faulty (fault returns after reconnecting)","Squib in the right rear retractor open"],["SRS message or airbag lamp permanently displayed","Right rear passenger loses shoulder-belt tensioning","Safety note: pyrotechnic tensioner – only work on it with the battery disconnected and after the wait time, ideally at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00E3","B00E5","B0075","B007C","B0055"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות ימנית שורה שנייה‏ C"],B00E5:["Second Row Center Seat Belt Pretensioner C Deployment Control","B00E5 covers a C-stage tensioner at the middle seat of row two. No manufacturer publishes it. Rear centre tensioners are scarce: Mercedes' 2017 GLS manual names tensioners only for the outer second-row belts, and the Mercedes bulletin that assigns B00E3 and B00E4 to the outer rear retractors has no centre entry.",["Centre-seat tensioner plug under the rear bench not engaged","Module coded for a centre tensioner that the vehicle lacks","Lead damaged where it passes the split or folding rear bench hinge"],["Airbag lamp on","Rear centre passenger may not be held back early in a frontal crash","Safety note: the tensioner holds a pyrotechnic charge – battery off, wait time observed, repair at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00E3","B00E4","B0074","B007D","B0054"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות מרכזית שורה שנייה‏ C"],B00E6:["Third Row Right Seat Belt Pretensioner C Deployment Control","Note the order in this block: B00E6 is the right seat of the third row, while B00E7 is the left. Mercedes-Benz fills B00E6 with the retractor tensioner on that seat: LI54.21-P-070658 (first issued December 2019 for A-Class and CLA, extended to GLB in version 4) reads B00E613 as an interrupted igniter in the tensioning retractor on the right of row three.",["Contact resistance at the airbag unit connector (Mercedes LI54.21-P-070658)","Plug of the right third-row retractor behind the cargo trim loose","Wiring in the rear wheel arch area pinched by trim or cargo","Squib of the right third-row retractor defective"],["SRS message or airbag warning lamp","Right third-row belt stays slack in a crash","Safety note: work on this pyrotechnic retractor only de-energised (battery disconnected, wait time) and preferably by a specialist"],4,0,["B00E7","B00E8","B00E1","B0078","B0058"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות ימנית שורה שלישית‏ C"],B00E7:["Third Row Left Seat Belt Pretensioner C Deployment Control","B00E7 marks the C-stage tensioner of the third row's left seat, listed after its right-hand twin B00E6. Mercedes-Benz documents it: LI54.21-P-070658 uses B00E713 when the firing pill of the left third-row tensioning retractor shows an open, in the same list as the rear and driver retractors.",["Raised resistance at the restraint unit plug","Left third-row retractor connector disturbed during trim or seat work","Control unit below the required level, fault keeps returning","Retractor squib open internally"],["Airbag lamp or fixed SRS message","No pretensioning for the left third-row seat","Safety note: pyrotechnic device – disconnect the battery and wait before touching it; have it serviced at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00E6","B00E8","B00E0","B0076","B0056"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות שמאלית שורה שלישית‏ C"],B00E8:["Third Row Center Seat Belt Pretensioner C Deployment Control","B00E8 closes the C row of the table with the centre seat of the third row. No manufacturer publishes it, and the one public list that uses this block, Mercedes-Benz LI54.21-P-070658, stops at a left and a right third-row retractor (B00E7, B00E6). A centre tensioner in row three would mostly appear in large vans or SUVs with a three-seat rear bench.",["Connector of the seat-mounted centre retractor unplugged after removing the rear bench","Restraint module coded for a three-seat third row on a two-seat vehicle","Squib of the centre retractor faulty"],["Airbag warning lamp illuminated","Centre seat of the third row without belt tensioning","Safety note: contains a pyrotechnic charge – no work without disconnecting the battery and waiting; leave it to a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00E6","B00E7","B00E2","B0077","B0057"],"בקרת הפעלת קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות מרכזית שורה שלישית‏ C"],B00F0:["Driver Inflatable Seat Belt Deployment Control","B00F0 is the firing circuit for an inflatable belt at the driver's seat: a section of webbing that a gas source fills in a crash so the load spreads over a wider area of the chest. The production inflatable belts known from Ford and Mercedes-Benz sit only at rear outer seats; no carmaker documents B00F0.",["Airbag module variant expects a driver inflatable belt that is not fitted","Plug of the belt gas generator at the lower anchor or seat loose or corroded","Lead to the inflator chafed by seat adjustment","Igniter of the belt inflator faulty"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Driver belt would not inflate in a crash","Safety note: the belt contains a pyrotechnic gas generator; work only de-energised (battery off, wait time) and at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00F1","B0070","B007E"],""],B00F1:["Passenger Inflatable Seat Belt Deployment Control","B00F1 is the front passenger counterpart of B00F0, reserved for an inflatable belt at that seat. No manufacturer documents it, and no series vehicle is publicly known to have a passenger inflatable belt; Mercedes' S-Class manual offers the beltbag only for the outer rear belts.",["Module coded for a passenger inflatable belt that the car does not have","Connector at the buckle-side inflator under the passenger seat loose","Seat wiring damaged by objects under the seat or by seat movement"],["Airbag lamp lit in the cluster","Passenger belt cannot inflate in a crash","Safety note: pyrotechnic belt inflator – disconnect the battery, respect the wait time and have repairs done by a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00F0","B0072","B007F","B0052"],""],B00F2:["Second Row Left Inflatable Seat Belt Deployment Control","B00F2 covers the inflatable belt at the left outer seat of row two, the position where such belts actually reached production. Ford offered them from the 2011 Explorer; its 2018 owner's manual puts the bag into the shoulder part of the belts at both outer seats in row two, filled with cooled gas at lower pressure, deployed in frontal, side and rollover crashes and monitored by the same module and lamp as the front…",["Internal wire damage in the second-row seat harness at the belt connector (Ford programme 21B11)","Plug of the inflator under the left rear seat loose after folding or removing the seat","Fault in the belt inflator igniter"],["Airbag warning light on","Left rear inflatable belt may not deploy in a crash","Safety note: the belt holds a stored-gas or pyrotechnic inflator – battery off, wait time, work only at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00F4","B00F3","B0073","B0053"],""],B00F3:["Second Row Center Inflatable Seat Belt Deployment Control","B00F3 refers to an inflatable belt at the centre seat of the second row. No manufacturer documents the code, and the known systems leave this seat out: Ford's 2018 Explorer manual limits its inflatable belts to the outermost second-row positions, and Mercedes fits its beltbag to the outer rear belts (S-Class manual 2017); the E-Class manual of the same year lists the belt air bag as a frontal-impact device.",["Restraint module configured for a centre inflatable belt not present in the vehicle","Connector at the centre buckle inflator under the bench disconnected","Igniter of the centre belt inflator open or shorted"],["Airbag indicator remains on","Rear centre belt would not inflate in a crash","Safety note: pyrotechnic or stored-gas inflator – only work with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed, at a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00F2","B00F4","B0074","B0054"],""],B00F4:["Second Row Right Inflatable Seat Belt Deployment Control","B00F4 covers the inflatable belt on the outboard right seat of row two. The hardware exists in series cars, but the code is not documented by any maker. Ford's Explorer (2014–2016) logs belt faults as B141B and/or B141C; supplement 2 of programme 21B11 (June 2022) stresses checking those codes first and allows a separate labour time when both are present, then repositioning or replacing the seat harness pigtail.",["Worn or broken wires in the right second-row seat pigtail (Ford Explorer 2014–2016)","Inflator plug at the lower belt anchor or under the seat not latched","Inflator igniter faulty"],["Airbag lamp illuminated","Right rear inflatable belt not ready to deploy","Safety note: do not open or probe the belt or its inflator; battery off, wait time, and leave the job to a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00F2","B00F3","B0075","B0055"],""],B00F5:["Third Row Left Inflatable Seat Belt Deployment Control","B00F5 opens the third-row part of the inflatable-belt block with the left seat; B00F6 (centre) and B00F7 (right) follow. No manufacturer documents B00F5, and the known systems stop at row two: Ford's Explorer has its inflatable belts only at the second-row outer seats, even though it has a third row, and Mercedes offers the beltbag for rear belts of S- and E-Class (outer seats in the S-Class).",["Airbag module coded with a third-row inflatable belt that is not installed","Plug at the left third-row belt inflator disturbed when folding the seat","Defective igniter in the third-row belt inflator"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left third-row inflatable belt not available in a crash","Safety note: inflator with explosive igniter – disconnect the battery, wait, and have it handled by a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00F6","B00F7","B00F2","B0076","B0056"],""],B00F6:["Third Row Center Inflatable Seat Belt Deployment Control","B00F6 names the deployment circuit for an inflatable belt at the middle seat of row three. That seat is the least likely place for such a belt: the series systems on record sit at outboard rear seats, Ford's Explorer only in row two and Mercedes' beltbag on the outer rear belts.",["Airbag module coded for a centre third-row inflatable belt the vehicle does not have","Inflator plug of the centre belt loosened when the third-row seat was folded or removed","Igniter in the centre belt inflator out of its resistance window"],["Airbag warning lamp lit","Centre third-row inflatable belt would not inflate in a crash","Safety note: igniter-equipped part – battery off, observe waiting time, work only in a specialist workshop"],4,0,["B00F5","B00F7","B00F2"],""],B00F7:["Third Row Right Inflatable Seat Belt Deployment Control","B00F7 closes the inflatable-belt block with the right seat of row three. No manufacturer documents it. The nearest real case is one row further forward: on the 2014–2016 Ford Explorer, the dealer bulletin for programme 21B11 names B141C as the right and B141B as the left second-row harness code and has technicians re-route or repair the seat pigtail when either appears.",["Chafed wires in the right rear seat harness, as seen one row forward on the Explorer (B141C)","Restraint module variant coding expects a right third-row inflatable belt","Open or shorted igniter in the right third-row belt inflator"],["Airbag lamp stays on after start-up check","Right third-row inflatable belt not armed","Safety note: never probe the inflator circuit with a test lamp; disconnect battery, wait, leave it to a specialist"],4,0,["B00F5","B00F6","B00F4"],""],B0100:["Sensor Cleaning Air Blower Actuator A","B0100 is the general fault for air blower A in a sensor cleaning system, i.e. the fan or motor unit itself rather than its wiring or relay (those are B0102 and B0104). Such blowers keep camera lenses and lidar windows clear of droplets, dust and insects. Ford's patent US12115948B2 mounts a blower on the sensor bracket;",["Blower A motor worn, seized or with an open winding","Impeller blocked by ice, leaves or debris in the intake duct","Corroded or loose plug directly at blower A"],["Sensor blocked or cleaning fault message","Driver assistance or automated driving functions limited or switched off","No airflow audible or felt at the sensor outlets"],2,2,["B0101","B0102","B0104","U022E"],""],B0101:["Sensor Cleaning Air Blower Actuator B","B0101 reports a fault of the second cleaning air source, blower B. A second unit makes sense where sensors are spread over the body: a roof pod and a bumper or corner sensor need separate air supplies. Not every design uses a fan;",["Blower or compressor B worn out or drawing too much current","Leaking or split air hose so blower B cannot build pressure","Water or salt ingress into blower B at an exposed mounting point"],["Cleaning fault shown for the sensor group served by blower B","Water droplets or dust remain on lidar or camera window","Assistance functions reduced when the affected sensor goes blind"],2,2,["B0100","B0103","B0105","U022F"],""],B0102:["Sensor Cleaning Air Blower Actuator A Control","B0102 narrows the blower A problem down to its control path: the controlling module sees a wrong voltage or current on the line that commands blower A, typically an open circuit, a short to ground or a short to supply. In Ford's lidar cleaning patent US10569746B2 a computer opens airflow from a blower or compressor by driving an electric solenoid valve and may modulate it;",["Broken control wire or pin between module and blower A","Control line of blower A shorted to ground or to battery voltage","Output stage in the cleaning or maintenance module defective"],["Blower A never starts although cleaning is requested","Blower A runs constantly when the line is shorted to supply","Sensor blocked message and limited assistance features"],2,2,["B0100","B0103","B0104"],""],B0103:["Sensor Cleaning Air Blower Actuator B Control","With B0103 the module flags the command line of blower B, not the blower: open wire, short or a driver that cannot switch. In compressed-air layouts the controlled element is often a valve bank. Uber's patent lets the controller fire individual solenoids for set times, for example one valve for three seconds, so a single faulty drive line leaves only part of the lidar or one camera without air.",["Damaged harness or connector in the control path of blower B","Solenoid coil of the B air valve open or shorted, where air is valve-switched","Failed driver for blower B in the controlling module"],["Lens streaks or droplets remain after a wash cycle","Cleaning warning for sensors on the B circuit only","Assistance features temporarily unavailable in rain or dust"],2,2,["B0101","B0102","B0105"],""],B0104:["Sensor Cleaning Air Blower Actuator A Control Relay","B0104 points at the relay that switches power to blower A. A fan motor draws more current than a module output can carry, so a relay is a natural choice: the module energises the coil (terminals 85/86 in HELLA's scheme) and the contact (30/87) feeds the motor.",["Burnt or welded contacts in the blower A relay","Relay coil open or its control wire interrupted","Blown fuse or loose socket on the relay supply side"],["Blower A dead, or running without command if contacts are welded","No relay click when cleaning is requested","Sensor cleaning warning with possible loss of assistance functions"],1,2,["B0100","B0102","B0105"],""],B0105:["Sensor Cleaning Air Blower Actuator B Control Relay","B0105 is the relay fault on the B side of the sensor-cleaning air supply. If B is a compressor rather than a small fan, as in Uber's patent where a compressor charges an accumulator and recharges once pressure drops to roughly 130–140 psi, the relay carries a sizable inrush current, and pitted contacts become the usual weak point.",["Contacts of relay B pitted by high motor or compressor inrush current","Relay B coil or its suppression diode failed","Corroded relay socket or wrong relay type fitted"],["Blower or compressor B does not start, or will not switch off","Droplets stay on sensor windows in rain","Assistance functions drop out when a sensor is reported blocked"],1,2,["B0101","B0103","B0104"],""],B0106:["LIDAR Washer Actuator A","B0106 opens a row of four lidar washer actuators (A to D). The actuator is whatever delivers fluid to a lidar window: a washer pump or an electromagnetic valve. In Ford's patent US10569746B2 a computer triggers a wash pump for the spray nozzle of a roof lidar, after an air nozzle has run for about 5 s and the window is still more than about 20 % opaque; a wiper follows only if needed.",["Washer pump or valve A for the lidar nozzle seized or electrically open","Wiring or plug fault at actuator A","Frozen washer fluid blocking pump A"],["No spray reaches lidar A during a cleaning cycle","Lidar blocked message and reduced automated driving availability"],2,2,["B0107","B0108","B0109","B010A","B012F"],""],B0107:["LIDAR Washer Actuator B","B0107 is the second lidar washer actuator. Why a car would need several becomes clear in Uber's 2016 patent: its roof lidar is washed by three separate nozzle units, each with its own pump and check valve, fed from one reservoir, and the controller normally sprays fluid first and then dries with air. A fault on one pump leaves only that segment of the window dirty.",["Washer pump B worn or its motor open","Check valve or line to nozzle B blocked, pump runs against closed path","Chafed wiring to actuator B"],["One section of the lidar window stays dirty after washing","Repeated cleaning requests and lidar degraded warning"],2,2,["B0106","B0108","B0109","B011C"],""],B0108:["LIDAR Washer Actuator C","B0108 covers lidar washer actuator C. Robotaxis with several lidars, for example on roof and corners, are where a third circuit would fit. Valeo lists a heated telescopic lidar nozzle, a 2021 PACE award finalist, and says it supplies cleaning systems with ECU and software for private cars and robotaxis; a telescopic nozzle adds a moving part that can stick in frost.",["Telescopic nozzle C stuck by ice or dirt, actuator overloaded","Distribution valve position C not switching","Nozzle heater or shared connector on circuit C faulty"],["Lidar C not cleaned, especially in frost or snow","Automated driving refuses to engage or hands back control"],2,2,["B0106","B0107","B0109","B012F"],""],B0109:["LIDAR Washer Actuator D","B0109 ends the lidar washer group with actuator D; the next codes, B010A onward, move on to camera washers. Four lidar circuits match fleets built for driverless service: Kautex fits two complete Allegro cleaning and clearing systems to every Zoox robotaxi, combining water and air for cameras and lidars.",["Pump or valve D for the fourth lidar nozzle defective","Hose to lidar D kinked or pulled off, so the actuator runs dry or overloaded","Open or shorted wire to actuator D"],["One lidar remains dirty while the other sensors are cleaned","Vehicle limits or ends automated driving"],2,2,["B0106","B0107","B0108","B010A","U022E"],""],B010A:["Camera Washer Actuator A","B010A opens a row of eighteen camera washer actuators, lettered A to S with I left out. The actuator is the electrically driven part that sends fluid to one camera lens: a pump of its own or a valve on a shared line.",["Valve coil or pump motor of actuator A open or shorted","Corroded or loose plug at actuator A, which sits in the splash zone near the camera","Driver stage in the controlling module defective"],["The camera assigned to actuator A is no longer washed, neither on request nor automatically","Camera view stays dirty in rain, mud or road salt; a camera blocked message may appear"],2,0,["B010B","B010C","B0106","B011C"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ A"],B010B:["Camera Washer Actuator B","B010B covers actuator B. A common way to reach a reversing camera is a branch off the rear-window washer line with an electric switching valve. Asmo's application US20120266926A1 (2011) describes a solenoid spool valve: unpowered it feeds the rear-screen nozzle, energised it diverts fluid to the camera nozzle.",["Coil of the rear-window/camera switching valve open or shorted","Broken wire in the tailgate or boot-lid harness passage to the valve","Reverse-gear signal that enables the camera wash not reaching the module"],["In reverse the washer switch no longer sprays the reversing camera","Rear window may be washed instead of the camera, or neither"],2,0,["B010A","B010C","B010D"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ B"],B010C:["Camera Washer Actuator C","B010C names actuator C. Front cameras sit in the grille and get a jet of their own. Ford's TSB 20-2267 (2020) covers 2015–2020 F-150 (not Raptor), 2017–2020 Super Duty and 2018–2020 Expedition fitted with a front camera wash: the jet dripped fluid when idle because of its internal rubber seal, and the cure is a new jet, with the grille removed and the 360-degree camera aligned afterwards.",["Damaged wiring or plug at the front end, exposed to stone chips, water and salt","Pump or valve C seized or electrically defective","Plug left disconnected after grille or bumper work"],["Front camera lens is not sprayed when the wash is requested","Front or 360-degree camera image stays dirty in winter or after off-road driving"],2,0,["B010B","B010D","B010A"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ C"],B010D:["Camera Washer Actuator D","B010D covers actuator D. Audi's TSB 2059228/2 (2022) for the 2019–2022 e-tron and 2020–2022 e-tron Sportback shows what a missing check valve does to a rear camera wash: the line empties while driving or when the tailgate opens, the system stops after four activations to save fluid, and four tries are not enough to refill and pressurise it, so the lens stays dirty until the ignition (terminal 15) is switched off and…",["Pump or valve D open, shorted or drawing abnormal current","Wire break where the harness flexes into the tailgate","Pump damaged by repeatedly running dry on an empty line"],["Camera wash request must be repeated several times before fluid arrives, or nothing arrives","Reversing camera stays smeared after the wash function has been used"],2,0,["B010C","B010E","B0119"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ D"],B010E:["Camera Washer Actuator E","B010E names actuator E, which may be a dedicated pump rather than a valve. Audi's TSB 2073568/1 (2024) for e-tron, e-tron S and Q8/SQ8 e-tron models reports rear camera washer pressure too low to clean the lens: the mono pump could not build enough pressure, and production moved to a dual pump (1K6 955 651) whose spare outlet is plugged.",["Camera washer pump motor E worn, seized or open","Low supply voltage or poor ground at the pump","Clogged inlet filter making the pump labour and draw high current"],["Camera nozzle only dribbles; the spray does not reach across the lens","Pump hum without spray, or no pump sound at all when the wash is requested"],2,0,["B010D","B010F","B011C"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ E"],B010F:["Camera Washer Actuator F","B010F covers actuator F. On 2021 Chevrolet Tahoe and Suburban and GMC Yukon with the rear camera mirror (RPO DRZ), GM service update N202311260 found the hose feeding the rear camera nozzle kinked behind the tailgate trim in about 630 vehicles; technicians test the wash, shorten the hose to 127 mm at most and slide an 85 mm split sleeve over it.",["Open or shorted circuit to valve or pump F","Wiring pinched or unplugged during tailgate trim removal","Actuator F itself defective"],["Camera mirror or reversing image stays dirty because the rear camera wash does not work","Rearview image itself is still shown when reversing"],2,0,["B010E","B0110","B010B"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ F"],B0110:["Camera Washer Actuator G","B0110 names actuator G. Not every washed camera sees visible light. Bentley's product information 2051045 (2023) concerns the infrared night-vision camera in the front bumper of Bentayga, Continental GT/GTC and Flying Spur: fluid dripping from its washer jet is cured by a new non-return valve, and the camera needs recalibrating only if it is replaced itself.",["Valve or pump G for the camera jet electrically open or shorted","Harness damage in the lower bumper area after a parking knock or repair","Output stage of the controlling module defective"],["Night-vision or front camera image stays smeared; the camera jet does not spray","Assistance functions relying on that camera may report limited availability"],2,0,["B010F","B0111","B010C"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ G"],B0111:["Camera Washer Actuator H","B0111 is the J2012 code for camera washer actuator H, but the number has an older second life. Toyota's bulletin T-SB-0069-12 (revision 2, 2014) for the 2004–2009 Sienna lists B0111 together with B0116 as an open side-airbag squib circuit with the SRS lamp lit, repaired in the floor harness. On that van the code has nothing to do with washing, and a scan tool showing the generic title would mislead.",["Pump or valve H open, shorted or seized","Water ingress or corrosion in the plug of actuator H"],["Camera served by actuator H is not washed","No washer fluid leaves the nozzle served by actuator H when the wash is requested"],2,0,["B0110","B0112","B0116"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ H"],B0112:["Camera Washer Actuator J","B0112 covers actuator J; the letter I is skipped in this row, so J is the ninth. Large systems wash many cameras from one fluid network. Stellantis TSB 23-028-23 (2023) for the 2022 Grand Wagoneer and Wagoneer built up to 28 February 2022 names rear backup camera washer, surround-view cameras, night vision and the digital rearview mirror as the equipment involved;",["Valve or pump J electrically open or shorted","Washer fluid from a loose coupling running into the actuator plug and corroding it","Chafed wire on the route to actuator J"],["One camera of a multi-camera system is not sprayed while others are","Damp trim or puddles of washer fluid inside the vehicle if a coupling has also come loose"],2,0,["B0111","B0113","B0115"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ J"],B0113:["Camera Washer Actuator K","B0113 names actuator K. Even a working actuator is useless if the jet misses the lens. Stellantis TSB 23-049-22 Rev. A for 2022–2023 Jeep Grand Cherokee (WL) built between 13 April and 15 September 2022 found the liftgate nozzle of the digital rearview mirror camera pointing the wrong way;",["Open or short in the circuit of valve or pump K","Wire fatigue in the liftgate hinge area","Plug not reconnected after the camera or nozzle was removed"],["Camera wash does not run for the camera served by actuator K","Digital mirror or reversing picture stays dirty after the wash is requested"],2,0,["B0112","B0114","B010B"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ K"],B0114:["Camera Washer Actuator L","B0114 covers actuator L. Stellantis STAR case S2123000051 (2021, Jeep Grand Cherokee) describes a front camera washer pump that stopped spraying when the reservoir ran low although the cluster showed no low-fluid warning; a new pump, reservoir or level sensor did not help, and engineering was still investigating.",["Pump or actuator L damaged after running with a nearly empty reservoir","Open or shorted wiring to actuator L","Level sensor not warning in time, so the actuator runs without fluid"],["Camera wash stops working while the reservoir is low, without a low-fluid warning","Front camera view remains dirty after a wash request"],2,0,["B0113","B0115","B011C"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ L"],B0115:["Camera Washer Actuator M","B0115 names actuator M. Where several cameras share one pump, the actuator is often a distribution valve. Solero's SCV43 is a 4/3-way valve switched by voltage, with one inlet and three independently switched outlets, so a single pump can serve up to three nozzles and fewer DC pumps are needed in the reservoir.",["Coil for outlet M in a shared valve block open or shorted","Valve M stuck by deposits or frozen fluid, drawing abnormal current","Wiring or plug fault on the line to valve M"],["One camera stays unwashed while other cameras on the same pump are sprayed","Camera blocked message for that camera in bad weather"],2,0,["B0114","B0116","B0112"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ M"],B0116:["Camera Washer Actuator N","B0116 covers actuator N. Like B0111 it also turns up on the 2004–2009 Toyota Sienna, where bulletin T-SB-0069-12 uses it for an open side-airbag squib circuit, not a washer. In the generic sense, cold is a typical burden for camera washers.",["Washer fluid without enough antifreeze frozen in pump or valve N","Actuator N electrically open or shorted"],["Camera wash fails mainly in frost and recovers after the car has warmed up","Ice or salt film stays on the lens of the camera served by actuator N"],2,0,["B0115","B0117","B0111"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ N"],B0117:["Camera Washer Actuator O","B0117 names actuator O; unlike I, the letter O is used in this row. Not every silent washer is faulty. Continental's patent US11673532B2 (granted 2023, now held by Aumovio) lets the controller hold back the camera valves on purpose: in an off-road mode only selected cameras are washed, and with four-wheel drive engaged below about 20 km/h all valves stay shut so mud does not use up the fluid;",["Valve or pump O open, shorted or seized","Wiring to a low-mounted camera actuator damaged by mud, water or off-road use","Module software or configuration fault in actuator O control; update per maker"],["Camera stays unwashed also in normal road mode, not only when washing is intentionally paused","Camera blocked message in mud or rain"],2,0,["B0116","B0118","B010A"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ O"],B0118:["Camera Washer Actuator P","B0118 covers actuator P. Equipment can disappear in the middle of a model year. Ford's SSM 51564 notes that the 2023 Lincoln Aviator and the 2022–2023 Explorer and Police Interceptor Utility built from mid-July or August 2022 lost washing of the rear parking camera; the jet may still be fitted without a hose, which is normal and needs no repair.",["Module coded for a camera washer actuator the vehicle is not built with","Actuator P or its feed open circuit","Replacement module fitted with the wrong variant data"],["Fault stored although the camera has no working wash, or only a dummy jet without a hose","Camera image and parking aid otherwise work normally"],2,0,["B0117","B0119","B010B"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ P"],B0119:["Camera Washer Actuator Q","B0119 names actuator Q. Land Rover's SSM76076 (2023) for the Defender (L663) from model year 2020 traces dripping headlamp washer jets and a dripping rear camera washer jet to a one-way valve in the feed pipe that no longer seals; the dealer tool runs a guided leak test and may call for a new rear camera washer hose with the valve. Headlamp and camera washing thus often share fluid and parts.",["Pump or valve Q electrically open or shorted","Fluid dripping from a leaking jet or valve corroding the nearby actuator plug","Chafed wire between module and actuator Q"],["Camera wash for the camera served by actuator Q does not respond","Washer fluid level drops faster than usual if a valve is also leaking"],2,0,["B0118","B011A","B010D"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ Q"],B011A:["Camera Washer Actuator R","B011A covers actuator R. Some camera cleaners use air as well as fluid, so the actuator may be a blower as much as a pump. Thunder Power's patent US9539988B2 places a water nozzle and an air nozzle at a reversing camera: air blasts first, then unheated fluid, and below about 0 °C heated fluid, while an infrared drop sensor behind the lens decides when cleaning is needed.",["Pump, valve or air blower R electrically open or shorted","Heater element in the camera wash circuit defective, affecting cold-weather operation","Corroded plug at actuator R"],["Camera served by actuator R is neither blown nor sprayed clean","Drops or mud remain on the lens; assistance functions may warn of a blocked camera"],2,0,["B0119","B011B","B0100"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ R"],B011B:["Camera Washer Actuator S","B011B closes the row with actuator S. Electrically, each actuator in the row is a coil or motor switched by a module or a relay. HELLA's relay guide explains the switching side: a control coil on terminals 85 and 86 pulls in the armature and moves the contact from 87a over to 87, and some types carry a resistor or diode across the coil to tame the spike at switch-off.",["Coil or motor of actuator S open or shorted","Relay feeding actuator S sticking or with a burnt contact","Blown fuse or broken supply wire to the relay or actuator"],["Camera wash for the camera served by actuator S does nothing","Wash may run continuously or not stop if a relay contact has welded"],2,0,["B011A","B0119","B010A"],"מפעיל מתז מצלמה‏ S"],B011C:["Fluid Reservoir Level Sensor A","B011C is the first of six fluid reservoir level sensors, A to F. J2012 does not say which reservoir each letter belongs to; the neighbouring codes deal with washing windows, cameras and other sensors, so washer tanks are the obvious candidates. The classic design pairs a magnet-bearing float with a reed switch: falling fluid lowers the float, and the contact flips.",["Float jammed, rotated out of its guide or soaked with fluid","Reed contact inside the sensor broken or welded","Leaking grommet letting fluid reach the plug, corroded terminals"],["Low-fluid warning stays on although the reservoir is full","No warning at all when the reservoir runs empty"],2,0,["B011D","B011E","B011F","B0120","B0121"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל נוזל‏ A"],B011D:["Fluid Reservoir Level Sensor B","B011D concerns level sensor B. Not every washer tank relies on a float. Volkswagen's bulletin 2037322 (2015) describes its washer level sensor G33 as a part whose reading depends on the fluid itself: the wrong mix or additives coat the sensor, cut its sensitivity and leave the lamp lit with a full tank; the remedy is draining, cleaning the sensor and refilling with approved fluid.",["Deposits from unsuitable washer fluid or additives on the sensing surface","Sensor electronics or electrodes defective","Open or short in the sensor wiring"],["Warning lamp lit with a full reservoir, often after a change of washer fluid","Level warning appears late or not at all"],2,0,["B011C","B011E","B011F","B0120","B0121"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל נוזל‏ B"],B011E:["Fluid Reservoir Level Sensor C","B011E covers level sensor C. Vehicles that steer by camera and lidar need their own cleaning supply, and there the level reading becomes an operating condition. Uber's application US20180015907A1 shows a sensor-cleaning reservoir with a dedicated liquid level sensor reporting to the vehicle computer; below a threshold the computer lights an indicator or tells a remote operator to refill.",["Level sensor C defective or signal implausible","Damaged wiring or connector between sensor and computing module","Dirt or ice in the reservoir disturbing the measurement"],["Refill request or cleaning-system warning without obvious reason","Sensor cleaning may be withheld, and assistance functions may restrict themselves when sensors get dirty"],2,0,["B011C","B011D","B011F","B0120","B0121","B012F"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל נוזל‏ C"],B011F:["Fluid Reservoir Level Sensor D","B011F reports level sensor D. A recurring weakness of float switches in washer bottles is motion: fluid slopping around in corners or under braking lifts and drops the float and can set it spinning. Continental's patent US9003878B2 answers with a float guided in an angled carrier, ribs that stop it turning and an optional slosh guard, so one design suits side or bottom mounting.",["Loose or corroded pins at an intermediate harness connector","Float moving freely with sloshing fluid, guide or slosh guard broken","Level sensor D itself defective"],["Level warning switching on and off while driving, especially in bends","False low-level message with a full reservoir"],2,0,["B011C","B011D","B011E","B0120","B0121"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל נוזל‏ D"],B0120:["Fluid Reservoir Level Sensor E","B0120 relates to level sensor E. Ford's application US20190265715A1 describes a container for sensor cleaning whose level sensor measures conductance at a fixed height: air gives a resistance above roughly 1000 ohms, the slightly conductive fluid one below it.",["Electrodes fouled or fluid with unsuitable conductivity (e.g. plain distilled water)","Open or short in the sensor circuit","Leaking reservoir or hose making the level drop unexpectedly"],["Refill warning too early, too late or constantly on","Cleaning of exterior sensors may be restricted"],2,0,["B011C","B011D","B011E","B011F","B0121"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל נוזל‏ E"],B0121:["Fluid Reservoir Level Sensor F","B0121 closes the row with level sensor F. Small local reservoirs are one reason a vehicle might carry six level sensors: Ford's application DE102018109892A1 describes a camera washer with its own container close to the lens, fitted with a buoyant level sensor that signals when the fluid has fallen to a set low point and the container needs topping up. How the result reaches the driver is a separate design question;",["Float of sensor F stuck by deposits or ice","Wiring to the small reservoir chafed or connector corroded","Level sensor F defective"],["Missing or permanent refill message for the affected reservoir","Washer served by this reservoir runs dry without warning"],2,0,["B011C","B011D","B011E","B011F","B0120"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל נוזל‏ F"],B0122:["Pedestrian Alert Speaker A","B0122 flags pedestrian alert speaker A. Hybrid and electric vehicles are almost silent at walking pace, so they have to make an artificial sound. In the US, FMVSS 141 covers such vehicles up to 4,536 kg GVWR and sets minimum sound levels when stationary with propulsion active, in reverse and up to 30 km/h.",["Speaker A failed from water, salt or stone impact at the front end","Open or short in the speaker wiring, often after bumper repairs","Output stage of the sound generator module or its fuse faulty"],["No artificial driving sound at low speed from the affected side","Warning message about the pedestrian alert system in the cluster, depending on make","Vehicle no longer meets the legal minimum sound; repair promptly"],2,0,["B0123"],""],B0123:["Pedestrian Alert Speaker B","B0123 is the same check for pedestrian alert speaker B, which implies a second sounder. Ford's special service message 48451 for 2020 hybrids and plug-ins describes speakers at the front and the rear that sound in forward and reverse between 0 and 30 km/h.",["Speaker B defective, for example from moisture in the rear bumper or wheel arch area","Loose or corroded connector at speaker B or a rattling internal connector at the module","Fault in the sound generator module or its software"],["Artificial sound missing at the front or rear, e.g. only audible when moving off forwards","Possible warning message about the pedestrian alert system","Legally required warning sound incomplete; have it repaired soon"],2,0,["B0122"],""],B0124:["Night Vision Camera","B0124 points at the night vision camera, usually a far-infrared thermal sensor behind the grille or in the bumper; Teledyne FLIR says it has supplied more than a million automotive thermal sensors. Its exposed position causes most faults.",["Water ingress through a stone-chipped or cracked camera window","Loose or corroded LVDS video connector between camera and control module","Camera replaced but not learned or calibrated"],["Night vision image missing, distorted or pixelated","Message such as night vision unavailable, service required"],2,0,["B0125"],""],B0125:["Night Vision Control Module","B0125 concerns the night vision control module, which processes the camera image and passes it to the display. Stellantis uses this code: on the 2023 Jeep Grand Cherokee the cluster stores B0125-02, Night Vision Control Module general signal failure, alongside U02BD (lost communication) in the BCM. Case S2208000163 blames misaligned or not fully seated terminals at connector D3944A of the processing module;",["Misaligned, bent or not fully seated terminals at the module connector","Video link (LVDS) to the cluster loose or damaged","Camera delivers no usable image, e.g. cracked lens","Control module internally defective"],["Night vision unavailable message in the cluster","No, frozen or pixelated night vision image"],2,0,["B0124"],""],B0126:["Driver Monitoring Camera","B0126 belongs to the driver monitoring camera, an infrared camera aimed at the driver that tracks gaze and head position for hands-free and attention functions. GM uses the code: preliminary information PIC6556 (versions B to H, 2024–2025) for Super Cruise models from Cadillac Lyriq to Silverado EV lists B0126 symptom 82, stored by the module that processes camera images and often paired with B1DD0;",["Driver monitoring camera internally defective","LVDS cable to the image processing module damaged or poorly connected","Software fault, or camera view blocked by objects or mounting problems"],["Hands-free assistance such as Super Cruise unavailable or disengaging","Driver attention or distraction warning inactive, failure message shown"],2,0,["B0124","B0125"],"מצלמת ניטור נהג"],B0127:['DC/AC Converter A High Voltage Power Outlet "A" Circuit/Open',"B0127 reports an open circuit to power outlet A of DC/AC converter A, one of the household-voltage sockets the converter supplies. Ford's patent US11043801B2, behind Pro Power Onboard, gives every socket its own conductor, on/off switch and ground-fault interrupter, fed by an inverter that draws on the traction battery, the motor-generator or both;",["Wire or terminal in the feed to outlet A broken or pushed out","Socket insert or its built-in protection defective","Output switch or relay for outlet A inside the converter faulty"],["Outlet A supplies no power while other outlets may still work","Message that onboard power or the outlet is unavailable","Outlet circuits carry 120/240 V AC from a high-voltage source; work only with the system de-energised"],4,0,["B0128","B0129","B012A","B012B","B012C","P2DA8"],"יציאת כוח מתח גבוה ממיר DC/AC‏ A A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],B0128:['DC/AC Converter A High Voltage Power Outlet "B" Circuit/Open',"B0128 is the open-circuit fault for outlet B. Such a fault has to be told apart from a tripped protective device. In Ford's patent US11043801B2 each socket has a ground-fault interrupter whose breaker opens on a current imbalance and normally needs a manual reset; Ford adds an actuator so it can also be reset from a distance, plus test switches for the interrupters.",["Feed to outlet B interrupted at a connector or in the harness","Ground-fault interrupter of outlet B defective or its reset actuator stuck","Moisture or dirt in socket B"],["Socket B dead, ground-fault or outlet message on the screen","Reset does not restore power to socket B","Outlet circuits carry 120/240 V AC from a high-voltage source; work only with the system de-energised"],4,0,["B0127","B0129","B012A","B012B","B012C"],"יציאת כוח מתח גבוה ממיר DC/AC‏ A B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],B0129:['DC/AC Converter A High Voltage Power Outlet "C" Circuit/Open',"B0129 covers outlet C. Apart from wiring faults, the converter also cuts sockets on purpose when the load is too high. Ford's patent US11043801B2 gives limits of 20 A for the 120 V sockets and 30 A for the 240 V socket, and when total power exceeds the ceiling it de-energises sockets by priority, the lowest first.",["Terminal at outlet C overheated or burnt from heavy loads, contact lost","Harness to outlet C open","Switching element for outlet C inside the converter defective"],["Socket C stays dead even with no load connected","Outlet message that cannot be cleared by unplugging and resetting","Outlet circuits carry 120/240 V AC from a high-voltage source; work only with the system de-energised"],4,0,["B0127","B0128","B012A","B012B","B012C"],"יציאת כוח מתח גבוה ממיר DC/AC‏ A C — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],B012A:['DC/AC Converter A High Voltage Power Outlet "D" Circuit/Open',"B012A concerns outlet D. Sockets in a pickup bed live in a harsher place than those in the cab: dust, rain, washing and cords left plugged in. Ford's customer satisfaction program 21B52 shows how tightly bed outlets are tied into the vehicle: on certain 2021 F-150 Raptor trucks with Pro Power Onboard, a bed outlet cover standing open more than about 17 degrees kept the truck from shifting out of Park until the PCM…",["Water or corrosion in socket D or its connector, typical for exterior or bed outlets","Harness to outlet D chafed or crushed in the body or bed","Socket insert mechanically damaged"],["Socket D without power, other sockets may work","Message that onboard power or an outlet is unavailable","Outlet circuits carry 120/240 V AC from a high-voltage source; work only with the system de-energised"],4,0,["B0127","B0128","B0129","B012B","B012C"],"יציאת כוח מתח גבוה ממיר DC/AC‏ A D — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],B012B:['DC/AC Converter A High Voltage Power Outlet "E" Circuit/Open',"B012B is the last outlet circuit code, for outlet E. Many trucks combine bed sockets with one in the cabin. Ford's SSM 49562 for the 2021 F-150 with the 7.2 kW system notes that a message about a tripped bed-panel breaker could really come from the breaker above the 120 V outlet in the instrument panel, or from that outlet's connector not being fully plugged in; an over-the-air update corrected the wording.",["Connector at outlet E not fully engaged, e.g. after dash work","Circuit breaker of outlet E tripped or defective","Wiring between converter and outlet E open"],["Socket E dead, possibly with a misleading breaker message for another outlet","Outlet circuits carry 120/240 V AC from a high-voltage source; work only with the system de-energised"],4,0,["B0127","B0128","B0129","B012A","B012C"],"יציאת כוח מתח גבוה ממיר DC/AC‏ A E — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],B012C:['DC/AC Converter A High Voltage Power Outlet Control Module "A"',"B012C names power outlet control module A of converter A without a fault type, so the module itself is under suspicion rather than one socket. Ford calls its unit DCACA; on the F-150 with the 2.0 kW system it sits in the cab under the left rear seat.",["Outdated or corrupted module software; reprogramming per maker bulletin","Power, ground or network connection of module A faulty","Module A internally defective, e.g. cooling fan or power stage"],["Onboard power unavailable or service message in the centre display","Unusual fan noise from the module's location","Module handles 120/240 V AC from a high-voltage source; work only with the system de-energised"],4,0,["B012D","B012E","B0127","P2DA8","P2EA9"],"מודול בקרת יציאת כוח מתח גבוה ממיר DC/AC‏ A A"],B012D:['DC/AC Converter A High Voltage Power Outlet Control Module "B"',"B012D addresses outlet control module B. A converter for household sockets interacts with the rest of the vehicle both electrically and by radio. Ford's TSB 23-2218 for 2021–2023 F-150 with the DCACA inverter shows radio-frequency interference from the inverter upsetting the tyre pressure system, so the BCM stores B124D and lights the TPMS lamp;",["Supply voltage outside the permitted window, weak 12 V battery or poor ground","Module B overheating, blocked air path or cooling fan failed","Module B internally defective or emitting interference"],["Outlets switch off or are unavailable","Side effects on radio-based systems such as tyre pressure monitoring","Module handles 120/240 V AC from a high-voltage source; work only with the system de-energised"],4,0,["B012C","B012E","P2EA7","P2EA8","P2EA9"],"מודול בקרת יציאת כוח מתח גבוה ממיר DC/AC‏ A B"],B012E:['DC/AC Converter A High Voltage Power Outlet Control Module "C"',"B012E concerns outlet control module C. GM's name for the part is accessory AC and DC power control module: in program N222385490, 2023 Silverado and Sierra 1500 built from September 2022 without a working inverter, because of the chip shortage, received this module, a fuse and BCM reprogramming, with separate inverters for 110 V (RPO KI4) and 230 V (KI5).",["Module C or BCM not configured or programmed after installation or replacement","Fuse, supply or ground of module C faulty","Module C internally defective"],["Power outlets in cab and bed inoperative","Outlet functions missing from the display menu","Module handles 120/240 V AC from a high-voltage source; work only with the system de-energised"],4,0,["B012C","B012D","B0127"],"מודול בקרת יציאת כוח מתח גבוה ממיר DC/AC‏ A C"],B012F:["A/V Sensor Washer Fluid A Control Circuit","B012F reports a fault in the control circuit for A/V sensor washer fluid A, the first of six such circuits, with B0130 to B0134 following. A/V most likely stands for autonomous vehicle; the circuit drives the pump or valve that delivers fluid to one sensor.",["Pump motor or valve coil for fluid circuit A open or shorted","Damaged wiring or corroded connector in the control circuit","Driver stage in the controlling module defective"],["Sensor A is no longer washed, camera or lidar view stays dirty","Assistance or automated driving functions report sensor blocked or become unavailable"],2,0,["B0130","B0131","B0132","B0133","B0134","B011E"],"נוזל מתז חיישן‏ A/V‏ A — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],B0130:["A/V Sensor Washer Fluid B Control Circuit","B0130 reports a fault where the module switches A/V sensor washer fluid B, the second of six channels running from B012F (A) to B0134 (F). A/V almost certainly stands for autonomous vehicle. Uber's cleaning layout (US20180015907A1) shows what such a channel switches: a compressor charges an air accumulator, one reservoir with a level sensor holds the fluid, and several pumps feed the cleaning heads, each started…",["Pump motor or valve coil on fluid channel B open or shorted","Corroded or loose connector at the pump, exposed to washer spray and road salt","Output stage for channel B in the controlling module failed"],["The camera or lidar on channel B stays dirty while the others are cleaned","Driver assistance or automated driving reports a blocked sensor or is withdrawn"],2,0,["B012F","B0131","B0132","B0133","B0134"],"נוזל מתז חיישן‏ A/V‏ B — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],B0131:["A/V Sensor Washer Fluid C Control Circuit","B0131 points to the circuit that switches A/V sensor washer fluid C, the third channel of the B012F to B0134 series for autonomous vehicle sensors. Ford's patent US10569746B2 describes a rotating sensor cover: the computer first tries a contactless cleaner with fluid or air and only brings in a wiper when the window's measured opacity stays above a limit.",["Pump or solenoid valve of channel C with open or shorted winding","Harness to the sensor cleaning unit chafed or pinched at a bracket","Controlling module output for channel C defective"],["Washing of sensor C stops; dirt, salt or insects stay on its window","A wiper or air jet, if fitted, has to do the cleaning alone"],2,0,["B012F","B0130","B0132","B0133","B0134"],"נוזל מתז חיישן‏ A/V‏ C — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],B0132:["A/V Sensor Washer Fluid D Control Circuit","B0132 concerns washer fluid channel D of a self-driving vehicle's sensor cleaning, the fourth in the series that starts at B012F. In Uber's patent US10173646B1 the vehicle computer judges how dirty each sensor is and then works out a cleaning order, so the cleaning units fire one after another instead of all at once; a dead channel removes one sensor from that rotation.",["Open circuit in the channel D pump or valve, often a burnt-out winding","Supply or control lead of channel D shorted to ground or battery voltage","Pump blocked by frozen or contaminated fluid, drawing excess current"],["Sensor D is skipped in the cleaning sequence and stays dirty","Automated driving may limit itself or ask the driver to take over"],2,0,["B012F","B0130","B0131","B0133","B0134"],"נוזל מתז חיישן‏ A/V‏ D — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],B0133:["A/V Sensor Washer Fluid E Control Circuit","B0133 covers the control circuit of A/V sensor washer fluid E, the fifth channel after B012F to B0132. Autonomous vehicles carry many cameras and lidar units, so cleaning is split into several separately switched fluid paths. Uber's patent US10220817B2 shows a sensor platform whose grooves and raised rim carry fluid and air to the sensor heads.",["Pump or valve of channel E defective, coil open or shorted","Water ingress or corrosion in the connector of channel E","Output for channel E in the cleaning control module damaged"],["The sensor on channel E keeps a film of dirt or dried spray","Message that a sensor is blocked or an assistance function is unavailable"],2,0,["B012F","B0130","B0131","B0132","B0134"],"נוזל מתז חיישן‏ A/V‏ E — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],B0134:["A/V Sensor Washer Fluid F Control Circuit","B0134 is the last of the six A/V sensor washer fluid circuits (B012F for A up to B0134 for F) and covers channel F. The module drives a pump or valve on this channel and reports the code when it finds an open or shorted output. Ford's US10569746B2 lets the computer decide from the measured opacity of a sensor window whether spraying is enough or a wiper must follow.",["Winding of the channel F pump or valve open or shorted","Wiring of channel F damaged, for example after bodywork near the sensor mount","Driver stage for channel F in the module failed"],["Sensor F no longer gets washer fluid; only air or a wiper, if present, still works","Assistance functions that rely on sensor F report reduced availability"],2,0,["B012F","B0130","B0131","B0132","B0133"],"נוזל מתז חיישן‏ A/V‏ F — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],B0140:["Passenger Seatbelt Tension Sensor Circuit","Neither the J2012 code lists available here nor any carmaker's public material contains B0140; its wording repeats B0061, the J2012 code for the front passenger belt tension sensor, and resembles B0182. The part itself is well described. In Delphi's design (US6554318B2) the webbing runs through a slider that moves against springs, while a Hall element between two magnets reads the travel.",["Loose or corroded plug at the passenger belt tension sensor","Sensor signal out of range, for example from a jammed slider","Sensor lead trapped under the seat or at the sill panel"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag status indicator may show an unexpected state","Safety note: the sensor sits near pretensioner and side airbag plugs; unplug only with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0061","B0182","B0060"],""],B0150:["HVAC Mode Door Range/Performance","No publicly available J2012 code list includes B0150, and no carmaker publishes it with this meaning. The mode door decides whether air leaves at the face vents, the footwell or the windscreen. A range/performance fault means the door does not reach the commanded position or its feedback does not fit the command.",["Mode door or its linkage binding, broken lever or stripped gear","Mode door actuator worn, feedback track of the potentiometer dirty","End positions not relearned after actuator replacement"],["Air comes out of the wrong vents or the selected mode is not reached","Clicking or knocking behind the dashboard while the door moves","Windscreen demisting weaker because too little air reaches the defrost outlets"],2,0,["B0170","B0268","B0205"],"דלת מצב מיזוג אוויר — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],B0152:["Driver Buckle Switch Circuit Malfunction","B0152 appears in no J2012 code list and in no public carmaker document. In J2012 the driver's buckle sensor is B0050, so the title duplicates that code. The switch tells the vehicle whether the tongue is latched. TRW's patent US5898366A places a Hall device, a magnet and an armature in the buckle, and the latch movement changes the flux and thus the output;",["Buckle plug under the driver seat loose or corroded","Buckle lead pinched or broken by seat movement","Hall sensor or contact in the buckle defective, buckle must be replaced"],["Belt reminder for the driver stays on or does not come on","Airbag warning lamp on in vehicles that read the buckle in the airbag module","Safety note: the buckle plug sits under the seat near airbag and pretensioner plugs; unplug only with the battery off and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0050","B0154","B00D0"],"מתג אבזם נהג — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0154:["Passenger Buckle Switch Circuit Malfunction","B0154 has no entry in the publicly available J2012 lists, and carmakers do not describe it in public material; J2012 assigns the front passenger buckle sensor to B0052, which this title duplicates. On the passenger side the buckle signal does more than drive a reminder: together with seat occupancy it helps the restraint module choose how the passenger airbag and pretensioner act.",["Buckle connector under the passenger seat loose, corroded or kicked off","Buckle wire chafed by the seat rail or a seat adjustment","Switch inside the buckle worn or soiled by spilled drinks"],["Passenger belt reminder wrong, permanently on or missing","Airbag warning lamp on","Safety note: seat plugs share space with airbag and pretensioner wiring; disconnect the battery and wait before unplugging anything"],4,0,["B0052","B0152","B00D1"],"מתג אבזם נוסע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0156:["Sun Load Sensor Circuit","The publicly available J2012 lists skip B0156, and public carmaker documents do not mention it; the same meaning is covered by code B0305. A sun load sensor on top of the dashboard tells automatic climate control how strongly sunlight heats the cabin, so the system can add cooling early. HELLA's solar sensor sits centrally on the dash, measures radiation across different zones and reports over LIN.",["Sensor plug under the dash top cover loose or damaged after windscreen work","Photodiode or electronics in the sun load sensor failed","Signal or supply wire shorted or open behind the dashboard"],["Cabin gets too warm in strong sun because the system does not add cooling","Automatic blower and temperature react only to air temperature"],2,0,["B0162","B0305"],""],B0158:["Ambient Air Temperature Sensor Circuit","Although B0158 is absent from the publicly available J2012 lists, General Motors and Saab use it with exactly this meaning. In the 2011 Saab 9-4X the instrument cluster reads the outside air sensor and stores B0158 02 when the signal implies more than 88 °C, B0158 05 below −40 °C; the display then shows dashes.",["Sensor at the front bumper unplugged or connector damaged after front-end work","Thermistor in the outside air sensor open or shorted, often after stone impact","Signal or low reference wire to the cluster damaged"],["Outside temperature display missing or showing dashes","Automatic climate control works with a stored or default temperature","On some GM models the HVAC display switches to Celsius"],2,0,["B0159","B0255"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוויר חיצוני — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0159:["Outside Temperature Sensor Range/Performance","No public J2012 source lists B0159. General Motors uses it: bulletin PIP5094 from 2013 lists B0159 among its service information keywords, though without a description, so no public GM text states the exact fault logic. Its neighbour B0158 is GM's outside air sensor circuit code. The sensor is an NTC thermistor behind the front bumper;",["Outside air sensor drifted or slow to react, giving plausible but wrong values","Sensor mounted where engine or road heat reaches it, e.g. after a bumper repair","Corroded contact adding resistance and shifting the reading"],["Displayed outside temperature clearly too high or too low","Climate control or A/C compressor behaves oddly because of the wrong outside value"],2,0,["B0158","B0255"],"חיישן טמפרטורה חיצונית — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],B0160:["In-Vehicle Temperature Sensor Circuit","B0160 is not among the publicly available J2012 entries, and no maker publishes it with this meaning; a similar title belongs to B0250. The in-car sensor tells automatic climate control the actual cabin temperature. To read real cabin air it is usually aspirated: Denso's patent US20040016537A1 draws cabin air across the sensor with an aspirator fed by the HVAC case, so air keeps flowing in every mode.",["Thermistor in the in-car sensor open or shorted","Sensor plug behind the dash or headliner loose or corroded","Signal or reference wire damaged during interior work"],["Automatic climate control overheats or overcools the cabin","Blower speed does not settle as the cabin reaches the set temperature"],2,0,["B0250","B0164"],""],B0162:["Sun Load Sensor 2 Circuit","No public carmaker source and no publicly available J2012 list covers B0162. The title implies a second sun load channel, as used for dual-zone climate control: Eaton's patent US5957375A describes a sensor that sees how much sun reaches separate areas of the cabin so each side can be cooled on its own.",["Second photodiode or channel of a dual-zone sun sensor failed","Connector of the sensor in the dash top cover loose or damaged","Signal wire of the second channel open or shorted"],["One side of the cabin gets too warm in sun while the other is fine","Dual-zone automatic reacts to sunshine only on one side"],2,0,["B0156","B0305"],""],B0164:["Air Bag In-Vehicle Temperature Sensor Circuit","B0164 is not listed in any publicly available J2012 table. General Motors does use the number: bulletin PIP5094 from 2013 lists it as a service information keyword, but no public GM text gives its wording. The airbag meaning in the title is not documented by any carmaker.",["Temperature sensor or its wiring open or shorted","GM: fault in the climate control sensor group around B0163 rather than the airbag","Internal temperature measurement of the control module faulty"],["Airbag or climate warning, depending on which module stored the code","Climate control may run on a substitute cabin temperature","Safety note: if the airbag module is involved, work only with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B0160","B0250"],""],B0166:["HVAC Discharge Air Temperature Sensor","The public J2012 lists do not contain B0166, and no make describes it as a discharge air sensor. Saab does use it, for the cabin rather than the outlet: in 9-3 climate control manuals from 2003 to 2012, B0166 05 marks the indoor or compartment temperature sensor as open or shorted to supply once the module input rises above 4.8 V, checked continuously with the ignition on; B0165 02 is the matching short to ground.",["Sensor open or signal shorted to supply (Saab 9-3 cabin sensor)","Sensor connector loose or left unplugged after dashboard work","On other makes, the outlet duct sensor itself failed"],["Automatic climate control misjudges cabin or outlet temperature and over- or undercorrects","Set temperature is not held steadily"],2,0,["B0160","B0250","B0173"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוויר פריקת מיזוג אוויר"],B0168:["HVAC Air Mix Door Performance","B0168 shows up neither in the publicly available J2012 lists nor, with this meaning, in public carmaker documents; air mix door circuits have the codes B0258 and B0263. The air mix or blend door divides the airflow, sending part across the heater core and part past it, and so sets outlet temperature. A performance fault means it does not reach or hold its target.",["Blend door shaft or lever broken or slipping on the actuator","Air mix actuator gear worn or motor weak","Foreign object or debris in the HVAC case blocking the door"],["Outlet air stays hot or cold regardless of the temperature setting","Temperature swings or clicking behind the dash"],2,0,["B0258","B0263"],""],B0170:["HVAC Mode Door Position Sensor","Searching the available J2012 lists and public manufacturer material turned up no entry for B0170 with this title. Unlike B0150, which concerns how the mode door moves, this code points at the sensor that reports its position. In most electronic climate actuators that sensor is a potentiometer on the gear train;",["Worn or dirty potentiometer track inside the mode actuator","Feedback signal, 5 V supply or reference wire open or shorted","Bent or pushed-back pin in the actuator connector"],["Air distribution stays fixed in one position","Actuator runs repeatedly or ticks after switching on"],2,0,["B0150","B0268"],"חיישן מצב דלת מצב מיזוג אוויר"],B0173:["Upper Left Duct Air Temperature Sensor Circuit","B0173 lacks an entry in the public J2012 lists, but General Motors documents it clearly in its Global A climate control. In the 2011 Saab 9-5 and 9-4X manuals it covers the upper left duct air temperature sensor: B0173 02 when the signal is grounded, 05 for high voltage or an open; the module flags a signal under 0.1 V or over 4.9 V and continues with a default value.",["Duct sensor harness pinched between HVAC case and cross-car beam (GM 17-NA-049)","Upper left duct sensor thermistor open or shorted","HVAC module calibration needing an update (GM PIT5383, 2015 models)"],["Left vents too warm or too cold, or heating or cooling seems not to work","Climate control runs on a default duct temperature"],2,0,["B0166","B0175"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוויר תעלה שמאלית עליונה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0175:["HVAC Recirculation Door Performance","The J2012 tables at hand leave out B0175, and no maker ties it to the recirculation door; a recirculation door circuit has the code B0273. Saab assigns the number to a temperature sensor instead. Its 9-3 climate control manuals read B0175 02 as a grounded left vent air mix temperature sensor, with the 2003 manual naming an input below 0.2 V, and the module then borrows the value of the left floor sensor;",["Recirculation door sticking or its actuator gear stripped","Saab 9-3: left vent air mix sensor or its lead shorted to ground","Actuator wiring or connector fault behind the glovebox"],["Recirculation cannot be switched or windows fog because the door stays on recirculate","Saab 9-3: left outlet temperature regulated less precisely"],2,0,["B0273","B0173","B0166"],"דלת סחרור מיזוג אוויר — ביצועים לא תקינים"],B0181:["Front Blower Motor Circuit Low","B0181 is missing from every publicly available J2012 code list, and no carmaker publishes it as a front blower code. Saab does use the number, for something else: its 9-3 climate control stores B0181 05 when the left floor air mix temperature sensor input rises above 4.8 V, i.e. open or shorted to B+. In GM's later Global A climate control the front blower speed circuit is B0193;",["Speed command line between climate module and blower module open or chafed to ground","Blower control module or series resistor burnt out, often after a sluggish motor drew too much current","Blown fuse or melted connector in the blower power feed"],["Front blower does not run at all or only at the highest stage","Windscreen demists slowly because almost no air reaches it"],2,0,["B0283","B0186","B0184"],"מנוע מפוח קדמי — אות נמוך במעגל"],B0182:["Right Front/Passenger Side Buckle Tension Sensor Circuit","B0182 appears in no J2012 list and in no public document of any carmaker, so the code cannot be verified. Its meaning overlaps B0061, the passenger belt tension sensor, and B0140. Such a sensor sits at the lower belt anchor and tells the occupant detection system how hard the belt is pulled. Delphi's patent US6605877B1 feeds the sensor and reads its data over the same two wires;",["Plug at the belt anchor sensor loose, corroded or pulled off when the seat was moved","Two-wire lead to the occupant detection module pinched or chafed under the seat","Sensor electronics faulty, for instance after a crash load on the belt"],["Airbag warning lamp lit","Passenger airbag off indicator behaves unexpectedly with a child seat or adult in the seat","Safety note: airbag and pretensioner plugs are close by; disconnect the battery and wait before unplugging anything"],4,0,["B0061","B0140","B0052"],""],B0184:["Rear Blower Motor Circuit","No publicly available J2012 list includes B0184, and no maker documents it as a rear blower code. In Saab's 9-3 climate control the number belongs to the solar sensor: B0184 06 means that circuit is open or shorted to ground, and the system then regulates as on an overcast day. GM's Global A models report a rear blower speed circuit fault as B0208;",["Long harness run to the rear blower open or shorted, often at body joints or under trim","Auxiliary blower control module or rear resistor failed","Rear blower motor worn or blocked by debris drawn in through the rear intake"],["No airflow from the rear roof or floor vents","Rear seats stay warm in summer or cold in winter while the front is comfortable"],2,0,["B0330","B0181","B0186"],"מנוע מפוח אחורי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0186:["Front Blower Motor Speed Performance","B0186 is not in the publicly available J2012 lists, and no manufacturer uses it for front blower speed. Saab assigns it to the solar sensor of the 9-3: B0186 01 is a short to B+ in that circuit, after which the climate control assumes cloudy weather.",["Leaves or other debris drawn in through the air intake, braking or jamming the fan wheel","Worn blower motor bearings or brushes, motor runs slowly or stalls","Heavily clogged cabin filter loading the motor"],["Blower speed does not match the selected stage or fluctuates","Fan stops and restarts after a pause, sometimes with a grinding noise"],2,0,["B0181","B0283","B0184"],"מהירות מנוע מפוח קדמי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],B0188:["Rear Wiper Motor Circuit","B0188 cannot be traced: it appears in no publicly available J2012 list and in no public carmaker material. The rear wiper meaning repeats B0910, titled Wiper Motor Rear Circuit. Bosch describes the part: unlike the front system, the rear wiper has a single arm driven straight off the motor, with sweep angles from 88 to 177 degrees and wiped radii of 250 to 500 mm.",["Wires broken in the rubber boot between body and tailgate after years of opening","Corroded splice or connector in the rear wiper control circuit causing a voltage drop","Rear wiper motor seized, for example from a corroded spindle, or internally shorted"],["Rear wiper does not move or works only now and then","Rear wiper stops away from its rest position"],2,0,["B0910","B0190"],"מנוע מגב אחורי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0190:["Front Wiper Park Switch Circuit","No known public source lists B0190, neither a J2012 table nor a carmaker document. The part named in the title is common: a cam on the wiper gear opens or closes contacts, so the control knows when the blades are at rest and can keep the motor running until they get there. Controllers also use this signal for protection.",["Park contacts in the wiper motor gear housing worn, dirty or corroded by water","Park signal wire or connector at the wiper motor open or shorted","Fuse or relay in the park supply circuit failed"],["Wipers stop in the field of view instead of at the bottom of the screen","Wipers keep running after being switched off or intermittent mode fails"],2,0,["B0192","B0220","B0900"],"מתג חניית מגב קדמי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0192:["Front Wiper Speed Performance","B0192 is publicly unverifiable: it appears neither in a J2012 list nor in any carmaker's documents. A performance fault, unlike the circuit fault B0220, means the wiring may be fine while the wipers sweep too slowly or irregularly. Speed is usually judged from the park contact, which closes once per revolution.",["Wiper linkage pivots dry, corroded or binding, slowing the motor","Worn motor brushes or commutator, reduced torque and speed","Blades frozen to the glass or heavily loaded by snow"],["Wipers sweep noticeably slower than usual, especially on high speed","Wiper arms judder, hesitate or run out of step with each other"],2,0,["B0220","B0190","B0900"],"מהירות מגב קדמי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],B0200:["Air Bag System Voltage Out of Range","B0200 is not documented in public: no publicly available J2012 list and no carmaker uses it with this meaning. What the title describes is real. An airbag control unit runs from the vehicle battery and needs a stable supply to fire reliably; Bosch rates its commercial vehicle unit for 8.5 to 32 V.",["Weak battery or charging fault letting system voltage sag, often while cranking","Poor ground or loose supply pin at the airbag control unit connector, or a corroded fuse contact","Airbag control unit faulty, for example its internal supply or reserve capacitor"],["Airbag warning lamp on, sometimes only after a cold start or jump start","Other modules may also log low-voltage faults","Safety note: airbags may not deploy while the fault is present; work on the system only with the battery disconnected and the wait time observed"],4,0,["B00D2","B00D3"],"מתח מערכת כרית אוויר — מחוץ לטווח"],B0205:["HVAC Defroster Door Position","B0205 is absent from the published J2012 lists, and no carmaker documents it for the defroster door; a defrost door circuit has the code B0278. Saab files its 9-3 defrost door motor under B0240 06 and B0241 01, where an open, grounded or B+ shorted motor circuit leads to wrong air distribution. The defroster door sends air to the windscreen.",["Defroster door actuator with stripped gears or worn feedback potentiometer","Door or linkage binding, broken or blocked by foreign objects","Position feedback or reference wire open or shorted"],["Little or no air reaches the windscreen in defrost mode","Air comes from the wrong outlets or a clicking noise is heard behind the dashboard"],2,0,["B0278","B0170","B0150"],""],B0210:["Rain Sensor Module","No publicly available J2012 table mentions B0210, and no carmaker documents it; lost or invalid communication with a rain sensing module is covered by U0231 and U0532. The sensor is mounted behind the windscreen, inside the car and within the wiped area. According to HELLA, light-emitting diodes shine infrared light through a prism into the glass;",["Gel pad aged or with air bubbles, often after a windscreen replacement","Rain sensor electronics failed or moisture inside the housing","Supply or data wire to the sensor at the headliner damaged"],["Automatic wiping does not react to rain or wipes on a dry screen","Wipers only work in fixed interval or manual stages","Automatic headlamps may also stop working on combined rain/light sensors"],2,0,["U0231","U0532","B0192"],""],B0220:["Front Wiper Motor Speed Circuit","B0220 is absent from the openly accessible J2012 lists and from carmaker documents, so it cannot be proven publicly; the front wiper motor circuit itself has the code B0900. The speed circuit is the part that selects slow or fast wiping. Classic wiper motors have three brushes, one for low speed, one for high and a shared one.",["High/low speed relay or its contacts failed in the fuse box or control module","Wire or plug to the low or high speed brush of the motor open or shorted","One speed brush worn out or burnt inside the wiper motor"],["Wipers work at only one speed, slow or fast","Wipers run at one speed and cannot be switched to the other"],2,0,["B0192","B0190","B0900"],"מהירות מנוע מגב קדמי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0223:["Recirculate Position Command 1 Circuit","B0223 does not appear in the publicly available J2012 lists, but General Motors uses it for the recirculation door actuator. On GM Global A cars such as the Saab 9-5 and 9-4X of model year 2011 that actuator is a stepper motor with four control lines; B0223 01 means command circuit 1 is shorted to battery, B0223 06 that it is open or low.",["Recirculation door stepper motor faulty or its gears stripped","Control line 1 to the actuator open, grounded or shorted to battery voltage","HVAC control module software, as in GM bulletin PIT5383A, or module output stage"],["Recirculation cannot be switched on or off","Windows mist up or outside smells get in because the door is stuck"],2,0,["B0273","B0175","B00D2"],""],B0226:["Headlamp Auto-Leveling Front Sensor","The publicly available J2012 lists have no B0226, and no maker documents it for headlamp levelling. Saab uses the number in its 9-3 climate control: B0226 01 is a short to B+ in the recirculation motor circuit, possibly causing stale air or misted windows. Automatic levelling, as HELLA explains, keeps the beam cut-off steady as the load changes.",["Lever or coupling rod of the front axle sensor bent, broken or detached","Connector or wire at the sensor corroded or damaged by road splash","Sensor worn out internally or not calibrated after replacement or suspension work"],["Headlamp levelling warning shown and beam height no longer adjusts","Oncoming drivers flash because the beam is set too high under load"],2,0,["U0181","U0482"],""],B0228:["Front Fog Lamp Circuit","B0228 appears in none of the publicly available J2012 lists, and no carmaker publishes it as a fog lamp code. General Motors does use the number, but inside climate control: bulletin PIT5383 lists B0228 among the HVAC codes of 2015 Cadillac, Chevrolet and GMC models whose K33 climate module needed new software; GM does not publish its exact wording. Read as titled, the code concerns the drive of the front fog lamps.",["Fog lamp relay or fuse failed, so the lamps get no supply although the switch is on","Low-mounted harness in the front bumper torn or corroded, often after a parking knock or water ingress","Bulb burnt out or lamp housing flooded through a cracked lens","Fog position of the light switch worn or its signal line open"],["Front fog lamps stay dark although the switch is on","Fog lamp indicator lights up but only one lamp or none works"],1,0,["B0240","B0800"],""],B0231:["Front Marker Lamp Circuit","B0231 is found neither in any publicly available J2012 list nor in public service documents of a carmaker, so the code cannot be verified. The title points to the front marker or position lamps. FMVSS 108 places side marker lamps close to the leading and trailing ends of the body so that, seen from the side, they reveal how long the vehicle is.",["Bulb or LED module of the marker lamp failed","Corroded bulb holder or plug in the headlamp area, where spray water reaches it","Feed or ground wire to the front lamp open or shorted"],["One front marker or position lamp stays dark with parking lights on","Bulb failure warning in the instrument cluster, where the car has one"],1,0,["B0239","B0830"],""],B0233:["Air Flow Control Circuit","Public J2012 listings leave B0233 out, yet GM assigns it in its Global A climate control for the air distribution (mode) actuator. On 2011 Saab 9-5 and 9-4X cars that actuator is a stepper motor: the HVAC module feeds it a 12 V reference and switches its four coils to ground in pulses. B0233 01 means one of its control lines is shorted to voltage, B0233 06 that a line is open or low.",["Mode stepper actuator failed internally, e.g. a burnt coil or worn gear","One of the four control lines or the 12 V reference chafed, open or shorted behind the dash","HVAC module software fault on affected GM models, fixed by reprogramming"],["Air comes from the wrong outlets and the selected distribution is ignored","Windscreen cannot be demisted because air will not switch to defrost"],2,0,["B0268","B0150","B0170"],"זרימת אוויר — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],B0235:["Brake Lamp Circuit","No publicly available J2012 list contains B0235, nor does any carmaker describe it, which leaves it unverified; side-specific brake lamp codes are B0850 and B0851. Stop lamps send a steady red signal rearward while the driver brakes, and FMVSS 108 also demands a third stop lamp mounted high. The brake light switch at the pedal triggers them, directly or via a body module.",["Stop lamp bulb or LED unit failed","Brake light switch misadjusted, worn or wet inside","Blown fuse or broken wire, often in the tailgate or boot lid harness","Corroded lamp holder or plug in the rear light cluster"],["One or more brake lamps stay dark when the pedal is pressed","Bulb warning shown, sometimes together with traction or stability warning lamps","Safety note: following traffic gets no braking signal; repair before further driving"],1,0,["B0850","B0851"],"נורת בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0237:["Backup Lamp Circuit","Neither the publicly available J2012 lists nor any public service literature mention B0237, so it remains unconfirmed. In the words of FMVSS 108, backup lamps light the road behind the car and warn pedestrians and drivers that it is reversing or about to. HELLA notes that the circuit may only be live with the ignition on and reverse engaged. Manual gearboxes close a plunger switch in reverse;",["Reverse light switch on the gearbox worn or its plug corroded by road spray","Reversing lamp bulb burnt out or LED unit failed","Missing reverse signal from the range sensor or transmission module on automatics","Broken wire in the tailgate harness feeding the lamp"],["Reversing lamps stay dark with reverse gear engaged","Reversing lamps lit while driving forward"],1,0,["B0239","B0235"],""],B0239:["License Plate Lamp Circuit","B0239 cannot be traced in any J2012 source or factory document, so its use stays unproven; the same title belongs to B0860. The licence plate lamp lights the rear registration plate and is usually wired with the tail lamps. FMVSS 108 asks that it illuminate the plate without obstruction by body parts. HELLA quotes the European rule that the plate must be readable from 25 m, with no part of it below 2.5 cd/m².",["Plate lamp bulb or LED unit failed, often from water inside the housing","Wire broken in the flexible tube between body and tailgate or boot lid","Retrofitted LED lamp not matched by the body module coding"],["Rear number plate is not lit with the lights on","Bulb warning in the cluster, where the car monitors this lamp"],1,0,["B0860","B0237"],""],B0240:["Headlamp Switch Circuit","Searching J2012 sources turned up no B0240, and no maker applies it to the headlamp switch; the identical title belongs to B0800. Saab gives the number another job: in the 9-3 climate system B0240 06 means the defrost door motor circuit is open or grounded, with wrong air distribution as a result, and B0241 01 that this motor is shorted to B+. Going by its title, the code concerns the light switch input.",["Worn or dirty contacts or resistor track inside the light switch","Switch plug loose or corroded behind the dashboard trim","Signal line to the body module shorted to ground or supply"],["Lights do not follow the switch position or fall back to a fixed setting","Automatic lights or parking lights cannot be selected"],2,0,["B0800","B0228","B0278"],"מתג פנס ראשי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0245:["Driver Window Switch Circuit","B0245 is unknown to every publicly available J2012 source and undocumented by carmakers, so nothing public backs it; driver window faults have the code B0500. The driver's door usually holds the master switch block, which commands its own window and, by signal lines or a bus, the other doors.",["Master switch contacts corroded or sticking, often after drinks or rain got into the door panel","Wires broken in the rubber boot between body and driver's door","Plug of the switch block loose or with pushed-back pins"],["Driver's window or other windows do not respond to the master switch","A window moves on its own or the one-touch function misbehaves"],1,0,["B0247","B0252","B0500"],"מתג חלון נהג — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0247:["Passenger Window Switch Circuit","B0247 is listed in none of the publicly available J2012 sources and no carmaker publishes it; passenger window circuit faults have the code B0501. The passenger switch is the simpler partner of the driver's master block: it moves only its own window, and the master can override it or lock it out.",["Passenger window switch worn or contaminated","Signal line between passenger door and master switch broken at the door hinge","Window lock button on the master stuck or its circuit faulty"],["Passenger window works from the driver's switch but not from its own","Passenger switch moves the window only in one direction"],1,0,["B0245","B0501"],"מתג חלון נוסע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0250:["HVAC Air Temperature Internal Sensor Circuit","None of the publicly available J2012 lists contain B0250. On the Saab 9-3 the number marks an actuator fault instead: B0250 06 means the floor door motor circuit is open or grounded, which upsets air distribution, while B0251 01 is the B+ short. Taken by its title, the code is about the cabin temperature sensor, which also has the code B0160.",["Sensor plug or wiring behind the dashboard open or shorted to ground","NTC element in the sensor damaged","Aspirator fan seized or its intake grille blocked, so the reading lags behind cabin temperature"],["Automatic climate control holds the wrong cabin temperature","Blower speed and outlet temperature no longer adapt as the cabin warms up"],1,0,["B0160","B0255","B0164"],"חיישן פנימי טמפרטורת אוויר מיזוג אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0252:["Driver Window Motor Down Circuit","For B0252 there is neither a J2012 entry nor any factory description, so the code is unverified. The title names one direction of the driver's window motor. A reversible DC motor moves the glass; the down path is the half of the drive that puts supply on one motor terminal and ground on the other.",["Down relay contact or driver transistor in the door module burnt","One motor lead broken in the door or at the motor plug","Worn motor brushes or commutator with a dead spot in one direction"],["Driver's window closes but will not go down","Pinch protection or one-touch down no longer works"],2,0,["B0245","B0500"],""],B0255:["HVAC Air Temperature External Sensor Circuit","B0255 shows up in no publicly available J2012 source. Saab's 9-3 uses it for a door motor: B0255 06 reports the right vent door motor circuit open or grounded, B0256 01 the B+ short on that motor. By its title, though, the code means the outside air sensor; that component also has the codes B0158 and B0159.",["Outside sensor broken by stone impact or corroded by road salt","Sensor wiring behind the bumper pinched or torn, often after front-end repairs","Moisture in the sensor plug changing the measured resistance"],["Outside temperature display shows dashes or an implausible value","Automatic climate control regulates poorly, especially in cold or hot weather"],1,0,["B0158","B0159","B0250"],"חיישן חיצוני טמפרטורת אוויר מיזוג אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0258:["HVAC Air Mix Door 1 Circuit","The public J2012 sources do not list B0258, and no carmaker documents it publicly; it cannot be verified. GM's Global A system logs its left, or main, temperature actuator under B0408 instead, as the 2011 Saab 9-5 manual shows. Air mix door 1 is normally the main or driver-side blend door and divides the air between heater core and bypass.",["Blend door actuator motor or its feedback potentiometer failed","Actuator plug or wires under the dashboard loose, chafed or shorted","Door jammed by debris or a broken shaft, overloading the motor drive"],["Air from the vents stays hot or cold whatever temperature is set","Clicking or knocking behind the dashboard when the temperature is changed"],2,0,["B0263","B0168"],""],B0260:["Interior Light Circuit","No publicly available J2012 list contains B0260 with this meaning, and the same title belongs to B0970. Saab uses the number in the climate control of the 2003 9-3: B0260 06 stands for the left vent door motor circuit open or grounded, B0261 01 for a short to B+. By its title, the code means the courtesy lamp supply. Door ajar switches ground an input when a door opens;",["Door contact switch or lock contact sticking, so the module sees a door open","Lamp feed shorted in the roof liner or a lamp unit with water damage","Battery saver relay or output stage in the body module faulty"],["Interior lamps do not come on when a door opens","Interior lamps stay lit or the battery is flat after the car stood overnight"],1,0,["B0970","B0540","B0510"],"אור פנימי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0263:["HVAC Air Mix Door 2 Circuit","B0263 shares the fate of its sibling B0258: no publicly available J2012 source lists it and no maker describes it. The second blend door usually serves the passenger side or the rear zone. Saab's 9-5 and 9-4X service data, which follow GM's Global A scheme, file the right temperature actuator under B0418 and the rear one under B0428, each a stepper motor checked for shorts to voltage and for opens.",["Passenger-side or rear blend actuator failed","Wiring to the second actuator open or shorted, often near the centre console","Shared linkage or door shaft broken, overloading the drive"],["Passenger side or rear outlets stay at one temperature whatever is set","Noticeable temperature difference between left and right outlets"],2,0,["B0258","B0168"],""],B0265:["Driver Door Lock/Unlock Switch Circuit","Nothing in the publicly available J2012 sources or carmaker literature mentions B0265, so it is unverifiable; related codes are B0270 and B0272. The lock/unlock button in the driver's door tells the body or door module to run all lock motors, as HELLA's overview of central locking describes.",["Lock/unlock button sticking or shorted by moisture in the door panel","Switch wires broken in the boot between body and driver's door","Input stage in the body or door module damaged"],["Doors cannot be locked or unlocked with the interior button","Locks cycle on their own or ignore the remote key"],2,0,["B0270","B0272","B0530"],""],B0268:["HVAC Mode Door 1 Circuit","B0268 is not in the published J2012 lists, but General Motors uses the number: bulletin PIP5094, written for 2014 and older GM cars and light trucks, includes it in its keyword list of body codes, without a descriptor. The mode door routes air to face vents, footwell or windscreen. GM's later Global A system files the mode actuator under B0233; B0150 and B0170 also exist for this door.",["Mode door actuator motor or position feedback failed","Actuator over-travelling or binding at the door, overloading its drive","Actuator plug or wiring behind the dash open or shorted"],["Air stays on one outlet, for example defrost, whatever mode is chosen","Pressing the mode button no longer changes where the air comes out"],2,0,["B0150","B0170","B0233","B0278"],"דלת מצב מיזוג אוויר‏ 1 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0270:["Passenger Door Lock Switch Circuit","Public evidence for B0270 is lacking: it is absent from every publicly available J2012 list, and no manufacturer describes it. The title points to the lock/unlock rocker in the front passenger door.",["Lock rocker in the passenger door worn, sticking or contaminated","Switch signal wire chafed to ground or broken in the door hinge passage","Water ingress or corrosion at the door trim switch connector","Door or body control module input stage faulty"],["Passenger door lock button has no effect on central locking","Doors lock or unlock by themselves when the switch line is shorted","Remote key and driver switch still lock the car normally"],1,0,["B0265","B0272","B0531"],"מתג נעילת דלת נוסע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0272:["Power Door Lock Switch Circuit","Neither the reachable J2012 lists nor any carmaker's documents mention B0272, which leaves the code unproven. Its title covers the interior central-locking button in general, without naming a door. Saab logs a held button in the 9-3 driver door module as B3270 61: if the input stays low, the module waits until the key is released and pressed again before acting.",["Central-locking button mechanically stuck or contacts worn","Switch wire shorted to ground or open between switch and module","Spilled liquid or condensation in the switch panel","Door or body control module misreads the switch input"],["Interior lock button does not lock or unlock the doors","Locks cycle unexpectedly or only react to the remote key"],1,0,["B0265","B0270","B0530"],"מתג נעילת דלת כוח — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0273:["HVAC Recirculation Door Circuit","B0273 could not be traced in the code lists at hand, nor in any manufacturer publication. The title concerns the electrical circuit of the actuator that swings the intake door between outside air and cabin air. Saab uses its own numbers here: in the 9-3 climate module B0225 06 stands for an open or grounded recirculation motor circuit and B0226 01 for a line shorted to battery voltage;",["Recirculation door actuator motor burnt out or internally open","Actuator wiring behind the glovebox chafed, shorted or unplugged","Door jammed by leaves or debris so the motor stalls at high current","Driver stage in the climate control module defective"],["Recirculation button changes nothing at the air intake","Windows fog up or outside odours enter the cabin","Reduced cooling on hot days"],2,0,["B0175","B0278"],"דלת סחרור מיזוג אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0274:["Trunk Lid Release Switch Circuit","Nothing public confirms B0274 – the publicly available J2012 tables skip it and no maker explains it. The title refers to the switch the driver or a passer-by uses to release the boot lid electrically. Saab treats the button separately in the 9-3: the driver door module sets B2730 61 when the boot button stays active for more than 20 s, after which the lid will not open.",["Exterior release button corroded or full of water and dirt","Wires broken in the flexible boot lid hinge loom","Interior release button held or jammed by trim","Door or body module input reading the switch defective"],["Boot lid cannot be opened with the button, only by key or remote","Lid unlatches without anyone pressing the button"],1,0,["B0272"],"מתג שחרור מכסה תא מטען — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0278:["HVAC Defrost Door Circuit","B0278 appears neither in J2012 tables nor in factory service material, so its existence is open. By its title it covers the electrical side of the defrost door actuator, the flap that routes air to the windscreen. Saab's 9-3 climate module stores the matching fault as B0240 06 (actuator circuit open or grounded) and B0241 01 (short to battery or excessive current); both lead to wrong air distribution.",["Defrost door actuator motor open or shorted internally","Actuator wiring under the dashboard damaged or connector loose","Door or linkage seized so the motor draws excessive current","Actuator driver in the climate control module failed"],["Windscreen clears slowly because little air reaches it","Air keeps blowing at the windscreen whatever mode is selected"],2,0,["B0205","B0273"],"דלת הפשרת מיזוג אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0283:["Rear Defogger Relay Control Circuit","B0283 is not in any publicly available J2012 list; it is documented by Saab/GM, where it means the heated rear window relay, not a blower. In the Saab 9-3 (2003–2012) the rear electrical centre sets B0283 01 when the relay output exceeds 6 V with heating on, and B0283 06 when it stays below 6 V (open or grounded line).",["Rear window heater relay with open coil or welded contacts","Relay control wire open, grounded or shorted to battery voltage","Poor ground or corroded socket at the relay","Output stage of the climate or electrical centre module faulty"],["Heated rear window does not work when switched on","Rear window heats continuously and cannot be switched off","Battery drained if the grid keeps heating"],1,0,["B0290","B0950"],""],B0288:["HVAC A/C Pressure Sensor Circuit","A search found B0288 in no J2012 list and in no carmaker's service data; it stays unconfirmed. The refrigerant pressure sensor it names sits on the high-pressure line; its signal decides whether the compressor may run and how fast the cooling fan turns. On most cars the engine controller reads it and stores P0530–P0533.",["Refrigerant pressure sensor failed or signal drifting","Sensor connector near the condenser corroded by road spray","5 V reference, ground or signal wire open or shorted","Very low refrigerant charge giving an implausible reading"],["Air conditioning blows warm because the compressor is disabled","Radiator fan runs constantly or at the wrong speed"],1,0,["P0530","P0532","P0533","B0292"],"חיישן לחץ מזגן מיזוג אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0290:["Rear Defrost Switch Circuit","B0290 has no public source: the publicly available J2012 tables omit it, and service literature is silent. The title names the push button that requests the heated rear window. On the 2011 Saab 9-5 (GM) that button sits in the climate control faceplate, which passes the request to the climate module; only the relay output has its own code there (B0283). Saab's 9-3 monitors the button lamp separately as B0969 02.",["Rear defrost button contacts worn or button stuck in the panel","Climate control faceplate or its circuit board defective","Signal or data line between panel and module interrupted"],["Pressing the rear defrost button has no effect","Rear window heating switches on by itself or cannot be cancelled","Indicator lamp in the button stays dark or lit"],1,0,["B0283","B0950"],"מתג הפשרה אחורית — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0292:["HVAC A/C Compressor Clutch Circuit","Whether B0292 is used anywhere is unknown; no consulted J2012 list carries it and no maker documents it. Its title points to the electromagnetic clutch that couples a belt-driven compressor to its pulley, and the relay feeding the clutch coil. Usually the engine controller owns this circuit and logs P0645–P0647;",["Clutch coil open or shorted, often after overheating","A/C clutch relay failed or contacts welded","Excessive clutch air gap so the plate does not pull in","Clutch feed or ground wire at the compressor damaged by heat"],["No cooling, compressor hub does not turn with A/C on","Compressor runs permanently even with A/C switched off"],2,0,["P0645","P0646","P0647","B0288"],"מצמד מדחס מזגן מיזוג אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0300:["HVAC Evaporator Temperature Sensor Circuit","Public code lists do not show B0300, and factory documentation for it is missing too. The evaporator temperature sensor is a thermistor on or just behind the evaporator core; the climate controller cycles or throttles the compressor with it so that the core does not ice up (US6427465B1, US4326386A).",["Evaporator thermistor open, shorted or out of tolerance","Sensor pushed out of the core or poorly sealed after service","Connector at the HVAC housing loose or corroded by condensate","Sensor input in the climate control module faulty"],["Cooling weak or fluctuating, especially in hot weather","Airflow drops after a long drive because the evaporator ices up"],2,0,["B0292","B0288"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מאייד מיזוג אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0305:["HVAC Sun Load Sensor Circuit","B0305 is unconfirmed by any public J2012 list or manufacturer, and its subject matches B0156. The sun load sensor is a photodiode on top of the dashboard that tells automatic climate control how much solar heat enters the cabin (US6888120B2, US5957375A).",["Sun load sensor photodiode aged or damaged","Sensor unclipped from the dashboard grille, connector pulled off","Signal or ground wire to the sensor open or shorted"],["Cabin too warm in bright sunshine with auto climate","Blower speed does not rise when the sun comes out"],1,0,["B0156","B0162"],""],B0310:["Driver Seat Position Sensor Circuit","For B0310 there is neither a J2012 list entry nor a known manufacturer description. The title refers to the position feedback of the power driver seat. GM's 2011 Saab 9-5 uses Hall sensors built into each seat motor; the memory module feeds them 12 V and counts their pulses (0–65,535) to know where the seat is; its codes are B1825, B2355, B2365 and B2375.",["Hall sensor inside a seat motor failed","Wiring under the seat pinched by the rails or pulled off","Sensor supply or ground circuit open or shorted","Seat memory module input fault"],["Memory buttons do not recall stored seat positions","Seat moves jerkily or stops short of its end position","Easy-entry function does not move the seat back"],2,0,["B0320","B0322","B0325","B0580"],"חיישן מצב מושב נהג — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0312:["Driver Seat Forward/Back Switch Circuit","B0312 is undocumented in public: no accessible code list includes it and no automaker defines it. The title means the switch that moves the driver seat fore and aft. GM's 2011 Saab 9-5 tracks it as B1755 (forward) and B1760 (rearward): a switch line shorted to ground, or one direction active while the opposite is pressed, disables that motor both ways and blocks memory recall.",["Seat switch contacts worn or the knob stuck in one direction","Drink spilled into the side-mounted switch","Switch wiring chafed under the seat cover","Seat module misreading the switch inputs"],["Driver seat moves only forward or only backward","Seat fore-aft movement dead while other axes work","Memory recall ignored"],1,0,["B0560","B0310"],""],B0320:["Passenger Seat Position Sensor Circuit","None of the J2012 lists on hand names B0320, and no vehicle maker publishes a definition. The title concerns position feedback on a powered front passenger seat, which exists mainly where that seat has memory or an easy-entry function. Saab's 9-3 passenger seat module uses B2375 for its fore-aft sensor: 01 when the input exceeds 7 ± 0.2 V, 04 for an open line;",["Position sensor in the passenger seat motor failed","Seat loom damaged by objects or feet under the seat","Sensor signal shorted to supply voltage","Passenger seat module input faulty"],["Passenger seat memory or easy-entry does not work","Seat jerks when starting or stopping"],2,0,["B0310","B0327","B0570"],"חיישן מצב מושב נוסע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0322:["Driver Seat Tilt Position Sensor","B0322 lacks any public definition, either in J2012 lists or from a manufacturer. The title describes the sensor reporting the cushion tilt of the power driver seat, normally made by raising or lowering the front edge. Saab's 9-3 driver seat module calls it the tilt position sensor and stores B3923: 01 above 7 ± 0.2 V, 02 when shorted to ground, 04 for an open line and 29 when no pulses arrive while the engine runs.",["Sensor in the cushion tilt motor failed","Tilt motor wiring pinched in the seat frame","Shared sensor supply shorted or open","Seat module input stage defective"],["Cushion tilt not restored by memory recall","Tilt adjustment jerks or stops before the end"],2,0,["B0310","B0561"],""],B0325:["Driver Seat Memory Set Switch","Searches turned up B0325 in no J2012 list and in no factory documentation. The title names the SET or M button used to store the current seat position under one of the memory buttons. Saab's 9-3 driver seat module knows it as the memorize button: B2765 01 when its line is shorted to battery voltage, B2765 61 when it is held or stuck for more than 60 s;",["Memory set button stuck in the door or seat panel","Switch contacts worn or contaminated","Button wire shorted to supply voltage or broken"],["New seat positions cannot be stored","Memory buttons recall old settings only"],1,0,["B0580","B0310","B0327"],""],B0327:["Passenger Seat Position Memory","No known public list or manufacturer document defines B0327. The title is vague: it suggests a fault in storing or restoring positions of a power passenger seat. For that a module needs working position feedback; in Saab's 9-3 passenger seat module a lost slide sensor signal (B2375) switches off all memory functions and erases the end-stop calibration.",["Missing position feedback from a passenger seat motor","Stored positions lost after battery disconnection or low voltage","End stops not relearned after seat or motor replacement","Passenger seat module memory faulty"],["Passenger seat does not return to its stored position","Stored settings forgotten after the ignition is switched off"],2,0,["B0320","B0325"],"זיכרון מצב מושב נוסע"],B0330:["HVAC Rear Blower Motor Circuit","B0330 cannot be found in accessible J2012 lists or carmaker sources, and it overlaps B0184 in content. The rear blower moves conditioned air to the back rows, often as a second fan in a rear duct (US6915650B2) or a separate rear unit with its own speed control (US4949779A).",["Rear blower speed controller or resistor burnt out","Rear blower motor seized or brushes worn","Speed command wire open or shorted between modules","Rear blower fuse or supply relay failed"],["No air from the rear vents","Rear blower runs only at one speed or cannot be switched off"],2,0,["B0184","B0181"],"מנוע מפוח אחורי מיזוג אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0335:["Driver Seat Heater Circuit","B0335 is unsupported by J2012 lists and by service information; its topic duplicates B0341. The circuit is the heating mat in the driver cushion and backrest plus its supply. Real codes elsewhere: Saab's 9-3 climate module stores B2428 01 when the left heater is shorted to battery voltage and B2429 06 for an open left heater;",["Heating wire in the driver cushion broken by repeated flexing","Seat heater connector under the seat loose or burnt","Element or feed wire shorted to the seat frame","Output stage of the seat heating or climate module defective"],["Driver seat stays cold although heating is switched on","Seat heating indicator flashes or goes out after a few seconds","Only the backrest or only the cushion warms up"],2,0,["B0337","B0339","B0341"],"גוף חימום מושב נהג — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0337:["Passenger Seat Heater Circuit","There is no public trace of B0337 in J2012 lists or factory data; its subject repeats B0342. It covers the passenger seat heating mat and its feed. Because that seat is often empty, a fault may go unnoticed for a long time. Saab's 9-3 climate module reports B2433 01 when the right heater is shorted to battery voltage and B2434 06 for an open or grounded circuit; GM's 2011 Saab 9-5 uses B2430 0B/0D/0E.",["Heating wire in the passenger cushion or backrest broken","Connector under the passenger seat kicked loose or corroded","Damage during work on the occupant detection mat in the same cushion","Heater output in the controlling module defective"],["Passenger seat heating does not warm up","Heating switches off shortly after activation"],2,0,["B0335","B0339","B0342"],"גוף חימום מושב נוסע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0339:["Rear Seat Heater Circuit","B0339 shows up neither in the public code lists nor in published service material. Rear seat heating is an option on larger cars; the GM-built 2011 Saab 9-4X with heated rear seats has a dedicated control module behind the rear backrest.",["Heating mat in a rear seat cushion broken","Connector damaged when the rear seat was folded or removed","Rear seat heating control module or its supply faulty","Seat temperature sensor implausible so heating is disabled"],["One or both rear seat heaters stay cold","Rear seat heating indicator flashes or goes out"],2,0,["B0335","B0337"],"גוף חימום מושב אחורי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0341:["HVAC Heated Seat Driver Circuit","B0341 is not backed by any known J2012 list or carmaker text, and it covers the same ground as B0335. The HVAC prefix fits cars whose climate control module also runs the seat heaters. Saab's 9-3 is one: its climate module drives the left seat heater and reads a seat temperature sensor; B1927 02 (input below 0.2 V) switches the left heater off, and B2429 06 reports an open element.",["Driver heating mat open circuit","Seat temperature sensor shorted or open so heating is blocked","Long harness from climate module to seat damaged at the seat rail","Seat heater output in the climate control module failed"],["Driver seat heating dead while climate control works","Heating starts but stops after a short time"],2,0,["B0335","B0342"],"נהג מושב מחומם מיזוג אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0342:["HVAC Heated Seat Passenger Circuit","No accessible J2012 list or manufacturer source mentions B0342; it matches B0337 in substance. As with the driver side, the HVAC prefix implies a climate module that also drives the passenger seat heater.",["Right seat temperature sensor open or shorted","Passenger heating mat broken","Connector under the passenger seat loose","Climate module seat heater driver or sensor input faulty"],["Passenger seat heating switches off immediately","Passenger seat stays cold"],2,0,["B0337","B0341"],"נוסע מושב מחומם מיזוג אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0420:["Audio System Internal Failure","No public J2012 list carries B0420 with this meaning, and no carmaker describes an audio-system fault under it. The one documented use is unrelated: Saab files B0420 06 in the 9-3 (2003–2012) climate control as an open or grounded circuit to the right air-mix flap motor, which upsets temperature control. Read literally, the title points to a fault inside the head unit, the part that feeds every speaker channel.",["Internal electronics or software of the head unit faulty","Low or unstable supply voltage or poor ground at the head unit","Unit overheated because of blocked ventilation behind the dash"],["No sound from any speaker, or the radio restarts by itself","Head unit freezes or ignores its buttons","Code stored together with other infotainment faults"],2,0,["B0425","B0455","U0184"],""],B0425:["Audio Amplifier Internal Failure","Every accessible J2012 list lacks B0425, and no maker's literature mentions it, leaving the code itself unverified. The title concerns a fault inside the separate audio amplifier rather than in its wiring. Amplifier chips such as TI's TAS6424E-Q1 check each channel for open load, shorted load and shorts to battery or ground, and raise a warning on clipping or overtemperature.",["Output stage or internal electronics of the amplifier failed","Amplifier overheated, e.g. under a seat or in the boot without airflow","Moisture or water in the amplifier housing or plug","Shorted speaker or wiring that has overloaded the output stage"],["No sound or only very low volume from the amplified speakers","Crackling, hum or distortion, often worse when warm","Subwoofer or premium sound channels drop out"],2,0,["B0420","U0186","U0262"],""],B0440:["Bluetooth Module Fault","No public J2012 source lists B0440, and no carmaker explains it, so the code cannot be verified. The title concerns the Bluetooth unit that pairs a phone for hands-free calls and music streaming. Automotive chips such as NXP's AW300, qualified to AEC-Q100, handle the HFP and A2DP profiles; TI's WiLink 8Q family combines Bluetooth with Wi-Fi and GNSS for infotainment units.",["Software fault or hung state of the Bluetooth/telematics unit","Bluetooth chip or its module failed internally","Poor supply or ground connection at the module"],["Phone cannot be paired or is not found","Hands-free calls drop or music streaming stops","Bluetooth menu greyed out or missing"],2,0,["B0460","B0450","U0198"],""],B0445:["USB Hub Fault","B0445 does not appear in any reachable J2012 list and is not described by a manufacturer, so its existence is unproven. A USB hub in the car splits one host port of the head unit across several sockets for media and charging.",["Socket damaged or contaminated, short between pins","Cable between hub and head unit loose or chafed","Hub electronics or protection switch failed","Connected device or cable draws too much current"],["USB stick or phone not recognised","Socket charges but transfers no data, or vice versa","Phone projection drops out repeatedly"],1,0,["B0420","B0440"],""],B0450:["Microphone Circuit","The code B0450 is absent from the publicly accessible J2012 lists, and no carmaker publishes it, so it remains unverified. Its title covers the hands-free microphone line. The module puts a bias voltage on the signal wire and reads speech back on the same wire.",["Microphone in the headliner or mirror failed","Microphone wire pinched or broken in the headliner or A-pillar","Plug at microphone or module loose or corroded"],["Caller cannot hear the driver during hands-free calls","Voice control does not react to spoken commands","Emergency call or telematics status lamp shows a fault"],1,0,["B0440","U0198"],"מיקרופון — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0455:["Display Module Internal Failure","No J2012 list available to the public includes B0455, and factory literature is silent on it, so the code is unverified. It names an internal fault of a display module, such as the centre screen or a cluster panel, not its wiring or data link. Saab's 2011 9-5 sets B1020 when the radio gets an improper status reply from its display assembly, pointing to an electronics fault or a jammed button;",["Display controller or panel electronics failed","Software fault, often curable by an update","Button on the display unit jammed and reported as a fault"],["Screen stays black, flickers or freezes on one picture","Touch input or buttons on the display do not respond","Information moves to another display or a warning appears"],2,0,["B0490","U0162","U0255"],""],B0460:["Bluetooth Antenna Circuit","B0460 appears in none of the accessible J2012 lists and in no manufacturer document, so it remains unproven. Its title concerns the Bluetooth antenna circuit. GM's Global A system in the Saab 9-5 and 9-4X (2011) covers the same part under its own number B2485: the small antenna sits directly on the OnStar module without a cable, is tested once a second, and an open or grounded antenna disables Bluetooth and turns…",["Antenna contact or plug at the module loose or corroded","Antenna or its lead damaged, e.g. after work behind the dash","Antenna detection or radio stage inside the module faulty"],["Phone pairs only at very short distance or not at all","Bluetooth switched off by the module, status lamp red","Calls and streaming break up repeatedly"],2,0,["B0440","U0198"],""],B0490:["Display Backlight Circuit","B0490 is not listed in any accessible J2012 source, nor does a carmaker's literature cover it, so public proof is lacking. The title covers the backlight of a display, today usually LED strings fed by a boost driver. TI's LP8866-Q1 and LP8872-Q1 flag open strings, shorted LEDs and LED shorts to ground and report them to the host;",["LED string or single LED of the backlight failed","Backlight driver or its boost stage defective","Brightness control line open or shorted"],["Screen dark although content is faintly visible in bright light","Brightness cannot be adjusted or follows no day/night change","Uneven, flickering or partly dark backlight"],2,0,["B0455"],""],B0500:["Driver Power Window Circuit Malfunction","No public J2012 list includes B0500, and no carmaker documents it, so the code is not verified. The title concerns the driver's power window circuit. Saab handles this under its own numbers: in the 9-3 (2003–2012) the driver door module logs B3205/B3210 for an open, shorted or overloaded down or up path and retries on every new drive cycle;",["Window motor worn, sluggish or with a dead spot","Wires broken in the rubber boot between body and door","Regulator or glass runs bind, motor overloads","End positions lost after battery disconnection, relearn needed"],["Driver window does not move or only in one direction","One-touch up/down and pinch protection out of action","Window stops or reverses partway without reason"],2,0,["B0245","B0252","B0501","U0222"],"חלון כוח נהג — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0501:["Passenger Power Window Circuit Malfunction","For B0501 neither the reachable J2012 lists nor any manufacturer offer a definition, so the code is unverified. The title points to the front passenger window circuit. Saab's 9-3 passenger door module uses B3205/B3210 for its own motor paths and B3932 when it measures current while the motor should be idle; one-touch travel then stops.",["Passenger window motor worn or internally faulty","Passenger button in the driver's master switch faulty","Wiring broken in the passenger door hinge passage","Replacement motor not coded or not matched to the body module"],["Passenger window dead from both the local and the master switch","Window works only while the button is held","Window moves slowly or stops partway"],2,0,["B0247","B0500","U0223"],"חלון כוח נוסע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0502:["Left Rear Power Window Circuit Malfunction","B0502 has no entry in any accessible J2012 list, and no carmaker describes it, so the code stays unproven. Its title concerns the left rear window circuit. In the Saab 9-3 the left rear door module logs B3210 04 when the motor's up path is open and the glass will not close, and B3543 if the two Hall signals arrive in reverse order for 150 ms, which disables one-touch travel.",["Hall sensor in the motor or its supply faulty","Left rear window motor worn or with an open winding","Wires broken in the rear door hinge passage"],["Left rear window will not close or will not open","One-touch function and pinch protection not available","Window reverses on its own without an obstacle"],2,0,["B0503","B0500","U0224"],"חלון כוח אחורי שמאלי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0503:["Right Rear Power Window Circuit Malfunction","Public J2012 lists do not contain B0503, and no carmaker publishes a description, so the code is unverified. The title names the right rear window circuit. In the 9-3, Saab's right rear door module sets B3205 04 for an open down path and b3992 11 when the glass travels further than expected between its end stops; one-touch up and pinch protection then stop working.",["Regulator cable or guide slipped, glass travel no longer matches","Right rear window motor worn or internally faulty","Motor or door plug corroded by water in the door"],["Right rear window does not open or moves only jerkily","One-touch closing and pinch protection disabled","Window stops short of the top seal or runs past it with noise"],2,0,["B0502","B0501","U0225"],"חלון כוח אחורי ימני — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0510:["Driver Door Open Switch","B0510 is missing from the publicly available J2012 lists, and no manufacturer defines it in accessible documents. GM does list B0510 among the circuit DTC keywords of bulletin PIP5094 (2014 and earlier cars and light trucks), but without a descriptor. The title points to the switch that tells the body electronics the driver door is being opened.",["Driver door switch worn, dirty or stuck in one position","Wire broken or chafed in the driver door hinge passage","Moisture or corrosion at the switch connector","Input stage of the body or keyless entry module faulty"],["Interior light stays off when the driver door is opened","Keyless opening at the driver handle does not respond","Door-open message or chime missing or shown permanently"],1,0,["B0520","B0540","B0260"],""],B0520:["Passenger Door Open Switch","No accessible J2012 list contains B0520, and its meaning is not published by any carmaker. The code exists at GM: PIP5094, a circuit-testing bulletin for 2014 and earlier GM vehicles, lists it as a keyword but leaves it undefined. The title describes the switch reporting that the front passenger door is opening.",["Passenger door switch contacts worn, greased up or frozen","Wire break in the passenger door hinge passage","Exterior handle switch shorted by water ingress","Body or keyless entry module input faulty"],["Passenger door opening not detected by interior light or alarm","Passenger exterior handle ignored by the keyless system","Auto-lock may relock the car with the key inside"],1,0,["B0510","B0541","B0260"],""],B0530:["Driver Door Lock Actuator Circuit","B0530 does not appear in the publicly available J2012 lists. GM names it among the circuit keywords of PIP5094 without a descriptor, and the GM-era Saab 9-3 (2003–2012) uses B0530 for something else entirely: the left turn indicator.",["Lock motor in the driver door latch worn or seized","Wire break in the door hinge passage","Stiff or contaminated latch mechanism overloading the motor","Output stage of the door or body control module faulty"],["Driver door does not lock or unlock with remote or switch","Other doors keep locking normally","On a Saab 9-3 the code instead comes with a left turn signal fault"],2,0,["B0531","B0532","B0533","B0265"],"מפעיל נעילת דלת נהג — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0531:["Passenger Door Lock Actuator Circuit","B0531 is neither in the accessible J2012 lists nor in any public manufacturer document, so the code itself cannot be verified. Its title covers the lock motor in the front passenger door. The Saab 9-3 checks that motor in the passenger door module and stores B3135 02 when the line is grounded during a lock or unlock request.",["Passenger door lock motor burnt out or seized","Lock motor wire chafed to ground in the door","Water ingress at the latch connector","Door or body control module output faulty"],["Passenger door stays locked or unlocked while others follow","Whole central locking inoperative if a shared line is grounded","Audible click without latch movement"],2,0,["B0530","B0532","B0533","B0270"],"מפעיל נעילת דלת נוסע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0532:["Left Rear Door Lock Actuator Circuit","Public J2012 lists do not include B0532. At GM it exists only as an undefined keyword in PIP5094, the general circuit-testing bulletin for GM cars and light trucks up to model year 2014. Its title refers to the lock motor in the left rear door. Rear doors carry an extra duty here: FMVSS 206 requires each rear side door to have a lock that, when engaged, also blocks the inside handle.",["Left rear lock motor worn or jammed","Broken wire in the left rear door boot","Latch linkage stiff from dirt or corrosion","Rear door or body module output faulty"],["Left rear door does not follow central locking","Vehicle cannot be fully secured from outside","Inside handle locking at that door may not work"],2,0,["B0530","B0531","B0533","B0272"],"מפעיל נעילת דלת אחורית שמאלית — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0533:["Right Rear Door Lock Actuator Circuit","B0533 is absent from the J2012 lists that can be consulted publicly; GM's PIP5094 merely names it as a circuit keyword for 2014-and-earlier models without saying what it covers. The title assigns it to the lock motor of the right rear door. In the Saab 9-3 the right rear door module watches this motor and reports B3135 02 if its line is shorted to ground while the car is being locked or unlocked.",["Right rear lock motor worn or jammed","Electric child lock motor or its wiring shorted","Broken wire in the right rear door boot","Rear door or body module output faulty"],["Right rear door stays locked or unlocked","Electric child lock at the rear may not engage","Power locks inoperative if a shared rear circuit is grounded"],2,0,["B0530","B0531","B0532","B0272"],"מפעיל נעילת דלת אחורית ימנית — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0540:["Driver Door Ajar Switch Circuit","Neither the public J2012 lists nor any accessible maker document define B0540, so the code is unverified. The title concerns the circuit of the switch that signals the driver door is not fully shut.",["Ajar switch in the latch or door frame stuck or corroded","Switch wire chafed to ground in the door hinge passage","Open wire or loose pin at the latch connector","Body control module input faulty"],["Door-open warning shown although the driver door is shut","Interior light stays on and may drain the battery","Alarm or auto-lock behaves erratically"],1,0,["B0541","B0510","B0260"],""],B0541:["Passenger Door Ajar Switch Circuit","B0541 cannot be traced in public J2012 lists or published manufacturer data. By its title it covers the ajar switch circuit of the front passenger door. Saab's 9-3 monitors that switch as B2991 in the body control module using the driver-side thresholds: 02 for a grounded line under 2.9 V, 05 for an open line or battery short over 10.2 V. Many modern doors have no separate jamb plunger;",["Ajar switch inside the passenger door latch worn","Door only reaching the safety catch due to misaligned striker","Switch wire open or grounded in the hinge passage","Body control module input faulty"],["Passenger door reported open while driving","Courtesy light does not react to the passenger door","Alarm cannot be armed or triggers falsely"],1,0,["B0540","B0520","B0260"],""],B0560:["Driver Power Seat Forward/Back Circuit","B0560 is not part of the publicly available J2012 lists. GM does use the code: preliminary information PIT5404 for the 2015 Tahoe, Suburban, Yukon and Escalade tells technicians to check B0560 together with B1277, B127C and B127D while chasing active-noise-cancellation drone, but it gives no descriptor, so a seat meaning is not supported there.",["Seat track blocked by objects or debris, overloading the motor","Fore/aft motor or its gear drive worn","Wiring under the seat pinched or connector loose","Relay or driver stage in the seat module faulty"],["Driver seat does not move forward or backward","Stored seat positions cannot be recalled","Seat stops after a short distance or moves in one direction only"],2,0,["B0561","B0562","B0570","B0312","B0310"],""],B0561:["Driver Power Seat Up/Down Circuit","B0561 has no entry in the accessible J2012 lists and no public manufacturer definition. The title refers to the motor that raises and lowers the driver seat; Chrysler's US4682088A splits this into front and rear cushion motors with about 1.5 in of travel. In the Saab 9-3 the height motor circuit is B1765 in the driver seat module: 04 for an open output, 0B for more than 40 A;",["Height motor or spindle gear seized","Motor wires pinched by the seat frame when lowering","Short on a motor line shared with other seat axes","Seat module driver stage faulty"],["Driver seat height cannot be adjusted","Other seat axes may stop working as well","Memory recall incomplete or blocked"],2,0,["B0560","B0562","B0580"],""],B0562:["Driver Power Seat Recline Circuit","B0562 is missing from public J2012 lists, and no manufacturer documents it. The title names the circuit of the backrest recline motor in the driver seat, which in Chrysler's US4682088A tilts the seatback through roughly 38 degrees.",["Recliner gear jammed or worn, motor draws excess current","Recline motor open winding or brushes worn","Wiring between seat base and backrest broken","Seat module output faulty"],["Driver backrest angle cannot be changed","Memory positions are not reached","Motor hums or clicks without backrest movement"],2,0,["B0560","B0561","B0322"],""],B0570:["Passenger Power Seat Forward/Back Circuit","B0570 is not found in any J2012 list open to the public, nor in published manufacturer material. Its title covers the fore/aft motor of the front passenger seat. The Saab 9-3 passenger seat module shows how such a circuit is policed: B1770 04 for an open output, 0B above 40 A, and 61 when a relay is stuck to ground, detected right after a soft start because the output exceeds 6 V.",["Objects under the passenger seat blocking the track","Seat module relay stuck, seat moves one way only","Fore/aft motor open circuit or worn brushes","Connector under the seat loose or corroded"],["Passenger seat does not slide forward or back","Seat moves only in one direction","Passenger seat memory or easy-entry function unavailable"],2,0,["B0560","B0320","B0327"],""],B0580:["Driver Seat Memory Module Malfunction","B0580 is absent from publicly available J2012 lists and lacks a public manufacturer definition. The title describes an internal fault of the driver seat memory module. GM's 2011 Saab 9-5 shows what such a module checks in itself: B3920 42 when its calibration was never programmed, B3920 00 when the current leaving a motor rail differs from the returning current, plus voltage faults on the rail;",["Replacement module installed without calibration or setup","Internal electronic fault of the memory module","Liquid under the seat reaching the module","Low battery voltage or poor module ground"],["Memory buttons do not recall seat or mirror positions","Power seat partly or completely inoperative","Stored positions lost after power interruption"],3,0,["B0560","B0561","B0562","B0325","B0327"],"מודול זיכרון מושב נהג — תקלה"],B0600:["Mirror Adjustment Driver Side Circuit","B0600 is not listed in the J2012 tables that are publicly accessible, and no manufacturer explains it. The title refers to the adjustment circuit of the driver's exterior mirror, which FMVSS 111 requires the driver to be able to tilt horizontally and vertically while seated.",["Mirror adjustment motor seized by corrosion or ice","Mirror wires broken in the door hinge passage","Water in the mirror housing shorting the motor or sensor","Driver door module output faulty"],["Driver mirror does not move in one or both axes","Mirror memory position not restored","Rear view to the driver's side limited until adjusted by hand"],2,0,["B0601","B0610"],"צד נהג כוונון מראה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0601:["Mirror Adjustment Passenger Side Circuit","B0601 is not covered by the public J2012 lists or by any accessible manufacturer documentation. By title it concerns the adjustment circuit of the passenger exterior mirror; FMVSS 111 only demands that it can be tilted, not remote control from the driving position, yet most are motorised.",["Passenger mirror motor seized or worn","Shared motor line shorted, affecting both axes","Wire break in the passenger door hinge passage","Passenger door module or window switch electronics faulty"],["Passenger mirror cannot be adjusted electrically","Reverse tilt-down or memory position of the mirror missing","Driver mirror usually keeps working"],2,0,["B0600","B0610"],"צד נוסע כוונון מראה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0610:["Mirror Heater Circuit","Public J2012 lists, OEM manuals and NHTSA bulletins all lack B0610; its use cannot be verified. The title describes the heating element behind the outside mirror glass. In the 2003–2012 Saab 9-3 each door module watches this load on its own: if the heater draws too much current when switched on, it stores B1640 02 and tries again only in the next drive cycle.",["Heating pad behind the mirror glass broken or shorted","Corroded plug at the mirror glass or in the mirror base","Wire chafed in the door hinge passage","Heater output of the door or body control module faulty"],["Outside mirror stays fogged or iced while the rear window clears","Mirror glass does not warm up when the heating is switched on","Code returns after every restart"],1,0,["B0600","B0601","B0950"],"גוף חימום מראה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0700:["Sunroof Open/Close Circuit","No accessible J2012 list, public manufacturer manual or NHTSA bulletin contains B0700, so the code cannot be verified. Its title points to the circuit that drives a power sunroof open and shut. GM-era Saab cars report such faults under their own numbers: the 9-3 sunroof module stores B3661 0E when motor current is too high and B3664 04 for an open switch line, after which button presses are ignored;",["Dirty or dry guide rails raising motor current","Sunroof switch or its wiring faulty","Sunroof motor or gearbox worn","Sunroof control electronics faulty"],["Sunroof does not move when the button is pressed","Roof stops or reverses on its own while closing","Motor hums without the panel moving"],2,0,["B0710"],""],B0710:["Sunroof Position Sensor Circuit","Nothing public confirms B0710: it is missing from J2012 extracts, workshop manuals and recall bulletins alike. The title refers to the position feedback of a power sunroof. Typical designs count pulses from a Hall sensor at the motor shaft: Nedap's NL1001829C2 derives panel position and speed from the pole changes, and Bosch's DE19815960A1 resets such a counter at a mechanical stop and uses it to separate sliding…",["End positions not relearned after battery disconnection or motor replacement","Hall sensor or motor electronics faulty","Binding mechanism or misfitted motor","Signal wire or connector at the motor damaged"],["One-touch opening or closing no longer works","Roof stops short of its end position or reverses unexpectedly","Roof can only be moved step by step until reinitialised"],2,0,["B0700"],"חיישן מצב גג שמש — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0800:["Headlamp Switch Circuit","B0800 lacks any public evidence; no J2012 extract or service document mentions it. The title concerns the light switch that tells the body control module which lamps to energise. In the GM-developed Saab 9-3 the BCM checks switch positions 1 and 2 and logs B2585 05 or B2575 05 when the respective line rises above 10.2 V; dipped beam then stays on whatever the switch says.",["Worn or corroded contacts in the light switch","Switch signal wire shorted to battery voltage","Loose or damaged plug behind the switch","Switch input of the body control module faulty"],["Dipped beam stays on regardless of switch position","Lights only work in automatic mode","Parking lights cannot be selected separately"],1,0,["B0240","B0810","B0811"],"מתג פנס ראשי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0810:["Left Headlamp Low Beam Circuit","Whether any carmaker sets B0810 is unknown – the number shows up in no J2012 excerpt and no service literature. The title covers the left dipped-beam output. The GM-era Saab 9-3 checks it in the front electrical centre under the number B2575: with the switch at dipped beam (position 2), a draw below 0.8 A sets B2575 04 (open) and one of 7.9–30 A sets B2575 0B, which may also mean a bulb of the wrong rating.",["Low-beam bulb burnt out","Bulb of the wrong wattage fitted","Xenon ballast or igniter faulty","Corroded headlamp plug or poor ground","Lamp output of the lighting or body module faulty"],["Left dipped beam dark, lamp failure message in the display","Reduced view of the left road edge at night; repair before driving in the dark","Light flickers or fails only after the lamp has warmed up"],1,0,["B0811","B0800","B0820"],""],B0811:["Right Headlamp Low Beam Circuit","No J2012 excerpt or published service text uses B0811, which leaves the code undocumented. The title names the right dipped-beam circuit. In GM's 2011 Saab 9-5 the body control module powers low beam or daytime running lamps, while a separate headlamp control module stores B2699 (02 grounded, 04 open, 00 malfunction) when it sees a commanded lamp stay dark.",["Right low-beam bulb or LED unit failed","Incorrect bulb rating after a replacement","Open or grounded supply wire to the headlamp","Headlamp or body control module output faulty"],["Right dipped beam or daytime running lamp stays dark","Lamp warning shown in the instrument cluster","Kerb side poorly lit at night; have it repaired promptly"],1,0,["B0810","B0800","B0821"],""],B0820:["Left Headlamp High Beam Circuit","B0820 is undocumented: neither open J2012 material nor factory or NHTSA papers list it. The title refers to the left main-beam output. In the second-generation Saab 9-3 the front electrical centre flags B2580 04 when the left main beam draws under 0.8 A while switched on and B2580 0B for 7.9 to 30 A.",["Left high-beam bulb burnt out","High-beam relay or its control line faulty","Shutter actuator in a bi-xenon module stuck","Corroded headlamp connector"],["Left main beam stays dark when high beam is selected","Both main beams fail if the shared relay circuit is affected","Lamp failure message in the display"],1,0,["B0821","B0810","B0800"],""],B0821:["Right Headlamp High Beam Circuit","For B0821 there is no public trace in J2012 extracts, factory manuals or NHTSA files. The title describes the right main-beam circuit. Saab's 9-3 (type 9440) watches it under its own number B3866: open (04) when the lamp draws under 0.8 A with main beam on, overcurrent (0B) in the 7.9–30 A band; apart from the warning the module takes no action.",["Right high-beam bulb failed","Supply wire to the right headlamp open or shorted","Higher-wattage bulb fitted, triggering overcurrent","Main-beam output of the lighting module faulty"],["Right main beam stays dark, left one works","Lamp warning in the display when high beam is switched on"],1,0,["B0820","B0811"],""],B0830:["Left Front Turn Signal Circuit","Open J2012 sources do not include B0830, and no workshop or NHTSA text quotes it, so it remains unconfirmed. The title covers the left front indicator. The GM-developed Saab 9-3 monitors this lamp as B0530 in its front electrical centre: a draw above 6 A for longer than 6 ms counts as a short to ground and the output is switched off, while less than 50 mA counts as an open circuit.",["Indicator bulb burnt out","Corroded bulb holder or plug in the headlamp housing","Supply wire shorted to ground, output shut off","Indicator output of the electrical centre faulty"],["Left front indicator dark, warning in the display","Pilot light stays steady or flashes noticeably faster","Turning intention not visible to oncoming traffic; repair promptly"],1,0,["B0831","B0840","B0841"],""],B0831:["Right Front Turn Signal Circuit","B0831 has no published definition; J2012 extracts, factory literature and NHTSA records are silent on it. Its title names the right front indicator circuit. In the GM-era Saab 9-3 this lamp is checked as B0525 by the front electrical centre, with the same limits as on the left: under 50 mA means open (04), while over 6 A lasting beyond 6 ms is read as a short to ground (02) and cuts the output.",["Right front indicator bulb failed","Water in the lamp housing corroding the contacts","Wire damaged after front-end repair or impact","Front electrical centre output faulty"],["Right front indicator dark when signalling right","Changed flash rate or steady pilot light in the cluster","Hazard lights incomplete on the right front corner"],1,0,["B0830","B0841","B0840"],""],B0840:["Left Rear Turn Signal Circuit","Neither J2012 extracts nor any OEM or NHTSA publication name B0840; its use is unproven. The title concerns the left rear indicator. In the 2003–2012 Saab 9-3 the rear electrical centre supervises this lamp under the number B0530: an open lamp (04) or a short to ground (02) shows up as a warning message and the remaining indicators flashing at double speed, which is exactly the pilot-indicator behaviour FMVSS 108…",["Rear indicator bulb or LED segment failed","Corroded plug or bulb carrier in the rear lamp","Wire break in the boot lid or tailgate harness","Rear electrical centre output faulty"],["Indicators flash at double speed when signalling left","Left rear indicator dark, warning message shown","Lane changes not visible to following traffic; repair promptly"],1,0,["B0841","B0830","B0850"],""],B0841:["Right Rear Turn Signal Circuit","No public record of B0841 exists in J2012 lists, OEM manuals or bulletins. The title refers to the right rear indicator circuit. The second-generation Saab 9-3 logs this lamp in its rear electrical centre as B0525: under 50 mA is treated as open (04), more than 6 A for over 6 ms as a short to ground (02), after which the output is switched off. In both cases the driver sees a message and a doubled flash rate.",["Right rear indicator bulb burnt out","Corroded contacts in the bulb holder","Pinched wire shorting to body ground","Lamp driver in the rear module faulty"],["Indicators flash at double speed when signalling right","Right rear indicator does not light, message in the display"],1,0,["B0840","B0831","B0851"],""],B0850:["Left Brake Lamp Circuit","B0850 cannot be confirmed from any open source – J2012 tables, OEM documentation and NHTSA bulletins omit it. The title covers the left stop lamp. In Saab's 9-3 (type 9440) the rear electrical centre checks it while braking under its own number B3445: below 50 mA it records an open circuit (04), and once current tops 6 A for over 6 ms a short to ground (02), shutting the output down.",["Left stop-lamp bulb or filament failed","Corroded bulb holder in the tail lamp","Open or grounded wire to the left tail lamp","Stop-lamp output of the rear module faulty"],["Left brake light stays dark when braking, warning shown","Weaker warning to following traffic; repair before further driving","Tail light on the same side may also be affected with combined bulbs"],1,0,["B0851","B0235"],"נורת בלם שמאלי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0851:["Right Brake Lamp Circuit","Published J2012 tables skip B0851, and service literature and NHTSA filings never cite it either. The title names the right stop-lamp circuit. The GM-developed Saab 9-3 tests this lamp whenever the brake light is on and stores B3878 04 once the right lamp draws less than 50 mA; the high-mounted lamp is judged separately under B3884 with a lower limit of 20 mA.",["Right stop-lamp bulb or LED segment failed","Loose or corroded plug at the right tail lamp","Wire to the right tail lamp broken","Lamp driver in the rear module faulty"],["Right brake light dark while the left one and the third lamp work","Brake light warning in the display","Reduced braking signal to following drivers; repair at once"],1,0,["B0850","B0235"],"נורת בלם ימני — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0860:["License Plate Lamp Circuit","B0860 is not traceable in public J2012 extracts, and no manufacturer or regulator text refers to it. The title describes the lamp lighting the rear number plate. GM's 2011 Saab 9-5 switches it through the body control module whenever parking or dipped lights are selected, logging B3883 02 for a grounded and B3883 04 for an open feed.",["Plate lamp bulb burnt out","Water in the lamp housing corroding contacts","Wire break in the boot lid hinge area","Lamp output of the body or rear module faulty"],["Number plate not illuminated with lights on","Lamp warning in the display","Plate lamp stays on permanently in some short-circuit cases"],1,0,["B0239","B0850"],""],B0900:["Wiper Motor Front Circuit","Open J2012 material, factory manuals and NHTSA bulletins contain no entry for B0900, so it is unconfirmed. The title concerns the windscreen wiper motor circuit. GM-era Saab models diagnose it at the relays: the 9-3 sets B3874 06 or B3875 06 when the low- or high-speed relay output stays below 6 V, so the wipers stop, run constantly or only at high speed.",["Wiper relay sticking or with burnt contacts","Wiper motor worn or park switch faulty","Seized linkage overloading the motor","Damaged wiring in the scuttle area"],["Wipers do not run, run continuously or only at one speed","Wipers stop outside the park position","Poor visibility in rain; do not drive in wet weather until repaired"],2,0,["B0910","B0920","B0220","B0190","B0192"],"קדמי מנוע מגב — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0910:["Wiper Motor Rear Circuit","A public definition of B0910 is lacking in J2012 extracts as well as in OEM and NHTSA documents. The title refers to the rear window wiper motor circuit. On the second-generation Saab 9-3 the rear electrical centre drives it through a relay and stores B3720: 01 if more than 6 V sits on the output during activation, so the wiper does not work, and 06 if over 6 V is present with the wiper off, where a short to ground…",["Wire break in the tailgate hinge harness","Rear wiper motor or spindle seized by corrosion","Rear wiper relay faulty","Rear module relay driver faulty"],["Rear wiper does not run when switched on","Rear wiper keeps running after switching off"],1,0,["B0900","B0188","B0920"],"אחורי מנוע מגב — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0920:["Washer Pump Circuit","B0920 has no verifiable source: it is absent from J2012 excerpts and from all published service information. The title covers the washer fluid pump circuit. GM's 2011 Saab 9-5 lets the body control module start the pump together with low-speed wiping as soon as washing is requested; with a supply of 9 to 16 V it watches the relay control line, stores B3873 02 on a short to ground and suspends washing.",["Washer pump motor seized, often after running dry or freezing","Corroded plug at the pump in the wheel arch","Washer relay or its control line faulty","Relay driver in the body control module faulty"],["No washer fluid sprays when the wash switch is used","Washer pump runs continuously","Headlamp washers inoperative as well on shared circuits"],1,0,["B0900","B0910"],"משאבת מתז — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0950:["Heated Rear Window Circuit","None of the accessible J2012 lists, OEM manuals or NHTSA bulletins mention B0950; it is therefore unverified. The title refers to the electrically heated rear window. GM-era Saab cars monitor this heater under other numbers: in the 2011 Saab 9-5 the climate control module energises the relay coil that switches battery voltage to the grid, and faults on that control line are stored as B0283.",["Broken heater line or detached terminal tab on the glass","Rear defogger relay faulty","Wire break in the tailgate or boot lid harness","Climate or body control module output faulty"],["Rear window does not clear when the heater is switched on","Only some heater lines warm up","Indicator in the button does not light"],1,0,["B0283","B0610"],"חלון אחורי מחומם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0960:["Parking Assist Rear Sensor Right Middle Circuit","B0960 does not appear in the accessible J2012 lists; it is documented by GM and the GM-era Saab models as the right middle rear parking sensor. The 2011 Saab 9-5 and 9-4X list B0960 01 (short to battery), 06 (low voltage or open), 08 (invalid signal), 21 (incorrect period) and 3A (wrong part fitted); B0958, B0959 and B0961 cover the other rear sensors.",["Sensor face dirty, iced or covered","Ultrasonic sensor defective or wrong part fitted","Bumper harness damaged after a parking knock or repair","Parking assist control module faulty"],["Parking assist switches off with a message when reversing","No warning tones although an obstacle is close","Obstacles behind the car must be checked visually until repaired"],2,0,[],"אמצעי ימני חיישן אחורי סיוע חניה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0970:["Interior Light Circuit","B0970 is not documented anywhere public, whether in J2012 extracts, workshop literature or NHTSA bulletins. The title covers the interior lighting circuit. The 2003–2012 Saab 9-3 supervises it through its BCM: B2556 02 when more than 10 A flows on the lamp feed, B2555 0F when the lamps are powered although they should be off, and B2610 02 when the dimmed PWM line drops below 2.0 V.",["Door contact switch stuck, keeping the lamps on","Short in a roof or footwell lamp, often after bulb changes","Chafed wire in the headliner or A-pillar","Lamp output of the body control module faulty"],["Interior lights stay off when a door is opened","Interior lights stay on permanently","Battery flat after the car has stood overnight"],1,0,["B0260"],"אור פנימי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],B0980:["Ignition Switch Run/Start Position Circuit","Public sources give no meaning for B0980: J2012 extracts and OEM or NHTSA documents leave it out. The title concerns the signal by which the ignition switch reports its run and start positions. GM-era Saab vehicles use other numbers for this: the 9-3 column module sets B1440 0F when the +15 supply from the ignition switch module is open and B1368 00 when that input is shorted to battery;",["Worn contacts in the ignition switch","Open or shorted ignition feed wire","Ignition relay or its control line faulty","Low battery voltage causing implausible signals"],["Engine does not crank although the key is turned","Ignition cannot be switched off or key cannot be removed","Steering lock or electrical consumers behave erratically"],2,0,["B0990"],""],B0990:["Body Control Module Internal Fault","For B0990 no public evidence exists, be it in J2012 lists or in carmaker or NHTSA papers. The title describes a self-detected failure inside the body control module. GM-era Saab models report this as B1000 or B101D: on the 2011 Saab 9-5 the module runs its internal test at every power-up, refuses further inputs on a fault and clears a history entry after 50 fault-free ignition cycles;",["Poor supply voltage or ground at the module","Moisture or corrosion inside the module","Corrupted or outdated module software","Internal electronic failure of the module"],["Several body functions fail at once, such as lights, locks or wipers","Car will not start if the immobiliser data cannot be read","Code stored only as history without any noticeable effect"],3,0,["B0980"],""]};export{e as default};
